  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-max-thinking-fast",
  "text": "Fixed. Both scripts now have `-rwxr-xr-x` permissions and the hook correctly blocks prompts containing the forbidden word.\n\n**Root cause:** The script was missing the execute permission bit (`-rw-r--r--` instead of `-rwxr-xr-x`). When Cursor tried to run `.cursor/hooks/secret_cleanup.sh` directly, the OS rejected it with \"permission denied\" (exit code 126), so the hook silently failed and the prompt went through unblocked.\n\n**Fix:** `chmod +x` on both hook scripts. The script logic itself was correct all along -- it just couldn't run.",
