  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive status update on the React Router v5 to v6 migration, feature flags, and test frameworks.\n\n---\n\n## React Router Migration Status\n\n### Current State: Hybrid (v5 core + v6 APIs via compat layer)\n\nThe codebase is in a **mid-migration state**. The core router is still React Router v5 (`5.3.4`), but nearly all component-level APIs have been migrated to v6-style usage through the `react-router-dom-v5-compat` package (`^6.26.1`, resolving to `6.30.3`).\n\n### Package versions (root `package.json`)\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 | Core v5 router |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 | v5 DOM bindings |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 | v6 API bridge |\n| `@types/react-router` | 5.1.20 | v5 types |\n| `@types/react-router-dom` | 5.3.3 | v5 types |\n\n### What's been migrated (v6-style APIs in use)\n\nThe migration of **component-level APIs is essentially complete**:\n\n- **~130 files** import from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n- `useNavigate` - used in ~15 files (replaces `useHistory`)\n- `useParams` - used in ~45 files\n- `<Routes>` / `<Route element={}>` - used in ~20-25 files\n- `<Navigate>` - used in ~15 files (replaces `<Redirect>`)\n- **Zero remaining** `useHistory`, `useRouteMatch`, `<Switch>`, `<Route exact>`, or `<Redirect>` from v5\n\n### What's still on v5\n\nThe **infrastructure layer** remains on v5:\n\n1. **`RoutesWrapper.tsx`** - uses `Router` from `react-router-dom` and wraps with `CompatRouter`\n2. **A handful of direct v5 imports** remain in:\n   - `AppNotificationList.tsx` (`useLocation` from `react-router-dom`)\n   - `explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx` (`Route`, `Router` from `react-router-dom`, ESLint-disabled)\n   - `RepositoryStatusPage.tsx`, `FileStatusPage.tsx`, `TabItemRenderer.tsx` (`useLocation` from `react-router`)\n\n### What hasn't been started\n\nThe final phase of the migration -- moving to the **v6 data router APIs** -- has not been started:\n\n- **No usage** of `createBrowserRouter`, `createRoutesFromElements`, or `RouterProvider`\n- **No usage** of `<Outlet>` (nested routing)\n- The app still relies on v5's `history` object for programmatic navigation at the infrastructure level\n\n### Key files to understand the architecture\n\n- `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` - where v5 `Router` + `CompatRouter` are set up\n- `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` - route definitions (uses custom `RouteDescriptor` pattern with `GrafanaRouteWrapper`)\n- `public/app/features/plugins/loader/sharedDependencies.ts` (lines 112-125) - migration notes for plugin shared deps\n\n---\n\n## Feature Flags\n\n**There are no feature flags for the React Router migration.** The migration is being done as a straightforward, non-flagged migration.\n\n### What was checked\n\n- `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` - no router-related flags\n- `packages/grafana-data/src/types/featureToggles.gen.ts` - no router-related toggles\n- No A/B testing or gradual rollout mechanisms for the router\n\n### Related (but unrelated) navigation flags\n\nThese flags exist but control different features, not the React Router migration:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `alertingNavigationV2` | New Alerting menu structure |\n| `preserveDashboardStateWhenNavigating` | Preserve variables/time range across dashboards |\n| `useScopesNavigationEndpoint` | Backend scopes navigation endpoint |\n\nA historical `newNavigation` flag existed (2022) for the sidebar UI, but it has been removed.\n\n---\n\n## Test Frameworks Available\n\n### Unit Testing: Jest + React Testing Library\n\n| Package | Version |\n|---------|---------|\n| `jest` | 29.7.0 |\n| `@testing-library/react` | 16.3.0 |\n| `@testing-library/dom` | 10.4.1 |\n| `@testing-library/jest-dom` | 6.6.4 |\n| `@testing-library/user-event` | 14.6.1 |\n| `msw` | 2.10.4 |\n\n### Central Test Utility: `public/test/test-utils.tsx`\n\nThis is the main render helper and is **the recommended starting point** for all component tests. It exports `render`, `getWrapper`, `userEvent`, and re-exports from `@testing-library/react`.\n\n**Key `render` options for routing tests:**\n\n- `renderWithRouter` (default: `true`) - wraps component with `Router` + `CompatRouter`\n- `historyOptions` - pass `{ initialEntries: ['/some/path'] }` to set the starting route\n\n**Example patterns:**\n\n```typescript\n// Pattern 1: render with initial route\nimport { render } from 'test/test-utils';\nrender(<MyComponent />, {\n  renderWithRouter: true,\n  historyOptions: { initialEntries: ['/alerting/admin'] },\n});\n\n// Pattern 2: renderHook with routing context\nimport { renderHook, getWrapper } from 'test/test-utils';\nconst wrapper = getWrapper({\n  renderWithRouter: true,\n  historyOptions: { initialEntries: ['/some/path'] },\n});\nconst { result } = renderHook(() => useMyHook(), { wrapper });\n\n// Pattern 3: Direct MemoryRouter for isolated tests\nimport { MemoryRouter } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\nrender(\n  <MemoryRouter initialEntries={['/dashboard/123']}>\n    <MyComponent />\n  </MemoryRouter>\n);\n```\n\n### E2E Testing\n\n| Framework | Config | Location |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| **Playwright** (primary) | `playwright.config.ts` | `e2e-playwright/` |\n| **Cypress** (legacy) | `cypress.config.js` | `e2e/cypress/` |\n\nPlaywright (`@playwright/test` 1.56.1) is the primary E2E framework. Cypress (14.3.2) is the legacy option.\n\n### Other utilities\n\n- `@grafana/test-utils` (workspace package) - MSW matchers and mock API utilities\n- `react-select-event` (5.5.1) - for testing `react-select` components\n- `testing-library-selector` (0.3.1) - selector utilities for Testing Library\n\n---\n\n## Summary & Remaining Work\n\nThe migration is in good shape at the component API level -- v5-specific APIs have been fully replaced with v6 equivalents via the compat layer. The remaining work falls into two categories:\n\n1. **Clean up stragglers** - Fix the ~5 files still importing directly from `react-router-dom` or `react-router` instead of `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n2. **Final migration** - Remove the compat layer entirely by:\n   - Replacing `Router` + `CompatRouter` with `createBrowserRouter` / `RouterProvider`\n   - Adopting `<Outlet>` for nested routing\n   - Upgrading `react-router-dom` to v6 directly and removing the v5 packages\n\nFor testing during the continued migration, the `render` helper in `public/test/test-utils.tsx` with `renderWithRouter` + `historyOptions` is the most ergonomic path. For isolated routing logic tests, using `MemoryRouter` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` directly works well.",
