  "text": "Created the subagent at `.cursor/agents/react-router-migrator.md`. Here's what it includes:\n\n### `react-router-migrator` subagent\n\n**Scope**: Project-level (`.cursor/agents/`), so it's available within this Grafana workspace and can be checked into version control for your team.\n\n**What it knows:**\n\n- The full current migration state -- v5 core with v6 APIs via `react-router-dom-v5-compat`, ~130 files already migrated, zero remaining v5 API patterns\n- The exact list of straggler files still importing directly from `react-router-dom` or `react-router`\n- That no feature flags control the migration\n- The infrastructure pieces not yet migrated (data router APIs, `<Outlet>`, `RouterProvider`)\n\n**What it does when invoked:**\n\n1. **Audits** target files for v5 imports and patterns\n2. **Applies** a full v5-to-v6 replacement table (`useHistory` -> `useNavigate`, `<Switch>` -> `<Routes>`, etc.)\n3. **Updates imports** to use `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n4. **Handles edge cases** like `useParams` returning `string | undefined`, nested route trailing `/*`, and render function children\n5. **Updates tests** using the correct Grafana test utilities (`render` with `renderWithRouter`, `getWrapper`, `MemoryRouter`)\n6. **Validates** with `jest --findRelatedTests`, typecheck, and lint\n\n**Constraints baked in:**\n\n- Won't prematurely remove the compat layer\n- Won't introduce `createBrowserRouter`/`RouterProvider` during file-level work\n- Preserves plugin system backward compatibility\n\n**To use it:**\n\n```\nUse the react-router-migrator to migrate public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx\n```\n\nOr point it at a broader scope like a directory of components that need migration work.",
