  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive orientation to the React Router migration in this Grafana codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Overview\n\nThe codebase is **mid-migration from React Router v5 to v6**, using the official `react-router-dom-v5-compat` package as a bridge. The core router infrastructure still runs on v5, while most component-level code has been migrated to use v6-style APIs through the compat layer.\n\n### Current dependency picture\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 | v5 core (still in use) |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 | v5 DOM bindings (infrastructure) |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 (resolves to 6.30.3) | v6 API surface on v5 plumbing |\n| `history` | 4.10.1 | v4 History API (used by v5 + `LocationService`) |\n\n### Architecture\n\nThe router setup lives in `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx`:\n\n```\n<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>     ← v5 Router + history v4\n  <LocationServiceProvider>\n    <CompatRouter>                                   ← bridges v6 APIs onto v5\n      <AppChrome>\n        <Routes> / <Route element={...}>             ← v6-style route rendering\n      </AppChrome>\n    </CompatRouter>\n  </LocationServiceProvider>\n</Router>\n```\n\nRoute definitions are in `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` via `getAppRoutes()`, which returns `RouteDescriptor[]` objects. Each route is rendered through `GrafanaRouteWrapper` in `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx`, which handles auth, roles, and lazy loading.\n\n### What's been migrated\n\n- ~130+ files import from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` using v6-style APIs (`useNavigate`, `useParams`, `useSearchParams`, `<Routes>`, `<Route element={}>`, `<Navigate>`)\n- Plugin shared dependencies in `public/app/features/plugins/loader/sharedDependencies.ts` expose `react-router-dom-v5-compat` as `react-router` for plugins adopting v6\n\n### What's NOT yet migrated\n\nA handful of files still import directly from `react-router-dom` or `react-router` (v5):\n\n| File | Direct v5 import |\n|------|-------------------|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/test/test-utils.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/test/helpers/TestProvider.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx` | `Route`, `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/Repository/RepositoryStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/File/FileStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` |\n| `public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/layout-tabs/TabItemRenderer.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` |\n\nThe v6 **data router APIs** (`createBrowserRouter`, `RouterProvider`, `<Outlet>`) are **not yet in use**. That would be the final step to fully remove the compat layer.\n\n---\n\n## Feature Flag Infrastructure\n\n**There are no feature flags controlling the React Router migration.** The migration is being done as a direct, incremental change without a toggle to switch between old and new router implementations.\n\n- `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` and `toggles_gen.json` contain no flags for \"react\", \"router\", \"reactRouter\", \"browserRouter\", or \"data-router\"\n- `RoutesWrapper.tsx` has no conditional logic -- it always uses the same `Router` + `CompatRouter` setup\n- Feature flags in `routes.tsx` (like `suggestedDashboards`, `restoreDashboards`, `enableExtensionsAdminPage`) control which **routes exist**, not which **router version** is used\n\nThe migration is un-flagged: once v5 imports are fully eliminated and `createBrowserRouter` is adopted, the compat layer can simply be removed.\n\n---\n\n## Migration-Related Tests\n\n### No dedicated migration tests\n\nThere are **no tests that explicitly verify React Router migration behavior**, version switching, or router compatibility. There are no integration tests for `RoutesWrapper.tsx` or `routes.tsx` themselves.\n\n### Test infrastructure uses the compat layer\n\nThe test utilities mirror the production setup:\n\n- `public/test/test-utils.tsx` -- `render()` wraps components in `Router` + `CompatRouter` when `renderWithRouter: true`, supports `historyOptions: { initialEntries: ['/path'] }`\n- `public/test/helpers/TestProvider.tsx` -- wraps tests with `Router` + `CompatRouter`\n\n### Tests consuming v6 APIs via compat\n\nA large number of test files already use `react-router-dom-v5-compat` imports. Key categories:\n\n| Area | Example files | What they test |\n|------|---------------|----------------|\n| **Alerting** | `public/app/features/alerting/unified/` (many files) | Route rendering, navigation with `MemoryRouter`, `Routes`, `Route` |\n| **Dashboards** | `DashboardPageProxy.test.tsx`, `DashboardScenePage.test.tsx`, `PublicDashboardPage.test.tsx` | `useParams` mocking, route matching |\n| **Plugins** | `AppRootPage.test.tsx`, `PluginDetails.test.tsx` | Plugin route rendering with v6 `Routes`/`Route` |\n| **Provisioning** | Multiple form tests | Mock `react-router-dom-v5-compat` for navigation |\n| **Connections** | `Connections.test.tsx`, `DataSourceTabs.test.tsx` | Tab routing with v6 `Route`/`Routes` |\n| **Browse dashboards** | `BrowseDashboardsPage.test.tsx`, folder pages | `useParams` mocking |\n| **grafana-ui** | `TextLink.test.tsx`, `VizTooltipFooter.test.tsx` | `MemoryRouter` from v5-compat |\n\n### Routing utility tests\n\n| File | What it covers |\n|------|----------------|\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.test.tsx` | Search parsing, lazy loading, error handling in `GrafanaRoute` |\n| `public/app/routes/utils.test.ts` | `isSoloRoute()` for solo/dashboard-solo URL detection |\n\n### Notable test notes\n\n- `public/app/features/alerting/unified/RedirectToRuleViewer.test.tsx` has TODO comments about console warnings when `CompatRouter` wraps the component\n- `public/app/features/alerting/unified/hooks/useReturnTo.test.tsx` mentions React Router Future Flag warnings\n- E2E tests in `e2e-playwright/` test navigation behavior at a higher level but don't exercise React Router directly\n\n---\n\n## Summary & Next Steps\n\nThe migration is in a **stable intermediate state**: v6-style APIs are used almost everywhere through the compat layer, but the underlying router is still v5. The remaining work is:\n\n1. **Eliminate remaining direct v5 imports** (the 8 files listed above)\n2. **Adopt v6 data router APIs** (`createBrowserRouter`, `RouterProvider`, `<Outlet>`)\n3. **Remove the compat layer** (`react-router-dom-v5-compat`, `CompatRouter`)\n4. **Remove `history` v4 dependency** and `LocationService`'s direct history usage\n\nThere's no feature flag gating any of this, and no migration-specific test coverage -- meaning any final switch would need careful integration testing.",
