  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "The implementation is complete with zero lint errors. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n### Category assignment\n\n`findParentSectionId` walks the nav tree to determine which top-level section a bookmarked URL belongs to. The `SECTION_TO_CATEGORY` map then assigns each nav section to one of three categories:\n\n- **Operations** -- alerting, connections, explore, drilldown, infrastructure, observability\n- **Admin** -- cfg (administration), profile, plugins, access control\n- **Content** -- dashboards, starred, reports, apps, home\n\nItems not matching any known section default to \"content\".\n\n### Filtering\n\n- A `FilterInput` provides text search across bookmark names and subtitles\n- A `RadioButtonGroup` lets users filter by category, with each option showing a count (e.g. \"Operations (3)\")\n\n### Grouping\n\nBookmarks are grouped into collapsible `CollapsableSection` panels by category. Each section shows a card grid identical to the original layout. Sections with no matching items are hidden automatically.\n\n### Patterns followed\n\n- `FilterInput` + `RadioButtonGroup` in a `Stack` layout (matches `UsersActionBar`, `ServiceAccountsListPage`)\n- `CollapsableSection` from `@grafana/ui` for collapsible groups\n- All user-facing strings wrapped with `t()` / `<Trans>` for i18n\n- Emotion CSS-in-JS with `useStyles2` for styling\n- `useMemo` for derived state to avoid unnecessary recalculations",
