  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the React Router migration status in the Grafana codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Current State: Hybrid v5/v6 via Compatibility Layer\n\nGrafana is mid-migration from **React Router v5 (5.3.4)** to **v6**, using the official `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (resolved to **6.30.3**) as a bridge. The core router infrastructure still runs on v5, while most feature code has adopted v6-style APIs through the compat layer.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Current Architecture\"\n        A[\"v5 Router<br/><code>Router history={locationService.getHistory()}</code>\"] --> B[\"CompatRouter<br/><code>react-router-dom-v5-compat</code>\"]\n        B --> C[\"Routes (v6-style)<br/><code>&lt;Routes&gt; + &lt;Route element={...}&gt;</code>\"]\n        C --> D[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/>Auth/Role checks, pageview tracking\"]\n        D --> E[\"Feature Pages\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Navigation Layer\"\n        F[\"LocationService<br/><code>history v4</code>\"] --> A\n        G[\"locationService.push/replace/partial\"] --> F\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Plugin System\"\n        H[\"sharedDependencies.ts\"] -->|\"'react-router-dom' → v5\"| I[\"Legacy Plugins\"]\n        H -->|\"'react-router' → v5-compat\"| J[\"v6-aware Plugins\"]\n    end\n\n    style A fill:#f9d,stroke:#333\n    style F fill:#f9d,stroke:#333\n    style H fill:#f9d,stroke:#333\n    style B fill:#ff9,stroke:#333\n    style C fill:#9f9,stroke:#333\n    style D fill:#9f9,stroke:#333\n```\n\n**Legend:** Pink = v5 (needs migration), Yellow = compat bridge (temporary), Green = v6-ready\n\n---\n\n## Package Dependencies\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 | v5 core (still installed) |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 | v5 DOM bindings (root router) |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 → **6.30.3** | v6 API bridge |\n| `history` | v4 | Used by LocationService |\n\n---\n\n## Migration Tiers\n\nThe remaining work breaks down into **3 tiers** based on dependency order:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Tier 1 — Critical Infrastructure\"\n        direction TB\n        T1A[\"LocationService<br/>(grafana-runtime)\"]\n        T1B[\"RoutesWrapper.tsx<br/>(v5 Router + CompatRouter)\"]\n        T1C[\"sharedDependencies.ts<br/>(plugin router exposure)\"]\n        T1D[\"webpack.dev.js<br/>(react-router-dom alias)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Tier 2 — Routing Components\"\n        direction TB\n        T2A[\"GrafanaRoute.tsx<br/>(compat imports)\"]\n        T2B[\"types.ts<br/>(Location from history)\"]\n        T2C[\"hooks.ts<br/>(compat useLocation)\"]\n        T2D[\"routes.tsx<br/>(compat Navigate/useParams)\"]\n        T2E[\"AppWrapper.tsx<br/>(compat Route/Routes)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Tier 3 — Feature Code\"\n        direction TB\n        T3A[\"~130 files using compat imports\"]\n        T3B[\"30+ files using locationService\"]\n        T3C[\"25+ files using GrafanaRouteComponentProps\"]\n        T3D[\"9 files with direct v5 imports\"]\n    end\n\n    T1A --> T2A\n    T1B --> T2A\n    T1C --> T3A\n    T2A --> T3A\n    T2B --> T3C\n\n    style T1A fill:#f66,stroke:#333,color:#fff\n    style T1B fill:#f66,stroke:#333,color:#fff\n    style T1C fill:#f66,stroke:#333,color:#fff\n    style T1D fill:#f66,stroke:#333,color:#fff\n    style T2A fill:#fa0,stroke:#333\n    style T2B fill:#fa0,stroke:#333\n    style T2C fill:#fa0,stroke:#333\n    style T2D fill:#fa0,stroke:#333\n    style T2E fill:#fa0,stroke:#333\n    style T3A fill:#fc0,stroke:#333\n    style T3B fill:#fc0,stroke:#333\n    style T3C fill:#fc0,stroke:#333\n    style T3D fill:#fc0,stroke:#333\n```\n\n---\n\n## Tier 1: Critical Infrastructure (Migrate First)\n\nThese files are the **blockers** — everything else depends on them.\n\n### 1. `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx`\n- Uses `history` v4 directly (`createBrowserHistory`, `createMemoryHistory`)\n- The entire app navigates through `locationService.push()`, `.replace()`, `.partial()`\n- **Decision needed:** Keep `LocationService` as a facade wired to v6 internals, or replace with `useNavigate` everywhere\n\n### 2. `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx`\n- Still uses `<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>` (v5 pattern)\n- Wraps with `<CompatRouter>` to enable v6 hooks\n- **Target:** Replace with `<BrowserRouter>` or `createBrowserRouter` (data router)\n\n### 3. `public/app/features/plugins/loader/sharedDependencies.ts`\n- Exposes `react-router-dom` (v5) and `react-router` (→ v5-compat) to plugins\n- **Target:** Update both to point to v6 after v5 is removed\n\n### 4. `scripts/webpack/webpack.dev.js` (line 73)\n- Hard-resolves `react-router-dom` to `./node_modules/react-router-dom` (v5)\n- Must be updated alongside the package swap\n\n---\n\n## Tier 2: Core Routing Components (Migrate Second)\n\nThese all import from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` — once Tier 1 is done, these are simple find-and-replace operations:\n\n| File | What Changes |\n|------|-------------|\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Switch compat → `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `Location` from `history` → v6 `Location`; `Params` from compat → `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/hooks.ts` | `useLocation` from compat → `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | `Navigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams` from compat → `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | `Route`, `Routes` from compat → `react-router-dom` |\n\n---\n\n## Tier 3: Feature Code (Migrate Last)\n\n### Direct v5 imports (9 files — migrate these first within Tier 3)\n\nThese still import from `react-router-dom` or `react-router` directly instead of the compat package:\n\n| File | Import |\n|------|--------|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/test/test-utils.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/test/helpers/TestProvider.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx` | `Route`, `Router` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router-dom` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/Repository/RepositoryStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/File/FileStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` |\n| `public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/layout-tabs/TabItemRenderer.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` |\n\n### `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` consumers (25+ files)\n\nThese receive route data via the custom props interface rather than hooks. Key files:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    GRC[\"GrafanaRouteComponentProps<br/>(route, queryParams, location)\"]\n\n    GRC --> DB[\"Dashboard Pages\"]\n    GRC --> EX[\"Explore\"]\n    GRC --> AD[\"Admin\"]\n    GRC --> BD[\"Browse Dashboards\"]\n    GRC --> AU[\"Auth (Signup, Password)\"]\n    GRC --> IM[\"Dashboard Import\"]\n\n    subgraph \"Dashboard Pages (highest impact)\"\n        DB --> D1[\"DashboardPage.tsx\"]\n        DB --> D2[\"DashboardScenePage.tsx\"]\n        DB --> D3[\"SoloPanelPage.tsx\"]\n        DB --> D4[\"PublicDashboardPage.tsx\"]\n        DB --> D5[\"DashboardPageProxy.tsx\"]\n        DB --> D6[\"PublicDashboardScenePage.tsx\"]\n    end\n\n    style GRC fill:#fa0,stroke:#333\n    style DB fill:#fc0,stroke:#333\n```\n\n### `locationService` consumers (30+ files)\n\nThese use the imperative navigation API. The most heavily impacted areas:\n\n```mermaid\npie title locationService Usage by Feature Area\n    \"Scopes\" : 8\n    \"Variables\" : 7\n    \"Search\" : 3\n    \"Dashboard\" : 3\n    \"Plugins/Panels\" : 3\n    \"Teams/ServiceAccounts\" : 3\n    \"Other\" : 6\n```\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Migration Order\n\nHere's what I'd suggest focusing on **next**, based on dependency analysis:\n\n### Phase 1: Prepare the Foundation\n1. **Decide on the v6 router strategy** — `BrowserRouter` (simple) vs `createBrowserRouter` (data router with loaders/actions). This decision affects everything downstream.\n2. **Refactor `LocationService`** to be backed by v6 internals (or plan its deprecation path). This is the hardest piece because 30+ files depend on it.\n\n### Phase 2: Swap the Root Router\n3. **Update `RoutesWrapper.tsx`** — Replace `<Router history={...}>` + `<CompatRouter>` with native v6 router.\n4. **Update `webpack.dev.js`** — Remove or update the `react-router-dom` alias.\n\n### Phase 3: Clean Up Feature Code\n5. **Fix the 9 direct v5 imports** — These are quick wins; just switch to `react-router-dom` (v6) or the compat package as an interim step.\n6. **Migrate `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` consumers** — Convert from props-based route data to `useParams`/`useLocation` hooks. Start with the dashboard pages (highest traffic).\n7. **Migrate `locationService` consumers** — Replace `locationService.push()` with `useNavigate()` where possible. The scopes and variables areas are heaviest.\n\n### Phase 4: Finalize\n8. **Update `sharedDependencies.ts`** — Point plugin router exposure to v6.\n9. **Global find-and-replace** — Swap all remaining `react-router-dom-v5-compat` imports to `react-router-dom`.\n10. **Remove packages** — Uninstall `react-router-dom-v5-compat`, `react-router@5`, `react-router-dom@5`, `@types/react-router`, `@types/react-router-dom`, and `history`.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Wins (Start Here)\n\nIf you want to make incremental progress before tackling the infrastructure, these files are safe to migrate independently:\n\n| File | Change | Risk |\n|------|--------|------|\n| `AppNotificationList.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router-dom` → compat | Trivial |\n| `RepositoryStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` → compat | Trivial |\n| `FileStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` → compat | Trivial |\n| `TabItemRenderer.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` → compat | Trivial |\n| Test helpers (`test-utils.tsx`, `TestProvider.tsx`) | Already need `Router` from v5 for now; defer until root router swaps | Low |\n\nThese 4 non-test files are single-line import changes with no behavioral impact.",
