{
  "conversation_id": "7994de2c-e59a-4a48-a739-b00b73ef42df",
  "generation_id": "14c5157d-cbb0-46e5-b78d-1909b571f17e",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's the full overview of the React Router v5 to v6 migration in the Grafana codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Overview: React Router v5 → v6 Migration\n\n### Current State\n\nGrafana is **mid-migration**. The codebase uses a **compatibility bridge** (`react-router-dom-v5-compat`) to run v6-style APIs on top of a v5 router core. Most feature code has already been migrated to v6 APIs, but the root plumbing and a handful of straggler files remain on v5.\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|-------|--------|\n| Root router (`<Router history={...}>`) | Still v5 |\n| Compatibility bridge (`<CompatRouter>`) | Active |\n| Route rendering (`<Routes>`, `<Route element={...}>`) | v6 via compat |\n| Hooks (`useNavigate`, `useParams`, `useLocation`) | v6 via compat |\n| Redirects (`<Navigate>`) | v6 via compat |\n| Data router (`createBrowserRouter`, `Outlet`) | Not used yet |\n| `LocationService` + `history` v4 | Custom abstraction, still in use |\n\n### Packages Installed\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 | v5 core (still the actual router) |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 | v5 DOM bindings |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 → 6.30.3 | Bridge: exposes v6 APIs on top of v5 |\n| `history` | 4.10.1 | Powers `LocationService` |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Diagrams\n\n### Current State: The Compatibility Bridge\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"Router (v5)<br/>react-router-dom\"] --> B[\"CompatRouter<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    B --> C[\"LocationServiceProvider<br/>@grafana/runtime\"]\n    C --> D[\"AppChrome\"]\n    D --> E[\"Routes (v6 API)<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    E --> F[\"Route element={...}<br/>(v6 pattern)\"]\n    F --> G[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/>auth + params\"]\n    G --> H[\"Page Component\"]\n\n    style A fill:#f9a825,color:#000\n    style B fill:#f9a825,color:#000\n    style E fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style F fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style G fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n```\n\nThe yellow nodes are still v5-dependent. The green nodes use v6 APIs (via the compat package).\n\n### Target State: Full v6\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"createBrowserRouter (v6)<br/>react-router-dom\"] --> B[\"RouterProvider\"]\n    B --> C[\"Root Layout + Outlet\"]\n    C --> D[\"AppChrome\"]\n    D --> E[\"Nested Routes<br/>with Outlet\"]\n    E --> F[\"Page Component\"]\n\n    style A fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style B fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style C fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style D fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style E fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style F fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n```\n\n### Migration Phases\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    P1[\"Phase 1<br/>Migrate feature code<br/>to v6 APIs\"] --> P2[\"Phase 2<br/>Remove straggler<br/>v5 imports\"]\n    P2 --> P3[\"Phase 3<br/>Replace Router +<br/>CompatRouter\"]\n    P3 --> P4[\"Phase 4<br/>Adopt data router<br/>+ Outlet\"]\n    P4 --> P5[\"Phase 5<br/>Remove compat<br/>package\"]\n\n    style P1 fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style P2 fill:#f9a825,color:#000\n    style P3 fill:#ef5350,color:#fff\n    style P4 fill:#ef5350,color:#fff\n    style P5 fill:#ef5350,color:#fff\n```\n\nGreen = done, yellow = in progress, red = not started.\n\n### Import Source Flow (Current)\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"~130+ feature files\"\n        FC[\"Feature Components\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Straggler files (6)\"\n        S1[\"AppNotificationList.tsx\"]\n        S2[\"RepositoryStatusPage.tsx\"]\n        S3[\"FileStatusPage.tsx\"]\n        S4[\"TabItemRenderer.tsx\"]\n        S5[\"RoutesWrapper.tsx\"]\n        S6[\"explore/setup.tsx\"]\n    end\n\n    FC -->|\"import from\"| COMPAT[\"react-router-dom-v5-compat<br/>(v6 APIs)\"]\n    S1 -->|\"import from\"| RRD[\"react-router-dom (v5)\"]\n    S2 -->|\"import from\"| RR[\"react-router (v5)\"]\n    S3 -->|\"import from\"| RR\n    S4 -->|\"import from\"| RR\n    S5 -->|\"import from\"| RRD\n    S6 -->|\"import from\"| RRD\n\n    style COMPAT fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style RRD fill:#f9a825,color:#000\n    style RR fill:#f9a825,color:#000\n```\n\n---\n\n## What's Already Migrated (Phase 1 - Complete)\n\nThe vast majority of v5 patterns are gone:\n\n- **`<Switch>`** → replaced with `<Routes>` (0 remaining)\n- **`useHistory`** → replaced with `useNavigate` (0 remaining from React Router; custom `useHistory` in plugins uses `locationService`)\n- **`useRouteMatch`** → removed (0 remaining)\n- **`<Route component={...}>`** → replaced with `<Route element={...}>` (0 remaining)\n- **`<Route render={...}>`** → removed (0 remaining)\n- **`<Redirect>`** → replaced with `<Navigate>` (0 remaining)\n- **`withRouter`** → removed (0 remaining)\n- **`match.params`** → replaced with `useParams()` (0 remaining)\n\n---\n\n## What Remains (Phase 2 - Straggler Files)\n\nThese 6 files still import directly from `react-router-dom` or `react-router` instead of `react-router-dom-v5-compat`:\n\n### Direct `react-router-dom` imports (v5 package)\n\n| File | Import | Fix |\n|------|--------|-----|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | `Router` | Needs architectural change (Phase 3) |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx` | `useLocation` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx` | `Route`, `Router` | Test helper - change imports |\n\n### Direct `react-router` imports (v5 core package)\n\n| File | Import | Fix |\n|------|--------|-----|\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/Repository/RepositoryStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/File/FileStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/layout-tabs/TabItemRenderer.tsx` | `useLocation` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n\n---\n\n## Candidate Files for a Small-Scope Migration Test\n\nThese are the simplest, lowest-risk files to migrate. Each one only requires changing an import statement from a v5 package to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` — no logic changes needed:\n\n1. **`public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx`**\n   - Change: `import { useLocation } from 'react-router-dom'` → `'react-router-dom-v5-compat'`\n   - Risk: Very low. Single import, widely-used component but trivial change.\n\n2. **`public/app/features/provisioning/Repository/RepositoryStatusPage.tsx`**\n   - Change: `import { useLocation } from 'react-router'` → `'react-router-dom-v5-compat'`\n   - Risk: Very low. Single import swap.\n\n3. **`public/app/features/provisioning/File/FileStatusPage.tsx`**\n   - Change: `import { useLocation } from 'react-router'` → `'react-router-dom-v5-compat'`\n   - Risk: Very low. Same pattern as above.\n\n4. **`public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/layout-tabs/TabItemRenderer.tsx`**\n   - Change: `import { useLocation } from 'react-router'` → `'react-router-dom-v5-compat'`\n   - Risk: Very low. Single import swap.\n\n5. **`public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx`** (test file)\n   - Change: `import { Route, Router } from 'react-router-dom'` → `'react-router-dom-v5-compat'`\n   - Risk: Low. Test helper only, but needs verification that test suite still passes.\n\nFiles 1-4 are all one-line import changes with zero behavioral impact — they're ideal for a first migration PR to validate the process. File 5 is also straightforward but involves a test helper, so it's worth running the explore test suite after the change.",
