  "text": "## React Router API Migration Overview\n\nGrafana is migrating from **React Router v5** (5.3.4) to **React Router v6** using `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (6.30.3) as a bridge. The migration is **largely complete at the component level**, but the root router infrastructure and `LocationService` abstraction remain on v5.\n\n---\n\n### Architecture: Before and After\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"v5 Era (Before)\"\n        A5[\"Router (v5)\"] --> B5[\"Switch\"]\n        B5 --> C5[\"Route component={...}\"]\n        C5 --> D5[\"useHistory()\"]\n        C5 --> E5[\"match.params\"]\n        C5 --> F5[\"Redirect\"]\n        C5 --> G5[\"withRouter HOC\"]\n    end\n```\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Current Hybrid State\"\n        A6[\"Router (v5)\"] --> LS[\"LocationServiceProvider\"]\n        LS --> CR[\"CompatRouter (v5-compat bridge)\"]\n        CR --> B6[\"Routes (v6-style)\"]\n        B6 --> C6[\"Route element={...} (v6-style)\"]\n        C6 --> D6[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        C6 --> E6[\"useParams()\"]\n        C6 --> F6[\"Navigate component\"]\n        C6 --> G6[\"useLocation() / useSearchParams()\"]\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n### Migration Layer Stack\n\nThe key insight is that the app runs a **v5 `Router` at the root**, but wraps it with `CompatRouter` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` so that all feature code can use v6 APIs.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"Root (still v5)\"\n        R[\"&lt;Router history={locationService.getHistory()}&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Bridge Layer\"\n        R --> LSP[\"&lt;LocationServiceProvider&gt;\"]\n        LSP --> C[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt; (v5-compat)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Feature Code (v6-style)\"\n        C --> RTS[\"&lt;Routes&gt;\"]\n        RTS --> RT1[\"&lt;Route path='...' element={...} /&gt;\"]\n        RTS --> RT2[\"&lt;Route path='...' element={...} /&gt;\"]\n        RT1 --> GRW[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper\"]\n        GRW --> FC[\"Feature Component\"]\n    end\n\n    style R fill:#f9d6d6\n    style C fill:#d6f9d6\n    style RTS fill:#d6f9d6\n    style RT1 fill:#d6f9d6\n    style RT2 fill:#d6f9d6\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key API Changes\n\n| v5 API (deprecated) | v6 API (current) | Import source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `<Switch>` | `<Routes>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `<Route component={X}>` | `<Route element={<X />}>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `<Redirect>` | `<Navigate>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `useHistory()` | `useNavigate()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `useRouteMatch()` | `useParams()` / `useMatch()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `match.params` | `useParams()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `withRouter` HOC | hooks directly | removed |\n\n---\n\n### Navigation Dual Path\n\nComponents can navigate via two mechanisms:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Navigation Options\"\n        A[\"Component needs to navigate\"]\n        A -->|\"React Router v6 hook\"| B[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        A -->|\"Grafana abstraction\"| C[\"locationService.push() / .partial()\"]\n    end\n\n    B --> D[\"React Router handles navigation\"]\n    C --> E[\"history v4 API → Router updates\"]\n\n    style B fill:#d6f9d6\n    style C fill:#fff3cd\n```\n\n`locationService` is a Grafana-specific abstraction over `history` v4. It provides `push()`, `partial()`, `replace()`, and observable location changes. It is still widely used, especially in non-component code (Redux actions, services, etc.).\n\n---\n\n### Plugin Compatibility\n\nGrafana exposes both router versions to plugins to allow gradual migration:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Shared Dependencies (plugins)\"\n        SD[\"sharedDependencies.ts\"]\n        SD -->|\"import 'react-router-dom'\"| V5[\"react-router-dom v5\"]\n        SD -->|\"import 'react-router'\"| VC[\"react-router-dom-v5-compat (v6 API)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Plugin Code\"\n        P1[\"Legacy plugin\"] --> V5\n        P2[\"Migrated plugin\"] --> VC\n    end\n\n    style V5 fill:#f9d6d6\n    style VC fill:#d6f9d6\n```\n\nPlugins using `react-router-dom` get v5. Plugins importing `react-router` get the v6-compatible version. Plugins wanting full v6 must bundle `react-router-dom` themselves but share `react-router` (core) with the host.\n\n---\n\n### Migration Status\n\n```mermaid\npie title Migration Progress\n    \"Migrated to v6 APIs (via compat)\" : 130\n    \"Still on v5 (stragglers)\" : 8\n```\n\n**Completed:**\n- ~130+ files import from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n- `<Routes>` / `<Route element={}>` used throughout\n- `useNavigate`, `useParams`, `useLocation`, `useSearchParams` adopted\n- `withRouter`, `useHistory`, `useRouteMatch`, `<Switch>`, `<Redirect>` removed from feature code\n\n**Remaining v5 stragglers (8 files):**\n- `RoutesWrapper.tsx` — root `Router` from `react-router-dom` (v5)\n- `test-utils.tsx`, `TestProvider.tsx` — test infrastructure `Router`\n- `explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx` — explore test helper\n- `AppNotificationList.tsx` — `useLocation` from `react-router-dom`\n- `RepositoryStatusPage.tsx`, `FileStatusPage.tsx`, `TabItemRenderer.tsx` — `useLocation` from `react-router`\n\n**Not yet started:**\n- Replacing root `Router` (v5) with v6's `createBrowserRouter` / `RouterProvider`\n- Migrating `LocationService` away from `history` v4\n- Adopting v6 data router features (loaders, actions, `<Outlet>`)\n- Removing `react-router-dom-v5-compat` entirely\n\n---\n\n### Remaining Migration Path\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    NOW[\"Current: v5 Router + CompatRouter + v6 APIs\"]\n    S1[\"Fix remaining 8 v5 import stragglers\"]\n    S2[\"Replace root Router with createBrowserRouter / RouterProvider\"]\n    S3[\"Migrate LocationService from history v4\"]\n    S4[\"Adopt data router features (loaders, actions, Outlet)\"]\n    S5[\"Remove react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    DONE[\"Fully on React Router v6\"]\n\n    NOW --> S1 --> S2 --> S3 --> S4 --> S5 --> DONE\n\n    style NOW fill:#fff3cd\n    style DONE fill:#d6f9d6\n```\n\nThe key files to understand the current setup are:\n- `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` — root router wiring\n- `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` — route rendering with `<Routes>` / `<Route>`\n- `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` — route wrapper with auth/roles\n- `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` — navigation abstraction\n- `public/app/features/plugins/loader/sharedDependencies.ts` — plugin router exposure",
