  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the React Router migration in the Grafana codebase.\n\n---\n\n## React Router Migration Overview\n\n### Current State: V5 Core + V6 Compat Layer\n\nGrafana is mid-migration from **React Router v5** to **v6**. The approach uses the official `react-router-dom-v5-compat` bridge package, which provides v6-style APIs on top of a v5 router core. The migration is **largely complete at the component level**, but the root router infrastructure is still v5.\n\n| Package | Version |\n|---|---|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 (resolves to 6.30.3) |\n\nThere are **no feature flags** gating the migration — it's a progressive, file-by-file shift.\n\n---\n\n### Architecture: Router Nesting\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"Router (v5)<br/>react-router-dom<br/>history={locationService.getHistory()}\"] --> B[\"LocationServiceProvider<br/>@grafana/runtime\"]\n    B --> C[\"CompatRouter<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    C --> D[\"Routes (v6-style)<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    D --> E[\"Route element={GrafanaRouteWrapper}<br/>per RouteDescriptor\"]\n    E --> F[\"GrafanaRoute<br/>Auth · Keybindings · Suspense · ErrorBoundary\"]\n    F --> G[\"Page Component\"]\n\n    style A fill:#f9d4d4,stroke:#c0392b\n    style C fill:#fdebd0,stroke:#e67e22\n    style D fill:#d5f5e3,stroke:#27ae60\n    style E fill:#d5f5e3,stroke:#27ae60\n```\n\nThe outermost `Router` is still the **v5** one, consuming a `history` v4 object from `locationService`. Inside that, `CompatRouter` provides the bridge so that child components can use v6 hooks and components.\n\n---\n\n### Migration Progress by API Surface\n\n```mermaid\npie title React Router API Usage\n    \"v6 via compat (~130 files)\" : 130\n    \"v5 direct (< 10 files)\" : 10\n```\n\n| API | Migrated to v6? | Notes |\n|-----|-----------------|-------|\n| `<Routes>` / `<Route element={}>` | Yes | Used in `AppWrapper.tsx`, feature pages |\n| `useNavigate` | Yes | Widely adopted |\n| `useParams` | Yes | Widely adopted |\n| `useLocation` | Mostly | A few files still import from `react-router-dom` v5 |\n| `<Navigate>` | Yes | Replaced `<Redirect>` |\n| `<Link>` | Yes | From compat |\n| `<Switch>` | Removed | Only in comments |\n| `useHistory` | Removed | Custom hook wraps `locationService` instead |\n| `withRouter` | Removed | Not found |\n| Root `<Router>` | **No** | Still v5 with `history` v4 |\n| `createBrowserRouter` / `RouterProvider` | **No** | Not adopted yet |\n| `Outlet` | **No** | Not in use |\n\n---\n\n### Two Navigation Paradigms\n\nGrafana has **two coexisting navigation patterns** — the legacy `locationService` abstraction and direct React Router hooks:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Imperative[\"locationService (Imperative)\"]\n        direction TB\n        LP[\"locationService.push('/path')\"]\n        LPR[\"locationService.partial({ key: val })\"]\n        LR[\"locationService.replace(path)\"]\n        LO[\"locationService.getLocationObservable()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Declarative[\"React Router Hooks (Declarative)\"]\n        direction TB\n        UN[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        UP[\"useParams()\"]\n        UL[\"useLocation()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Wrappers[\"Grafana Custom Hooks\"]\n        direction TB\n        UQP[\"useQueryParams()\"]\n        UUP[\"useUrlParams()\"]\n    end\n\n    LP --> H[\"history v4\"]\n    LPR --> H\n    LR --> H\n    H --> R[\"v5 Router\"]\n\n    UN --> CC[\"CompatRouter bridge\"]\n    CC --> R\n\n    UQP --> UL\n    UQP --> LPR\n    UUP --> UL\n    UUP --> LPR\n```\n\n- **`locationService`** — the older pattern, used extensively in non-React contexts (services, state management, Scenes, Angular leftovers). It wraps `history` v4.\n- **React Router hooks** — the newer pattern, adopted in feature components via the compat layer.\n- **Custom hooks** (`useQueryParams`, `useUrlParams`) — bridge both worlds, reading location from React Router but writing via `locationService.partial`.\n\n---\n\n### Key Files\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Root router setup — v5 `Router` + `CompatRouter` |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Maps `RouteDescriptor[]` to v6 `<Route>` elements |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | `getAppRoutes()` — all route definitions |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Route wrapper: auth, keybindings, Suspense |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor`, `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` |\n| `public/app/core/hooks/useQueryParams.ts` | Custom hook bridging React Router + locationService |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | `locationService` singleton, `HistoryWrapper` |\n| `public/app/features/plugins/loader/sharedDependencies.ts` | Plugin shared deps — exposes both v5 and compat |\n\n---\n\n### Plugin Impact\n\nThe migration has a direct impact on the plugin ecosystem:\n\n```mermaid\ntimeline\n    title Plugin Router Migration Timeline\n    v10.0 : App plugins can opt-in to React Router v6\n    v11.0 : React Router v5 deprecated for plugins\n          : Migration guide provided\n    Future : v5 support removal\n```\n\nIn `sharedDependencies.ts`, plugins get:\n- `react-router-dom` → v5 (for plugins still on v5)\n- `react-router` → `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (for plugins adopting v6)\n\n---\n\n### Remaining Migration Work\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Done[\"Completed\"]\n        A[\"Component-level v6 APIs<br/>(~130 files)\"]\n        B[\"<Navigate> replaces <Redirect>\"]\n        C[\"<Routes>/<Route element> replaces <Switch>\"]\n        D[\"useNavigate replaces useHistory\"]\n        E[\"Plugin compat layer\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Remaining[\"Not Yet Done\"]\n        F[\"Root Router → createBrowserRouter\"]\n        G[\"Adopt RouterProvider / Outlet\"]\n        H[\"Remove history v4 dependency\"]\n        I[\"Migrate locationService to v6 navigate\"]\n        J[\"Fix ~10 files still importing from v5\"]\n    end\n\n    Done --> Remaining\n\n    style Done fill:#d5f5e3,stroke:#27ae60\n    style Remaining fill:#fdebd0,stroke:#e67e22\n```\n\n1. **Root router swap** — Replace the v5 `<Router history={...}>` with v6's `createBrowserRouter` / `<RouterProvider>`. This is the biggest remaining step.\n2. **Drop `history` v4** — `locationService` is built on `history` v4, which is incompatible with v6's internal history. This abstraction will need to be reworked or replaced.\n3. **Adopt data router features** — `Outlet`, loaders, actions are not used yet.\n4. **Clean up straggler imports** — A handful of files still import directly from `react-router-dom` (v5) instead of the compat package.\n5. **Remove compat layer** — Once the root router is v6, `react-router-dom-v5-compat` and `CompatRouter` can be removed, and all imports can shift to `react-router-dom` v6 directly.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThe migration follows the [official incremental upgrade path](https://reactrouter.com/upgrading/v5): install `react-router-dom-v5-compat`, keep the v5 router at the root, and progressively migrate components to v6 APIs. Grafana is **~90% through** this process — virtually all components use v6 hooks and components via the compat layer. The final phase is swapping the root router infrastructure from v5 to v6 and decoupling `locationService` from `history` v4.",
