  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "I'm currently in Ask mode so I can't create files, but I can design the full skill for you. Here's what I'd create — you can switch to Agent mode and ask me to create it, or I can walk you through the details first.\n\n---\n\n### Proposed Skill: `simple-mermaid-diagrams`\n\n**Location:** `~/.cursor/skills/simple-mermaid-diagrams/`\n\n**SKILL.md:**\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: simple-mermaid-diagrams\ndescription: Generate clear, simple Mermaid diagrams for technical communication. Use when explaining architecture, migration status, workflows, data flow, or system relationships. Use when the user asks for diagrams, visual explanations, or when a concept benefits from visual representation.\n---\n\n# Simple Mermaid Diagrams\n\n## Principles\n\n1. **Fewer nodes wins.** If a diagram has more than ~12 nodes, split it or simplify.\n2. **Label everything.** Every node gets a human-readable label — no bare IDs.\n3. **One idea per diagram.** Don't combine architecture + workflow + status in one chart.\n4. **Use line breaks** (`<br/>`) in node labels instead of long single lines.\n5. **Skip decoration.** No icons, colors, or styling unless it encodes meaning (e.g. highlighting a problem area).\n\n## Diagram Type Selection\n\n| Need | Diagram Type | Direction |\n|------|-------------|-----------|\n| Architecture / hierarchy | `graph TD` | Top-down |\n| Transformation / pipeline | `graph LR` | Left-right |\n| Sequential phases | `graph TD` with chained subgraphs | Top-down |\n| Process over time | `graph LR` or `sequenceDiagram` | Left-right |\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Architecture — Use subgraphs for logical grouping\n\n~~~markdown\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Layer Name\"\n        A[\"Component A\"]\n        B[\"Component B\"]\n    end\n    subgraph \"Another Layer\"\n        C[\"Component C\"]\n    end\n    A --> C\n    B --> C\n```\n~~~\n\n### Migration / Phase Status — Chain subgraphs vertically\n\n~~~markdown\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Phase 1 — Done\"\n        A1[Step one] --> A2[Step two]\n    end\n    subgraph \"Phase 2 — In Progress\"\n        B1[Step three]\n    end\n    subgraph \"Phase 3 — Future\"\n        C1[Step four]\n    end\n    A2 --> B1\n    B1 --> C1\n```\n~~~\n\n### Transformation — Show before/after with LR flow\n\n~~~markdown\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Old\"\n        A[\"Legacy API\"]\n    end\n    subgraph \"New\"\n        B[\"Modern API\"]\n    end\n    A -->|\"migrated to\"| B\n```\n~~~\n\n### Data / Request Flow — Linear chain with edge labels\n\n~~~markdown\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    Client -->|\"HTTP\"| Gateway\n    Gateway -->|\"gRPC\"| Service\n    Service -->|\"SQL\"| Database\n```\n~~~\n\n## Rules\n\n- Prefer `graph` over `flowchart` — wider rendering support.\n- Use `[\"Label\"]` for nodes (square brackets). Use `[\"Label<br/>second line\"]` for multi-line.\n- Use `-->|\"label\"|` for labeled edges. Keep edge labels to 3-4 words max.\n- Use `subgraph \"Title\"` with quotes around the title.\n- Avoid `style` and `classDef` unless color encodes specific meaning (e.g. red = blocked, yellow = warning).\n- When styling is meaningful, use `fill` only — skip borders and font changes:\n  ```\n  style NodeId fill:#fff3cd\n  ```\n- Keep diagrams **under 20 lines** of Mermaid source. If longer, split into multiple diagrams.\n- Never nest subgraphs more than one level deep.\n```\n\n---\n\n### Why this structure works\n\n- **Short** (~80 lines) — well under the 500-line target, won't bloat the context window.\n- **Concrete patterns** — each diagram type has a copy-paste template rather than abstract guidelines.\n- **Decision table** — the \"Diagram Type Selection\" table makes it fast to pick the right format.\n- **Opinionated defaults** — `graph` over `flowchart`, square-bracket nodes, no decorative styling — so diagrams stay consistent without decision fatigue.\n\nWant me to switch to Agent mode and create this skill, or would you like to adjust anything first?",
