  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the React Router migration in the Grafana codebase.\n\n---\n\n## React Router Migration Overview\n\n### What's happening\n\nGrafana is incrementally migrating from **React Router v5** (5.3.4) to **React Router v6** using the official `react-router-dom-v5-compat` compatibility package (6.30.3). This follows the [official incremental upgrade path](https://reactrouter.com/upgrading/v5) — keeping the v5 router at the root while progressively adopting v6 APIs throughout the component tree.\n\n### Migration Strategy\n\nThe approach is a **bottom-up, file-by-file migration** with no feature flags. The compat layer lets v6-style APIs (`useNavigate`, `<Routes>`, `<Navigate>`) work on top of the v5 `<Router>`.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"Phase 1: Install compat package ✅\"] --> B[\"Phase 2: Wrap tree with CompatRouter ✅\"]\n    B --> C[\"Phase 3: Migrate components to v6 APIs ✅ ~95%\"]\n    C --> D[\"Phase 4: Replace root v5 Router with v6\"]\n    D --> E[\"Phase 5: Migrate LocationService off history v4\"]\n    E --> F[\"Phase 6: Adopt data router features<br/>(loaders, actions, Outlet)\"]\n    F --> G[\"Phase 7: Remove compat package<br/>+ v5 dependencies\"]\n\n    style A fill:#2d6a2d,color:#fff\n    style B fill:#2d6a2d,color:#fff\n    style C fill:#5a8a3a,color:#fff\n    style D fill:#b8860b,color:#fff\n    style E fill:#b8860b,color:#fff\n    style F fill:#8b4513,color:#fff\n    style G fill:#8b4513,color:#fff\n```\n\n### Current Architecture\n\nThe root of the app uses a v5 `<Router>` with a `<CompatRouter>` bridge, while almost all child components use v6 APIs.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"V5 Layer (legacy)\"\n        Router[\"Router history={locationService.getHistory()}\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Bridge Layer\"\n        Compat[\"CompatRouter<br/>(react-router-dom-v5-compat)\"]\n        LocSvc[\"LocationService<br/>(history v4 wrapper)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"V6 Layer (current)\"\n        Routes[\"&lt;Routes&gt;\"]\n        Route[\"&lt;Route element={...}&gt;\"]\n        Nav[\"&lt;Navigate&gt;\"]\n        Hooks[\"useNavigate / useParams / useLocation\"]\n    end\n\n    Router -->|wraps| Compat\n    LocSvc -->|shared history instance| Router\n    Compat -->|enables| Routes\n    Routes --> Route\n    Route --> Nav\n    Route --> Hooks\n```\n\n### API Replacements\n\n| v5 API (removed) | v6 API (in use) | Import source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `<Switch>` | `<Routes>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `<Route component={X}>` | `<Route element={<X />}>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `<Redirect>` | `<Navigate>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `useHistory()` | `useNavigate()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `useRouteMatch()` | `useParams()` / `useMatch()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `withRouter` HOC | hooks | removed |\n\n### Route Registration Flow\n\nRoutes flow through a centralized registration system:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Route Sources\"\n        Main[\"routes.tsx<br/>(core routes)\"]\n        Plugin[\"getAppPluginRoutes()\"]\n        Alert[\"getAlertingRoutes()\"]\n        Profile[\"getProfileRoutes()\"]\n        Conn[\"getDataConnectionsRoutes()\"]\n        Prov[\"getProvisioningRoutes()\"]\n        Extra[\"extraRoutes[]<br/>(enterprise)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Registration\"\n        GetApp[\"getAppRoutes()<br/>→ RouteDescriptor[]\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Rendering\"\n        AW[\"AppWrapper.renderRoute()\"]\n        GRW[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/>(auth, roles, redirects)\"]\n        GR[\"GrafanaRoute<br/>(renders component)\"]\n    end\n\n    Main --> GetApp\n    Plugin --> GetApp\n    Alert --> GetApp\n    Profile --> GetApp\n    Conn --> GetApp\n    Prov --> GetApp\n    Extra --> GetApp\n\n    GetApp --> AW\n    AW -->|\"&lt;Route element={...}&gt;\"| GRW\n    GRW --> GR\n```\n\nEach `RouteDescriptor` has a `component` property (not `element`), and `AppWrapper.renderRoute()` wraps it in the v6-style `<Route element={<GrafanaRouteWrapper />}>` pattern. `GrafanaRouteWrapper` handles authentication, role checks, and redirects before rendering the actual page component.\n\n### Key Files\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Root v5 `<Router>` + `<CompatRouter>` |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Renders `<Routes>` and `<Route element={...}>` (v6 style) |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central route definitions (`getAppRoutes()`) |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Route wrapper for auth, roles, lazy loading |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor` type definition |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | Navigation service wrapping `history` v4 |\n| `public/app/features/plugins/loader/sharedDependencies.ts` | Plugin router compatibility (exposes both v5 and v6) |\n\n### Current State\n\n**What's done (~95%):**\n- `<Switch>` fully replaced with `<Routes>`\n- `<Redirect>` fully replaced with `<Navigate>`\n- ~140+ files import from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n- `useNavigate`, `useParams`, `useLocation` used throughout\n\n**Stragglers (~8 files):**\n- `RoutesWrapper.tsx` — root v5 `<Router>`\n- 3 provisioning/dashboard files import `useLocation` from `react-router` (v5 core)\n- 1 file imports `useLocation` from `react-router-dom` (v5 DOM)\n- Test utilities still use v5 `<Router>` directly\n\n**Not yet started:**\n- Root router replacement (v5 `<Router>` → v6 `createBrowserRouter` / `RouterProvider`)\n- `LocationService` migration off `history` v4\n- Data router features (loaders, actions, `<Outlet>`)\n- Removal of the compat package\n\n### Plugin Compatibility\n\nGrafana exposes both v5 and v6 router packages to plugins via `sharedDependencies.ts`:\n- `react-router-dom` → v5 (for legacy plugins)\n- `react-router` → remapped to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (for plugins using v6 APIs)\n\nThis was documented as a **breaking change in Grafana v11** — plugins were told to migrate to v6 APIs, with v5 formally deprecated.\n\n### LocationService Dependency\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    LS[\"LocationService<br/>(HistoryWrapper)\"]\n    H4[\"history v4<br/>(createBrowserHistory)\"]\n    R5[\"v5 Router\"]\n    IC[\"interceptLinkClicks\"]\n    UP[\"useUrlParams\"]\n    PR[\"Prompt.tsx<br/>(unsaved changes)\"]\n    FT[\"~100+ feature files\"]\n\n    LS -->|wraps| H4\n    H4 -->|passed to| R5\n    LS -->|push/replace/partial| FT\n    IC -->|locationService.push| LS\n    UP -->|locationService.partial| LS\n    PR -->|history.block| H4\n```\n\n`LocationService` is the central navigation API used across ~100+ files. It wraps `history` v4 and shares the same history instance with the v5 router. Migrating this to v6 is the key remaining challenge — it requires replacing the `history` v4 dependency and updating all consumers.\n\n### Summary\n\nThe migration is well past the halfway point. The component-level migration to v6 APIs is essentially complete. The remaining work is architectural: replacing the root router, decoupling from `history` v4, and eventually adopting v6 data router patterns. The compat layer makes this safe to do incrementally without breaking plugins or existing functionality.",
