  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-max-thinking-fast",
  "text": "Here's the status of each file:\n\n**`PlaylistNewPage.tsx`** — No React Router imports at all. It uses Grafana's `locationService.push()` for navigation, so there's nothing to migrate on this file.\n\n**`PlaylistEditPage.tsx`** — Partially migrated. On line 1 it imports from the **compatibility shim**:\n\n```1:1:public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistEditPage.tsx\nimport { useParams } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n```\n\nThis is the transitional `react-router-dom-v5-compat` package, not the final `react-router-dom` v6 import. So it's been moved off the old v5 API but hasn't completed the migration to a direct v6 import.\n\nTo fully migrate `PlaylistEditPage.tsx`, the import would need to change from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` to `react-router-dom`. The `RouteParams` interface on lines 12-14 is also unused (the v5 pattern) — `useParams()` in v6 just returns a `Record<string, string | undefined>` without a generic, and the component already destructures `uid` with a default on line 17, so the interface can be removed.",
