{
  "conversation_id": "200ed786-2f1d-4586-b13b-39add82a30b6",
  "generation_id": "bb292e58-9832-4884-b6d0-d391b60542ea",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "# Grafana Codebase Overview\n\n## What is Grafana?\n\nGrafana is an open-source analytics and monitoring platform (AGPL-3.0) by Grafana Labs. It provides dashboards, alerting, data exploration, and visualization for metrics, logs, and traces.\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology |\n|-------|------------|\n| **Frontend** | React 18.3, TypeScript 5.9 |\n| **Backend** | Go 1.25 |\n| **State** | Redux 5 + Redux Toolkit 2 |\n| **Routing** | React Router 5.3.4 + `react-router-dom-v5-compat` 6.26+ |\n| **Build** | Webpack 5, Nx 21, Lerna 9, Yarn 4 (Berry) |\n| **Schemas** | CUE (resource kinds) |\n\n## High-Level Directory Structure\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    ROOT[grafana/] --> PUBLIC[public/app/ - Frontend React App]\n    ROOT --> PKG[pkg/ - Go Backend Packages]\n    ROOT --> APPS[apps/ - Go API Apps]\n    ROOT --> PACKAGES[packages/ - Shared NPM Packages]\n    ROOT --> DOCS[docs/ - Documentation]\n    ROOT --> SCRIPTS[scripts/ - Build & CI]\n    ROOT --> E2E[e2e-playwright/ - E2E Tests]\n    ROOT --> CONF[conf/ - Configuration]\n    ROOT --> KINDS[kinds/ - CUE Schemas]\n\n    PUBLIC --> FEATURES[features/ - 50+ Feature Modules]\n    PUBLIC --> CORE[core/ - Shared App Logic]\n    PUBLIC --> ROUTES[routes/ - Route Definitions]\n\n    PKG --> SERVICES[services/ - 76+ Business Logic Modules]\n    PKG --> API[api/ - HTTP Handlers]\n    PKG --> APISERVER[apiserver/ - K8s-style API Server]\n\n    PACKAGES --> UI[\"@grafana/ui\"]\n    PACKAGES --> DATA[\"@grafana/data\"]\n    PACKAGES --> RUNTIME[\"@grafana/runtime\"]\n    PACKAGES --> SCENES[\"@grafana/scenes\"]\n```\n\n### Key Shared Packages (`packages/`)\n\n- `@grafana/ui` -- UI component library\n- `@grafana/data` -- Data types and utilities\n- `@grafana/runtime` -- Runtime services (including `locationService`)\n- `@grafana/scenes` -- Scene-based dashboard framework\n- `@grafana/api-clients` -- Generated API clients\n- `@grafana/eslint-rules` -- Custom ESLint rules\n\n---\n\n## React Router Migration: v5 to v6\n\nThe codebase is in a **hybrid state** -- the root router is still React Router v5, but almost all component-level routing APIs have been migrated to v6-style via the official compatibility package.\n\n### Current Routing Dependencies\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 | Core v5 router |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 | v5 DOM bindings |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 | v6 API bridge running on v5 |\n| `history` | 4.10.1 | History API (used by v5 + `locationService`) |\n\n### Migration Approach\n\nGrafana uses the official **incremental migration** strategy recommended by React Router. The `react-router-dom-v5-compat` package provides v6 APIs (`useNavigate`, `useParams`, `Routes`, `Route`, `Navigate`) that work on top of the v5 router foundation.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Current State (Hybrid)\"\n        V5_ROUTER[\"v5 Router\\n(react-router-dom)\"] --> COMPAT[\"CompatRouter\\n(v5-compat bridge)\"]\n        COMPAT --> V6_APIS[\"v6-style APIs\\nuseNavigate, useParams\\nRoutes, Route, Navigate\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Future State\"\n        V6_ROUTER[\"v6 BrowserRouter or\\ncreateBrowserRouter\"] --> V6_NATIVE[\"Native v6 APIs\\nloaders, actions, Outlet\"]\n    end\n\n    V6_APIS -.->|\"remaining\\nmigration\"| V6_ROUTER\n\n    style V5_ROUTER fill:#f9a825,color:#000\n    style COMPAT fill:#42a5f5,color:#000\n    style V6_APIS fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style V6_ROUTER fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n    style V6_NATIVE fill:#66bb6a,color:#000\n```\n\n### API Patterns: Before and After\n\n| v5 Pattern (old) | v6 Pattern (current) |\n|---|---|\n| `useHistory()` | `useNavigate()` |\n| `match.params` | `useParams()` |\n| `<Switch>` | `<Routes>` |\n| `<Route component={C}>` | `<Route element={<C />}>` |\n| `<Redirect to=\"...\">` | `<Navigate to=\"...\" replace>` |\n| `withRouter` HOC | `useLocation`, `useParams` hooks |\n\n### Files Still on v5 Imports (~8 files)\n\nA handful of files still import directly from `react-router-dom` or `react-router` (v5) rather than the compat package -- primarily the root `RoutesWrapper.tsx` (which must use v5 `Router`), test utilities, and a few feature pages.\n\n---\n\n## Routing Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    INIT[\"GrafanaApp.init()\"] --> AW[\"AppWrapper\"]\n    AW --> RW[\"RouterWrapper\\n(RoutesWrapper.tsx)\"]\n\n    RW --> V5R[\"v5 Router\\nhistory=locationService.getHistory()\"]\n    V5R --> LSP[\"LocationServiceProvider\"]\n    LSP --> CR[\"CompatRouter\\n(v6 API bridge)\"]\n    CR --> CHROME[\"AppChrome\\n(MegaMenu, TopBar)\"]\n    CHROME --> ROUTES_COMP[\"&lt;Routes&gt;\\nfrom v5-compat\"]\n\n    ROUTES_COMP --> R1[\"Route: /d/:uid\\n→ DashboardPage\"]\n    ROUTES_COMP --> R2[\"Route: /explore\\n→ ExplorePage\"]\n    ROUTES_COMP --> R3[\"Route: /alerting/*\\n→ AlertingRoutes\"]\n    ROUTES_COMP --> R4[\"Route: /a/:pluginId/*\\n→ AppRootPage\"]\n    ROUTES_COMP --> R5[\"Route: /*\\n→ catch-all\"]\n\n    R1 --> GRW[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper\"]\n    R2 --> GRW\n    R3 --> GRW\n    R4 --> GRW\n    R5 --> GRW\n\n    GRW --> AUTH{\"Auth check\\n+ Role check\"}\n    AUTH -->|pass| GR[\"GrafanaRoute\\nErrorBoundary + Suspense\"]\n    AUTH -->|fail| LOGIN[\"/login redirect\"]\n    GR --> PAGE[\"route.component\\n(lazy-loaded page)\"]\n```\n\n### Key Routing Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Root router: v5 `Router` + `CompatRouter` |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | `getAppRoutes()` returns flat `RouteDescriptor[]` |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Maps route descriptors to `<Route>` elements |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Auth, roles, error boundary per route |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor`, `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` |\n\n### Route Configuration\n\nRoutes are defined as a **flat array** of `RouteDescriptor` objects -- there is no nested route tree. Each descriptor has:\n\n- `path` -- URL pattern (e.g. `/d/:uid/:slug?`)\n- `component` -- lazy-loaded page component\n- Optional: `roles`, `chromeless`, `allowAnonymous`, `sensitive`\n\nRoutes are assembled from multiple feature modules in `getAppRoutes()`:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    GAR[\"getAppRoutes()\"] --> PLUGINS[\"getAppPluginRoutes()\\n(registered first)\"]\n    GAR --> DASH[\"Dashboard routes\"]\n    GAR --> CONN[\"getDataConnectionsRoutes()\"]\n    GAR --> ALERT[\"getAlertingRoutes()\"]\n    GAR --> PROFILE[\"getProfileRoutes()\"]\n    GAR --> CATALOG[\"getPluginCatalogRoutes()\"]\n    GAR --> PUB[\"getPublicDashboardRoutes()\"]\n    GAR --> PROV[\"getProvisioningRoutes()\"]\n    GAR --> ENT[\"extraRoutes\\n(Enterprise extensions)\"]\n    GAR --> CATCH[\"/* catch-all\"]\n```\n\nPlugin routes are registered **first** so they can override core pages.\n\n---\n\n## `locationService` -- Grafana's Routing Abstraction\n\nGrafana has its own routing abstraction layer that sits between application code and React Router:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Application Code\"\n        APP_CODE[\"Feature code\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Routing APIs\"\n        LS[\"locationService\\n(@grafana/runtime)\"]\n        RR_HOOKS[\"React Router v6 Hooks\\n(via compat)\"]\n        INTERCEPT[\"interceptLinkClicks\\n(document-level handler)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Foundation\"\n        HISTORY[\"history v4\\n(createBrowserHistory)\"]\n        V5[\"React Router v5\\n(Router component)\"]\n    end\n\n    APP_CODE -->|\"push / replace / partial\"| LS\n    APP_CODE -->|\"useNavigate / useLocation\"| RR_HOOKS\n    INTERCEPT -->|\"<a> click → push()\"| LS\n\n    LS -->|\"owns\"| HISTORY\n    HISTORY -->|\"passed via getHistory()\"| V5\n    RR_HOOKS -->|\"reads from\"| V5\n```\n\nKey `locationService` methods:\n- `push(location)` / `replace(location)` -- full navigation\n- `partial(query, replace)` -- update query params only\n- `getHistory()` -- returns `history` instance (fed to v5 Router)\n- `getLocation()` / `getSearch()` -- current location info\n\nIt's used in **150+ files** across the codebase and acts as the primary navigation API alongside React Router hooks.\n\n---\n\n## Remaining Migration Work\n\nThe final steps to complete the v6 migration would be:\n\n1. **Replace the root v5 `<Router>`** with v6 `BrowserRouter` or `createBrowserRouter` + `RouterProvider`\n2. **Update the ~8 files** still importing from `react-router-dom`/`react-router` v5\n3. **Remove `react-router-dom-v5-compat`** dependency (no longer needed once fully on v6)\n4. **Optionally adopt data router APIs** -- `createBrowserRouter`, loaders, actions, `Outlet` for nested routes\n5. **Align `locationService`** with the v6 history/navigation model (v6 doesn't expose a `history` object the same way)\n\nThe migration is well-advanced -- the vast majority of component code already uses v6 patterns via the compat layer. The remaining work is primarily at the infrastructure/root level.",
