  "text": "\nMain files involved in the Bookmarks page UI:\n\n---\n\n## Core page component\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage.tsx`** | Main page component. Renders the layout, empty state, and grid of bookmark cards. Defines the grid styles (`gridTemplateColumns`, `gridAutoRows`, etc.). |\n\n---\n\n## Card component\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.tsx`** | Card used for each bookmark. Handles heading, description, link, and optional category styles (primary, secondary, success, warning, error). |\n\n---\n\n## Shared layout and data\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/core/components/Page/Page.tsx`** | Page wrapper (header, scroll, layout). Used via `<Page navId=\"bookmarks\">`. |\n| **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/hooks.ts`** | `usePinnedItems()` – returns bookmark URLs from user preferences. |\n| **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.ts`** | `findByUrl()` – finds nav items by URL in the nav tree. |\n\n---\n\n## Related reference\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPage.tsx`** | Similar landing page layout (e.g. Explore). Uses the same grid and `NavLandingPageCard`. |\n| **`public/app/routes/routes.tsx`** (lines 537–540) | Route definition for `/bookmarks`. |\n\n---\n\n## UI components from `@grafana/ui`\n\n- **`EmptyState`** – empty state when there are no bookmarks\n- **`Card`** – used inside `NavLandingPageCard`\n\n---\n\n## Translations\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/locales/en-US/grafana.json`** (around line 3614) | `bookmarks-page.empty.message` and `bookmarks-page.empty.tip` |\n\n---\n\n## Suggested starting points\n\n1. **Layout and grid** → `BookmarksPage.tsx` (lines 55–62, `getStyles`)\n2. **Card appearance** → `NavLandingPageCard.tsx`\n3. **Empty state** → `BookmarksPage.tsx` (lines 28–35) and `EmptyState` from `@grafana/ui`\n4. **Page shell** → `Page.tsx` and its subcomponents (`PageHeader`, `PageContents`, etc.)",
