  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a summary of what was added to the `BookmarksPage`:\n\n**Category system** -- Bookmarks are automatically assigned to one of three categories based on their URL:\n\n- **Operations** (`warning` style): URLs matching `/alerting`, `/explore`, `/connections`, `/monitoring`\n- **Admin** (`error` style): URLs matching `/admin`, `/org`, `/plugins`, `/correlations`, `/datasources`\n- **Content** (`primary` style): URLs matching `/d/`, `/dashboards`, `/playlists`, `/library-panels` (also the default fallback)\n\n**Filtering and grouping UI** using existing Grafana components:\n\n- `FilterInput` (from `@grafana/ui`) for text search across bookmark name and description\n- `RadioButtonGroup` (from `@grafana/ui`) with \"All\", \"Operations\", \"Admin\", and \"Content\" toggle buttons to filter by category\n- `Stack` for vertical layout of the action bar and grouped sections\n\n**Grouped rendering** -- when \"All\" is selected, bookmarks display under `h5` section headers (OPERATIONS, ADMIN, CONTENT) with each card color-coded using the existing `category` prop on `NavLandingPageCard`. When a specific category is selected, only that group shows.\n\n**Empty state** -- if no bookmarks match the current filter + search combination, a \"No bookmarks found\" empty state is shown (using the `not-found` variant).",
