  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the React Router migration status in Grafana.\n\n---\n\n## Current State: Hybrid v5/v6 via Compatibility Layer\n\nGrafana is **mid-migration** from React Router v5 to v6. The strategy uses `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (^6.26.1) as a bridge, allowing v6 APIs to work within the existing v5 `Router` shell.\n\n### Dependencies\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 | Legacy core |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 | Legacy DOM bindings |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 | Bridge layer providing v6 APIs |\n| `@types/react-router` | 5.1.20 | v5 types |\n| `@types/react-router-dom` | 5.3.3 | v5 types |\n\n### Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"Router (v5)<br/>react-router-dom<br/>history={locationService.getHistory()}\"] --> B[\"CompatRouter<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    B --> C[\"Routes (v6 API)<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    C --> D[\"Route element={...} (v6 API)\"]\n    D --> E[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/>uses useLocation(), useParams()\"]\n    E --> F[\"GrafanaRoute<br/>renders route.component\"]\n    F --> G[\"Page Components<br/>receive GrafanaRouteComponentProps\"]\n\n    style A fill:#f66,stroke:#333,color:#fff\n    style B fill:#fc6,stroke:#333\n    style C fill:#6c6,stroke:#333\n    style D fill:#6c6,stroke:#333\n    style E fill:#6c6,stroke:#333\n    style F fill:#fc6,stroke:#333\n    style G fill:#fc6,stroke:#333\n```\n\nThe red node is pure v5, green nodes use v6 APIs, and orange nodes are compatibility/legacy patterns that still need migration.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Progress by Pattern\n\n```mermaid\npie title API Pattern Migration Status\n    \"v6 APIs (via v5-compat)\" : 130\n    \"GrafanaRouteComponentProps (legacy pattern)\" : 18\n    \"Direct v5 imports\" : 3\n    \"locationService.getHistory() (v5 history)\" : 9\n```\n\n### What's Already Migrated (v6 APIs via compat)\n\nThese patterns are in active use across **~130 files** and are already v6-compatible:\n\n| Pattern | Source | Status |\n|---------|--------|--------|\n| `<Routes>` / `<Route element={...}>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | Used in `AppWrapper`, `Connections`, etc. |\n| `<Navigate>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ~15 usages, replaced `<Redirect>` |\n| `useNavigate()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ~20 files |\n| `useParams()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ~50 files |\n| `useLocation()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | Widespread |\n| `useSearchParams()` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | Several files |\n| `Link` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | Widespread |\n\n### What's Gone (no remaining v5 usage)\n\n| Legacy Pattern | Count |\n|---------------|-------|\n| `<Switch>` | 0 |\n| `<Redirect>` | 0 |\n| `useHistory` (React Router) | 0 |\n| `useRouteMatch` | 0 |\n| `withRouter` HOC | 0 |\n| `match.params` | 0 |\n| `RouteComponentProps` (React Router) | 0 |\n\n### What Still Needs Migration\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Remaining v5 Artifacts\"\n        R1[\"v5 Router shell<br/>(RoutesWrapper.tsx)\"]\n        R2[\"3 files importing<br/>from react-router-dom v5\"]\n        R3[\"~18 files using<br/>GrafanaRouteComponentProps\"]\n        R4[\"~9 files using<br/>locationService.getHistory()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Target State\"\n        T1[\"v6 createBrowserRouter<br/>or unstable_HistoryRouter\"]\n        T2[\"All imports from<br/>react-router-dom v6\"]\n        T3[\"Components use hooks<br/>directly (useParams, etc.)\"]\n        T4[\"v6-native history<br/>integration\"]\n    end\n\n    R1 --> T1\n    R2 --> T2\n    R3 --> T3\n    R4 --> T4\n\n    style R1 fill:#f66,stroke:#333,color:#fff\n    style R2 fill:#f96,stroke:#333\n    style R3 fill:#fc6,stroke:#333\n    style R4 fill:#fc6,stroke:#333\n    style T1 fill:#6c6,stroke:#333\n    style T2 fill:#6c6,stroke:#333\n    style T3 fill:#6c6,stroke:#333\n    style T4 fill:#6c6,stroke:#333\n```\n\n---\n\n## Remaining Work Breakdown\n\n### 1. Direct v5 `react-router-dom` Imports (3 files)\n\nOnly three files still import directly from the v5 package:\n\n| File | Import | Usage |\n|------|--------|-------|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | `Router` | Top-level v5 Router shell |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx` | `useLocation` | Should switch to v5-compat import |\n| `public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx` | `Route`, `Router` | Test helper |\n\n### 2. `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` Pattern (~18 files)\n\nThese page components receive `route`, `queryParams`, and `location` as props via `GrafanaRoute` instead of using hooks directly. This is a v5-era indirection layer.\n\n### 3. `locationService.getHistory()` (~9 files)\n\nUses of the v5 `history` object that would need to be replaced with v6-native navigation.\n\n---\n\n## Suggested Files for a Narrow-Scope Migration Test\n\nHere are candidates ranked by risk/effort, starting with the easiest:\n\n### Tier 1 -- Trivial (single import swap)\n\n1. **`public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx`**\n   - Just change `from 'react-router-dom'` to `from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat'` for `useLocation`\n   - Zero logic changes needed\n\n### Tier 2 -- Small page components using `GrafanaRouteComponentProps`\n\nThese are small, self-contained pages that could be converted from prop-based routing to hook-based routing:\n\n2. **`public/app/core/components/Signup/SignupPage.tsx`** -- Simple signup form\n3. **`public/app/core/components/ForgottenPassword/ChangePasswordPage.tsx`** -- Simple form page\n4. **`public/app/features/admin/UserCreatePage.tsx`** -- Admin user creation\n5. **`public/app/features/admin/ldap/LdapPage.tsx`** -- LDAP admin page\n6. **`public/app/features/manage-dashboards/DashboardImportPage.tsx`** -- Dashboard import\n\nFor these, the migration pattern would be:\n- Remove `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` from the component signature\n- Use `useLocation()` and `useParams()` hooks directly inside the component\n- Use `useSearchParams()` or `locationSearchToObject(useLocation().search)` for query params\n\n### Tier 3 -- Test helpers (isolated risk)\n\n7. **`public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx`** -- Switch test `Router`/`Route` imports to v5-compat\n\nThese test files are low-risk because they don't affect production behavior.\n\n---\n\nFor a **first narrow-scope migration test**, I'd recommend starting with file **#1** (`AppNotificationList.tsx`) as it's a pure import swap with zero risk, then moving to one of the Tier 2 pages like `SignupPage.tsx` or `ChangePasswordPage.tsx` to validate the pattern of removing `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` in favor of hooks.",
