  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the React Router architecture in Grafana and the ongoing v5 → v6 migration.\n\n---\n\n## Current State: Hybrid v5/v6\n\nGrafana is mid-migration from React Router **v5** to **v6**. The approach is **bottom-up**: individual components have been migrated to v6 APIs via the `react-router-dom-v5-compat` compatibility package, but the root router is still v5.\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | 5.3.4 | Core v5 router (root) |\n| `react-router-dom` | 5.3.4 | v5 DOM bindings (root) |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | ^6.26.1 | v6 API shim for components |\n| `history` | 4.10.1 | v5-compatible history API |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Diagram\n\nThe router hierarchy nests a v6 compat layer inside the v5 root:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"v5 Router<br/>(react-router-dom)<br/>history v4\"] --> B[\"LocationServiceProvider<br/>(grafana-runtime)\"]\n    B --> C[\"CompatRouter<br/>(react-router-dom-v5-compat)\"]\n    C --> D[\"AppChrome<br/>(shell, nav, mega menu)\"]\n    D --> E[\"Routes (v6-style)<br/>(react-router-dom-v5-compat)\"]\n    E --> F[\"Route element={GrafanaRouteWrapper}<br/>per RouteDescriptor\"]\n    F --> G[\"GrafanaRoute<br/>(auth, roles, error boundary)\"]\n    G --> H[\"Feature Page Component\"]\n\n    style A fill:#f9d,stroke:#333\n    style C fill:#bdf,stroke:#333\n    style E fill:#bdf,stroke:#333\n    style F fill:#bdf,stroke:#333\n```\n\n---\n\n## Route Registration Flow\n\nRoutes are defined as data, not JSX trees. This decouples route config from the router version:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant R as routes.tsx<br/>getAppRoutes()\n    participant AW as AppWrapper\n    participant RW as RoutesWrapper\n    participant GR as GrafanaRouteWrapper\n\n    R->>AW: RouteDescriptor[]\n    AW->>AW: renderRoute() maps each to<br/>v6 Route element={}\n    AW->>RW: Passes Routes JSX\n    RW->>RW: Wraps in v5 Router +<br/>CompatRouter + providers\n    Note over RW: v5 Router + CompatRouter<br/>bridges the gap\n    RW-->>GR: Matched route renders<br/>GrafanaRouteWrapper\n    GR->>GR: Auth check, role check\n    GR-->>GR: Renders page component<br/>or Navigate to /login\n```\n\n---\n\n## Import Migration Pattern\n\nThe migration strategy at the component level is straightforward:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Before (v5)\"\n        A1[\"import { useHistory } from 'react-router-dom'\"]\n        A2[\"import { useParams, useLocation } from 'react-router-dom'\"]\n        A3[\"import { Switch, Route } from 'react-router-dom'\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Current (compat)\"\n        B1[\"import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat'\"]\n        B2[\"import { useParams, useLocation } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat'\"]\n        B3[\"import { Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat'\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Future (native v6)\"\n        C1[\"import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom'\"]\n        C2[\"import { useParams, useLocation } from 'react-router-dom'\"]\n        C3[\"import { Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom'\"]\n    end\n\n    A1 --> B1\n    A2 --> B2\n    A3 --> B3\n    B1 -.-> C1\n    B2 -.-> C2\n    B3 -.-> C3\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Files in the Architecture\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central route list (`getAppRoutes()`) |\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | v5 Router + CompatRouter + providers |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Maps `RouteDescriptor[]` → v6 `<Routes>` |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Per-route auth/role/error wrapper |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor` interface |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | History wrapper, shared navigation API |\n\n---\n\n## Files to Migrate Next (Limited Scope)\n\nThese are simple, self-contained pages that use `useParams` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` with minimal routing logic -- ideal for a first batch:\n\n| File | What It Does | Why It's Easy |\n|------|-------------|---------------|\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistEditPage.tsx` | Edit a playlist by UID | Single `useParams`, simple page |\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistStartPage.tsx` | Start a playlist by UID | Single `useParams`, simple page |\n| `public/app/features/invites/SignupInvited.tsx` | Signup via invite code | Single `useParams`, standalone |\n| `public/app/features/serviceaccounts/ServiceAccountPage.tsx` | View service account | Single `useParams`, standalone |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/BrowseFolderLibraryPanelsPage.tsx` | Browse library panels in a folder | Single `useParams` |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/BrowseFolderAlertingPage.tsx` | Browse alerting in a folder | Single `useParams` |\n\n**Mixed-import quick fixes** (these have wrong import sources and are trivially fixable):\n\n| File | Issue |\n|------|-------|\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/Repository/RepositoryStatusPage.tsx` | Imports `useLocation` from `react-router` instead of `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/File/FileStatusPage.tsx` | Same as above |\n| `public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/layout-tabs/TabItemRenderer.tsx` | Imports from `react-router` directly |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx` | Imports from `react-router-dom` (v5) |\n\n---\n\n## Suggested Test Scope\n\nFor a limited migration test, focus on the **playlist feature** -- it has two simple pages and a new page already not using router hooks:\n\n1. `PlaylistEditPage.tsx` -- uses `useParams`\n2. `PlaylistStartPage.tsx` -- uses `useParams`\n3. `PlaylistNewPage.tsx` -- already clean (no router hooks)\n\nVerify with:\n- Existing playlist tests (check for test files in `public/app/features/playlist/`)\n- Manual navigation: create, edit, start playlist flows\n- Confirm imports come from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (current target) consistently\n\nThe four mixed-import files above are even simpler -- just changing the import source -- and would make a good \"zero-risk\" first PR to normalize imports across the codebase.",
