{
  "conversation_id": "04299084-0538-4010-b693-81b22003e61f",
  "generation_id": "b0bc77ab-7fc9-46eb-9d94-9738cc96eefb",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "# Grafana React Router Architecture\n\n## Version and Compatibility Layer\n\nGrafana uses **React Router v5** (`react-router` 5.3.4) with the **v5-compat** bridge (`react-router-dom-v5-compat` ^6.26.1). This hybrid setup lets the codebase use v6-style APIs (`<Routes>`, `<Route>`, `useLocation`, `useParams`, `<Navigate>`) while still relying on v5's `Router` component and `history` object under the hood.\n\n---\n\n## Bootstrap Flow\n\nThe app starts in `public/app/app.ts`, where `GrafanaApp.init()` renders `AppWrapper` into the DOM. `AppWrapper` maps each `RouteDescriptor` to a `<Route>` element wrapped by `GrafanaRouteWrapper`, then hands those routes to `RoutesWrapper` which sets up the router and all context providers.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"app.ts — GrafanaApp.init()\"] --> B[\"AppWrapper\"]\n    B -->|\"maps RouteDescriptor[] → Route elements\"| C[\"RoutesWrapper\"]\n    C --> D[\"Router (v5 + history)\"]\n    D --> E[\"CompatRouter (v5-compat bridge)\"]\n    E --> F[\"LocationServiceProvider\"]\n    F --> G[\"AppChrome (shell/layout)\"]\n    G --> H[\"Routes (v6-style)\"]\n    H --> I[\"Route → GrafanaRouteWrapper → GrafanaRoute → Page Component\"]\n```\n\n**Key files:**\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/app.ts` | Entry point, calls `createRoot().render(AppWrapper)` |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Converts `RouteDescriptor[]` into `<Route>` elements |\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Sets up `Router`, `CompatRouter`, and context providers |\n\n---\n\n## Route Configuration: Centralized + Distributed\n\nRoutes are defined centrally in `getAppRoutes()` (`public/app/routes/routes.tsx`) but are **composed** from multiple feature modules. Each feature module exports its own route-building function.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph \"getAppRoutes()\"\n        A[\"getAppPluginRoutes()\"] --> Z[\"RouteDescriptor[]\"]\n        B[\"Core routes (dashboards, explore, admin...)\"] --> Z\n        C[\"getAlertingRoutes()\"] --> Z\n        D[\"getProfileRoutes()\"] --> Z\n        E[\"getPublicDashboardRoutes()\"] --> Z\n        F[\"getProvisioningRoutes()\"] --> Z\n        G[\"extraRoutes (enterprise)\"] --> Z\n        H[\"/* → PageNotFound (catch-all)\"] --> Z\n    end\n```\n\nPlugin routes are **prepended** so they can override core routes when needed. The catch-all `/*` route is always last.\n\n### The `RouteDescriptor` Type\n\nEvery route is described by the `RouteDescriptor` interface in `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface RouteDescriptor {\n  path: string;\n  component: GrafanaRouteComponent;\n  roles?: () => string[];\n  pageClass?: string;\n  routeName?: string;\n  chromeless?: boolean;       // hide app chrome (used by login, solo panels)\n  sensitive?: boolean;         // case-sensitive matching\n  allowAnonymous?: boolean | ((params) => boolean);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Route Guards and Access Control\n\nEvery route passes through `GrafanaRouteWrapper` before rendering. This component performs two checks:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Incoming Route Request\"] --> B{\"Is frontend service<br/>& route requires auth?\"}\n    B -->|\"Yes & not signed in\"| C[\"Redirect → /login\"]\n    B -->|\"No / signed in\"| D{\"Route has<br/>role requirements?\"}\n    D -->|\"Yes & user lacks role\"| E[\"Redirect → /\"]\n    D -->|\"No / user has role\"| F[\"Render GrafanaRoute\"]\n    F --> G[\"Suspense boundary\"]\n    G --> H[\"Page Component\"]\n```\n\nThe guard logic lives in `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx`. Plugin pages have an additional permission layer in `AppRootPage` that checks plugin-specific `includes` for action-based and role-based access.\n\n---\n\n## Code Splitting with `SafeDynamicImport`\n\nAlmost every route component is lazily loaded using `SafeDynamicImport`, which is a thin wrapper around React's `lazy()`:\n\n```typescript\n// public/app/core/components/DynamicImports/SafeDynamicImport.tsx\nexport const SafeDynamicImport = (loader: () => Promise<any>): GrafanaRouteComponent => lazy(loader);\n```\n\nUsage in route definitions:\n\n```typescript\n{\n  path: '/d/:uid/:slug?',\n  component: SafeDynamicImport(\n    () => import(/* webpackChunkName: \"DashboardPageProxy\" */ '../features/dashboard/containers/DashboardPageProxy')\n  ),\n}\n```\n\n`GrafanaRoute` wraps the lazy component in a `<Suspense>` with a `GrafanaRouteLoading` fallback.\n\n---\n\n## Navigation Service\n\nProgrammatic navigation goes through `locationService` from `@grafana/runtime`, not directly through React Router hooks. This provides a framework-agnostic navigation API backed by a `history` instance.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph \"Navigation APIs\"\n        A[\"locationService.push(path)\"]\n        B[\"locationService.replace(path)\"]\n        C[\"locationService.partial(query)\"]\n        D[\"locationService.getHistory()\"]\n    end\n    A --> E[\"history.push()\"]\n    B --> E2[\"history.replace()\"]\n    C --> E3[\"URL query param merge\"]\n    D --> F[\"Provided to Router component\"]\n\n    subgraph \"Link interception\"\n        G[\"interceptLinkClicks.ts\"] -->|\"captures <a> clicks\"| A\n    end\n```\n\n**Link interception** (`public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts`) is a global click handler on `<a>` tags. It intercepts internal links and routes them through `locationService.push()` instead of triggering full page loads.\n\n---\n\n## Plugin Route Integration\n\nPlugins get their own routing subtree under `/a/:pluginId/*`. The system works in two layers:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"navIndex (Redux)\"] -->|\"filter plugin items\"| B[\"getAppPluginRoutes()\"]\n    B --> C[\"Explicit routes from plugin nav items\"]\n    B --> D[\"Fallback: /a/:pluginId/* → AppRootPage\"]\n    C --> E[\"getAppRoutes() — prepended first\"]\n    D --> E\n\n    E -->|\"when matched\"| F[\"AppRootPage\"]\n    F --> G[\"Load plugin via importApp()\"]\n    G --> H[\"Render plugin.root with PluginContextProvider\"]\n    H --> I[\"Plugin manages its own sub-routing\"]\n```\n\n`AppRootPage` (`public/app/features/plugins/components/AppRootPage.tsx`) dynamically loads the plugin, wraps it in a `PluginContextProvider` and `PluginErrorBoundary`, and checks plugin-level permissions before rendering.\n\n---\n\n## Nested Routing\n\nThe top-level routing is a **flat list** of `<Route>` elements (no `<Outlet>` at the root). However, certain features implement their own nested routing internally:\n\n- **Connections** (`/connections/*`) — defines internal `<Routes>` with sub-routes for datasources, add-new, etc.\n- **Plugins** (`/a/:pluginId/*`) — each plugin manages its own sub-routing inside `AppRootPage`.\n- **Alerting** (`/alerting/*`) — has its own extensive set of sub-routes.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Top-level flat Routes\"] --> B[\"/connections/*\"]\n    A --> C[\"/a/:pluginId/*\"]\n    A --> D[\"/alerting/*\"]\n    A --> E[\"/d/:uid/:slug?\"]\n    A --> F[\"/* catch-all\"]\n\n    B --> B1[\"Connections component\"]\n    B1 --> B2[\"Internal nested Routes\"]\n    B2 --> B3[\"/connections/datasources\"]\n    B2 --> B4[\"/connections/datasources/new\"]\n    B2 --> B5[\"/connections/datasources/edit/:uid\"]\n\n    C --> C1[\"AppRootPage\"]\n    C1 --> C2[\"Plugin-managed sub-routing\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## MegaMenu and Active State\n\nThe `MegaMenu` component (`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenu.tsx`) reads the nav tree from Redux (`state.navBarTree`, which originates from `config.bootData.navTree` on the backend). It determines the active item by matching `sectionNav.node` and the current `location.pathname` using `getActiveItem()` in `utils.ts`.\n\nThe MegaMenu itself doesn't navigate — its items render `<Link>` components (from `@grafana/ui`) for internal paths and `<a>` tags for external URLs.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `public/app/app.ts` | App entry point |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Route element rendering |\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Router + provider setup |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central route registry |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor` type |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Route guard + Suspense wrapper |\n| `public/app/core/components/DynamicImports/SafeDynamicImport.tsx` | Lazy loading wrapper |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | Navigation service |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` | Global link interception |\n| `public/app/features/plugins/routes.tsx` | Plugin route registration |\n| `public/app/features/plugins/components/AppRootPage.tsx` | Plugin page container |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenu.tsx` | Navigation menu |",
