  "text": "Here's a proposed migration set. The goal is to cover every distinct routing concern in a small, self-contained batch that proves out the patterns before you touch the remaining ~120 consumer files.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Migration Set (7 files)\n\n### Tier 1 — The Core (must be done together)\n\nThese three files form the backbone. Changing one forces changes to the others.\n\n| # | File | Lines | Why it's representative |\n|---|------|-------|------------------------|\n| 1 | `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | 56 | **The bridge itself.** This is where v5 `Router` + `CompatRouter` are composed. Migrating this to a native v6 `RouterProvider` / `BrowserRouter` is the single highest-leverage change. |\n| 2 | `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | 197 | **The navigation abstraction.** Wraps the `history` package (a v5 dependency). Migrating this to use v6's `createBrowserRouter` or `useNavigate` under the hood is the hardest design decision. |\n| 3 | `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | 31 | **The route contract.** `RouteDescriptor` and `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` reference `Location` from the `history` package. Updating these types propagates the new contract to every consumer. |\n\n### Tier 2 — Guards and Rendering\n\nThese handle what happens after a route matches.\n\n| # | File | Lines | Why it's representative |\n|---|------|-------|------------------------|\n| 4 | `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | 117 | **Route guard + Suspense wrapper.** Already imports from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`. Covers auth redirects (`<Navigate>`), `useLocation`, `useParams`, lazy-loaded `<Suspense>`, and body-class side effects. A single file that exercises most v6 hook APIs. |\n| 5 | `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | 152 | **Route-to-element mapping.** Converts `RouteDescriptor[]` into `<Route element={...}>` elements. Already uses v6-style `<Routes>` and `<Route>`. Main change: drop the `react-router-dom-v5-compat` import in favor of `react-router-dom` v6. |\n\n### Tier 3 — Consumers (prove the patterns work end-to-end)\n\nThese are small, self-contained files that use routing hooks — good canaries.\n\n| # | File | Lines | Why it's representative |\n|---|------|-------|------------------------|\n| 6 | `public/app/core/navigation/hooks.ts` | 19 | **Custom hook consumer.** Uses `useLocation` from v5-compat and delegates to `locationService.partial()`. Tiny file, tests that the new navigation abstraction works from a hook. |\n| 7 | `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` | 57 | **Non-React consumer.** A vanilla DOM event handler that calls `locationService.push()`. Proves the navigation service works outside of React component trees. |\n\n---\n\n## What this set covers\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph \"Tier 1 — Core\"\n        A[\"RoutesWrapper.tsx<br/><i>Router bootstrap</i>\"]\n        B[\"LocationService.tsx<br/><i>Navigation abstraction</i>\"]\n        C[\"types.ts<br/><i>Route contract / types</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Tier 2 — Guards & Rendering\"\n        D[\"GrafanaRoute.tsx<br/><i>Auth guard + Suspense</i>\"]\n        E[\"AppWrapper.tsx<br/><i>Route ↔ element mapping</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Tier 3 — Consumers\"\n        F[\"hooks.ts<br/><i>React hook consumer</i>\"]\n        G[\"interceptLinkClicks.ts<br/><i>Non-React consumer</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    A --> D\n    A --> E\n    B --> F\n    B --> G\n    C --> D\n    C --> E\n    E --> A\n```\n\n## Key migration decisions these files force you to make\n\n1. **`RoutesWrapper.tsx`** — Do you use `createBrowserRouter` + `RouterProvider` (data router pattern with loaders/actions), or `BrowserRouter` (drop-in upgrade)? The answer shapes everything else.\n\n2. **`LocationService.tsx`** — The `history` package is a v5 artifact. In v6, navigation is router-internal. You need to decide: does `locationService` become a thin wrapper around `router.navigate()`, or do you preserve the `history` instance for backward compatibility during the migration? (~120 files import from `@grafana/runtime`'s `locationService`.)\n\n3. **`types.ts`** — `Location` currently comes from the `history` package. In v6, it's `react-router-dom`'s own `Location` type (no `state` generic, slightly different shape). This change ripples into every `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` consumer.\n\n4. **`GrafanaRoute.tsx`** — The imports change from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` to `react-router-dom`. The hooks (`useLocation`, `useParams`, `Navigate`) have the same API in v6, so this validates that the guard logic survives the swap.\n\n## What you can defer\n\n- **`routes.tsx`** (574 lines) — Already uses v6-style `<Routes>`/`<Route>`. Only the import path changes (`v5-compat` → `react-router-dom`). Mechanical, not architectural.\n- **`SafeDynamicImport.tsx`** (5 lines) — Pure `React.lazy()` wrapper, no router dependency at all.\n- **Feature-level consumers** (~120 files) — Once the core 7 files compile and work, these are a bulk find-and-replace of import paths from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` to `react-router-dom`, plus updating any `Location` type references.\n- **`MegaMenu.tsx`** — Uses `useLocation` from v5-compat but doesn't navigate. Trivial import swap after the core is done.",
