  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "## Grafana Frontend Security Vulnerability Report\n\nFour parallel agents explored the codebase across XSS, injection, auth/data exposure, and CSRF/clickjacking/dependencies. Here is a consolidated summary, deduplicated and organized by severity.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings\n\n**1. XSS via unsanitized trace data in `KeyValuesTable.tsx`**\n\n`public/app/features/explore/TraceView/components/TraceTimelineViewer/SpanDetail/KeyValuesTable.tsx` (lines 131-136) interpolates `row.value` directly into HTML via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for `code` and `text` types without any escaping. Trace span data (tags, logs, stack traces) can be attacker-controlled.\n\n```\n__html: `<pre style=\"...\">${row.value}</pre>`\n__html: `<span style=\"...\">${row.value}</span>`\n```\n\n**2. Open redirect via unvalidated `redirectTo`**\n\n`public/app/app.ts` (lines 357-384) reads `redirectTo` from query params and stores it in `sessionStorage` without validation. Combined with `stripBaseFromUrl` in `packages/grafana-data/src/utils/location.ts` (line 32-34) which passes through external URLs unchanged, an attacker can craft `?redirectTo=https://evil.com` and redirect users post-login.\n\n**3. Arbitrary code execution via scripted dashboards**\n\n`public/app/features/dashboard/services/DashboardLoaderSrv.ts` (lines 75-87) uses `new Function()` to execute JavaScript loaded from `public/dashboards/{slug}`. If an attacker can place a file there, full code execution is achieved.\n\n---\n\n### High Findings\n\n**4. Auth token exposed in WebSocket URL**\n\n`public/app/features/live/centrifuge/service.ts` (line 85) appends `?auth_token=<token>` to the WebSocket URL, exposing it in browser history, server logs, and referrer headers.\n\n**5. Plugin readme rendered without sanitization**\n\n`public/app/features/plugins/admin/components/PluginDetailsBody.tsx` (lines 57-59) renders remote plugin `readme` via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization. A malicious plugin catalog entry could inject arbitrary HTML/JS.\n\n**6. `EmptyListCTA` accepts unsanitized HTML**\n\n`public/app/core/components/EmptyListCTA/EmptyListCTA.tsx` (line 64) renders `infoBox` via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without enforcing sanitization.\n\n**7. ReDoS in Loki query builder**\n\n`public/app/plugins/datasource/loki/querybuilder/components/LokiQueryBuilder.tsx` (lines 60, 86) constructs `new RegExp(filter.value)` from user input. Malicious patterns like `(a+)+$` can cause catastrophic backtracking.\n\n**8. Third-party script loading without SRI or allowlist**\n\n`public/app/core/services/echo/utils.ts` (lines 3-10) `loadScript(url)` loads any URL as a script with no Subresource Integrity check or URL validation.\n\n**9. `jsonMarkup` allows `javascript:` URLs**\n\n`KeyValuesTable.tsx` (line 140) uses `jsonMarkup` which constructs `<a href=\"...\">` links using `encodeURI`, which does not block `javascript:` or `data:` scheme URLs.\n\n**10. `disableSanitizeHtml` global toggle**\n\n`packages/grafana-runtime/src/config.ts` (line 136) provides a global config option `disableSanitizeHtml` that, when enabled, bypasses URL and HTML sanitization across markdown rendering, link services, and DashList. Misconfiguration opens broad XSS.\n\n**11. Testdata datasource arbitrary API path**\n\n`public/app/plugins/datasource/grafana-testdata-datasource/datasource.ts` (line 463) builds `/api/${target.stringInput}` from user-controlled input without encoding or path validation, enabling SSRF-like access to arbitrary `/api/*` paths.\n\n---\n\n### Medium Findings\n\n| # | Vulnerability | Location |\n|---|---|---|\n| 12 | `new Function()` with dashboard config in scatter chart | `public/app/plugins/panel/xychart/scatter.ts:672` |\n| 13 | Unencoded query params in admin API calls | `public/app/features/admin/state/actions.ts:295,362` |\n| 14 | Unencoded query params in UserPicker, TeamPicker, ServiceAccountPicker | `public/app/core/components/Select/UserPicker.tsx:31`, `TeamPicker.tsx:48`, `ServiceAccountPicker.tsx:31` |\n| 15 | GenAI content rendered via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` | `GenAISuggestionsDrawer.tsx:114`, `GenAIExplanationDrawer.tsx:24` |\n| 16 | Embed iframes lack `sandbox` attribute | `public/app/features/dashboard/components/ShareModal/utils.ts:163` |\n| 17 | Azure credentials error may leak details | `public/app/plugins/datasource/azuremonitor/credentials.ts:60` |\n| 18 | WebSocket downgrades to `ws://` on HTTP | `public/app/features/live/centrifuge/service.ts:81` |\n| 19 | Debug logging of full frame data | `RawFrameEditor.tsx:38-39` |\n| 20 | ReDoS via `new RegExp('^' + prefix)` in nodeGraph | `public/app/plugins/panel/nodeGraph/utils.ts:130` |\n| 21 | Client-side-only file type validation on uploads | `DashboardImportPage.tsx`, `ImportToGMARules.tsx` |\n| 22 | File delete path may allow traversal | `public/app/features/dimensions/editors/FileUploader.tsx:48-50` |\n\n---\n\n### Low Findings\n\n| # | Vulnerability | Location |\n|---|---|---|\n| 23 | `postMessage` with `targetOrigin: '*'` | `public/app/app.ts:138` |\n| 24 | Prism.js output via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` | Tempo/Azure `RawQuery.tsx` |\n| 25 | Plugin sandbox intercepts DOM mutations (mitigated) | `public/app/features/plugins/sandbox/distortions.ts` |\n| 26 | Various `console.log` with potentially sensitive data | `LivePublish.tsx`, `LegacyVariableWrapper.ts`, etc. |\n| 27 | Analytics API key from config exposed to client | `public/app/core/services/echo/init.ts:104` |\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Priority Actions\n\n1. **KeyValuesTable** -- Escape `row.value` with `textUtil.sanitize()` or `textUtil.escapeHtml()` before HTML interpolation. Block `javascript:` URLs in `jsonMarkup`.\n2. **Open redirect** -- Validate `redirectTo` in the frontend (allow only relative paths or same-origin) before storing in `sessionStorage`, matching backend `ValidateRedirectTo` logic.\n3. **Scripted dashboards** -- Deprecate or sandbox `new Function()` in `DashboardLoaderSrv`. Consider removing this legacy feature.\n4. **Plugin readme** -- Run remote readme through `renderMarkdown` or `textUtil.sanitize` before rendering.\n5. **Auth token in URL** -- Migrate WebSocket auth to headers or short-lived tokens.\n6. **ReDoS** -- Validate/limit regex patterns from user input in Loki builder; use a timeout wrapper or static pattern validation.\n7. **loadScript** -- Add URL allowlist and SRI support to `echo/utils.ts`.\n8. **URL encoding** -- Use `encodeURIComponent()` for all user-controlled query parameters in API calls.\n\nThis audit focused on static analysis of frontend source code. A dynamic penetration test would complement these findings, especially for CSRF token validation, CSP enforcement, and backend-side protections.",
