  "text": "\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\nCategory groupings were added to the Bookmarks page with automatic categorization, filtering, and grouped display.\n\n### 1. **Automatic categorization**\n\nThree categories:\n\n- **Operations** – Alerting, Explore, Connections, Data sources, monitoring apps (OnCall, SLO, k6, Kubernetes, etc.)\n- **Admin** – Administration, Users, Teams, Plugins, Org settings, server settings\n- **Content** – Dashboards, Create, Starred, Playlists, Library panels, Reports\n\nCategorization uses:\n\n1. Direct match on nav item `id` against predefined sets\n2. ID prefix matching (`alert*`, `connections*`, `plugin-page-grafana*` for operations; `cfg*`, `admin*` for admin; `dashboards*`, `create*` for content)\n3. URL prefix fallback (`/explore`, `/alerting`, `/connections`, etc.)\n4. Default: **Content** if nothing matches\n\n### 2. **Filter bar**\n\n`FilterPill` components (same pattern as `TraceFilterPills`) show:\n\n- Operations (count)\n- Admin (count)\n- Content (count)\n\nBehavior:\n\n- No selection: show all bookmarks\n- One or more selected: show only those categories\n\n### 3. **Grouped rendering**\n\nBookmarks are rendered in labeled sections:\n\n- Section headings per category\n- Same grid layout per section\n- Card styling via `NavLandingPageCard`:\n  - Operations → primary (blue)\n  - Admin → warning (amber)\n  - Content → success (green)\n\n### Components used\n\n- `FilterPill` – filtering (like `TraceFilterPills`)\n- `Stack` – layout\n- `NavLandingPageCard` – existing bookmark cards with optional `category` styling\n- `EmptyState` – empty state unchanged",
