  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what was added to `BookmarksPage.tsx`:\n\n**Category auto-assignment** -- Each bookmarked item is automatically assigned a category by tracing its URL back to the top-level nav section it belongs to:\n\n| Category | Nav sections |\n|---|---|\n| **Content** | `home`, `dashboards`, `starred` |\n| **Operations** | `alerting`, `explore`, `connections`, `data-connections`, `infrastructure` |\n| **Admin** | `admin`, `cfg` (configuration) |\n| **Other** | Anything not mapped above |\n\n**Filtering** -- A `RadioButtonGroup` at the top lets users filter by category. Each option shows the count of bookmarks in that category (e.g., \"Content (3)\"). Only categories with bookmarks appear as filter options.\n\n**Grouping** -- Bookmarks are grouped by category with section headers using `Text` variant `h5` and a `Badge` showing the item count. Groups render in a fixed order: Content, Operations, Admin, Other.\n\n**Visual differentiation** -- Each category gets a distinct card border/background color using the existing `NavLandingPageCard` `category` prop:\n- Content = `primary` (blue)\n- Operations = `warning` (amber)\n- Admin = `error` (red)\n- Other = `secondary` (gray)\n\nAll components used (`RadioButtonGroup`, `Badge`, `Text`, `Stack`) are existing `@grafana/ui` exports, and the i18n `t()` function is used for all user-facing strings.",
