  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Now I have a comprehensive picture. Here's the full overview:\n\n---\n\n# Grafana Codebase: React Router Architecture & v5 → v6 Migration\n\n## Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large TypeScript + Go monorepo. The frontend lives primarily under `public/app/` with shared packages in `packages/` (e.g., `@grafana/ui`, `@grafana/runtime`, `@grafana/data`). The routing system is central to how the single-page application renders different features like dashboards, alerting, explore, plugins, and admin pages.\n\n---\n\n## Routing Architecture\n\nThe routing stack has four key layers:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"app.ts — GrafanaApp.init()\"] --> B[\"AppWrapper.tsx\"]\n    B --> C[\"RoutesWrapper.tsx — RouterWrapper\"]\n    C --> D[\"react-router-dom v5 Router\\n(history from LocationService)\"]\n    D --> E[\"CompatRouter\\n(react-router-dom-v5-compat)\"]\n    E --> F[\"AppChrome — Shell/Nav/Breadcrumbs\"]\n    F --> G[\"routes.tsx — Routes + Route elements\"]\n    G --> H[\"GrafanaRoute.tsx — Suspense + ErrorBoundary + Guards\"]\n    H --> I[\"SafeDynamicImport — React.lazy() per page\"]\n\n    style D fill:#f9d,stroke:#333\n    style E fill:#ff9,stroke:#333\n    style G fill:#9df,stroke:#333\n```\n\n### Key Files\n\n| Layer | File | Role |\n|-------|------|------|\n| Entry | `public/app/app.ts` | Bootstraps app, renders `AppWrapper` |\n| Wrapper | `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Calls `getAppRoutes()`, renders inside `<Routes>` |\n| Router | `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | v5 `<Router>` + `<CompatRouter>` bridge |\n| Route defs | `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central `getAppRoutes()` returning `RouteDescriptor[]` |\n| Route types | `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor`, `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` |\n| Route guard | `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Auth/role checks, `Suspense`, error boundary |\n| Lazy loading | `public/app/core/components/DynamicImports/SafeDynamicImport.tsx` | `React.lazy()` wrapper |\n| Navigation state | `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/AppChromeService.tsx` | Manages nav model, breadcrumbs |\n| LocationService | `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | Wraps `history` v4 for programmatic nav |\n\n### Route Organization\n\nRoutes are **hybrid centralized + feature-modular**. The main `routes.tsx` imports sub-route arrays:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    R[\"routes.tsx<br/>getAppRoutes()\"] --> A[\"alerting/routes.tsx\"]\n    R --> P[\"profile/routes.tsx\"]\n    R --> C[\"connections/routes.tsx\"]\n    R --> PL[\"plugins/routes.tsx\"]\n    R --> PA[\"plugins/admin/routes.tsx\"]\n    R --> D[\"dashboard/routes.ts\"]\n    R --> PR[\"provisioning/utils/routes.ts\"]\n    R --> INLINE[\"~50 inline RouteDescriptors\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## v5 → v6 Migration Status\n\n### Package Versions\n\n| Package | Version | Role |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `react-router` | **5.3.4** | v5 core (still the root) |\n| `react-router-dom` | **5.3.4** | v5 DOM bindings (root `<Router>`) |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | **^6.26.1** (resolves to 6.30.3) | v6 API bridge |\n\nThe strategy is **incremental migration via the compat layer**: the root `<Router>` is still v5, but `<CompatRouter>` wraps the tree so that v6 hooks (`useNavigate`, `useParams`, `useLocation`, `useSearchParams`) work everywhere.\n\n### Migration Progress\n\n```mermaid\npie title React Router Import Sources (~140 files total)\n    \"v6 via compat layer\" : 130\n    \"v5 direct (react-router / react-router-dom)\" : 9\n```\n\n### Files Still on v5 Imports\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"Infrastructure — v5 Router (intentional, migrate last)\"\n        RW[\"RoutesWrapper.tsx<br/>Router from react-router-dom\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Test Utilities — v5 Router for test harness\"\n        TU[\"test/test-utils.tsx<br/>Router from react-router-dom\"]\n        TP[\"test/helpers/TestProvider.tsx<br/>Router from react-router-dom\"]\n        ES[\"explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx<br/>Route, Router from react-router-dom\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Straggler Imports — easy wins\"\n        AN[\"AppNotificationList.tsx<br/>useLocation from react-router-dom\"]\n        RS[\"RepositoryStatusPage.tsx<br/>useLocation from react-router\"]\n        FS[\"FileStatusPage.tsx<br/>useLocation from react-router\"]\n        TI[\"TabItemRenderer.tsx<br/>useLocation from react-router\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"E2E Plugin — standalone v6 (not a migration target)\"\n        EP[\"grafana-extensionstest-app<br/>Route, Routes from react-router-dom v6\"]\n    end\n\n    style RW fill:#f9d,stroke:#333\n    style TU fill:#ff9,stroke:#333\n    style TP fill:#ff9,stroke:#333\n    style ES fill:#ff9,stroke:#333\n    style AN fill:#9f9,stroke:#333\n    style RS fill:#9f9,stroke:#333\n    style FS fill:#9f9,stroke:#333\n    style TI fill:#9f9,stroke:#333\n    style EP fill:#ddd,stroke:#999\n```\n\n**Legend:** Pink = root infrastructure (complex), Yellow = test harness (moderate), Green = straggler imports (easy), Grey = not a migration target.\n\n### What's Already Migrated\n\n- **~130 files** import from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` and use v6 APIs\n- `<Routes>` / `<Route element={...}>` are the standard pattern in `AppWrapper`, `Connections`, alerting routes, etc.\n- `<Navigate>` replaces `<Redirect>` everywhere\n- `useNavigate`, `useParams`, `useSearchParams` used across provisioning, plugins, connections, alerting, dashboards\n- `GrafanaRouteComponentProps` already uses `Params` from the compat package\n\n### What Still Needs Migration\n\n1. **Root router** (`RoutesWrapper.tsx`): Still uses v5 `<Router>` + `<CompatRouter>`. Final migration means switching to v6 `<BrowserRouter>` or `createBrowserRouter` and removing the compat shim entirely.\n2. **`LocationService`**: Built on `history` v4, which v5 consumes. v6 internalizes its own history. This is the hardest piece.\n3. **4 straggler component files**: Import `useLocation` from `react-router` or `react-router-dom` instead of the compat layer.\n4. **3 test utility files**: Use v5 `Router` directly for test harnesses.\n5. **~20 files using `GrafanaRouteComponentProps`**: This pattern works but is v5-flavored. Eventual migration would have page components use `useParams`/`useLocation` directly.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Next Steps: Small-Scale Test Migration\n\nThe safest starting point is the **4 straggler files** that import from `react-router` or `react-router-dom` (not compat) in production code. These are pure import swaps with zero architectural risk:\n\n### Tier 1: Trivial Import Swaps (start here)\n\nThese files just need their import source changed from `react-router` / `react-router-dom` to `react-router-dom-v5-compat`:\n\n| File | Current Import | Change |\n|------|---------------|--------|\n| `public/app/core/components/AppNotifications/AppNotificationList.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router-dom` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/Repository/RepositoryStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `public/app/features/provisioning/File/FileStatusPage.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n| `public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/layout-tabs/TabItemRenderer.tsx` | `useLocation` from `react-router` | Change to `react-router-dom-v5-compat` |\n\n### Tier 2: Test Utility Updates (after Tier 1)\n\nThese require updating how test harnesses create routers, but are low-risk since they only affect tests:\n\n| File | Current Import | Change |\n|------|---------------|--------|\n| `public/test/test-utils.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` | Switch to `MemoryRouter` from compat |\n| `public/test/helpers/TestProvider.tsx` | `Router` from `react-router-dom` | Switch to `MemoryRouter` from compat |\n| `public/app/features/explore/spec/helper/setup.tsx` | `Route, Router` from `react-router-dom` | Switch to compat equivalents |\n\n### Tier 3: Larger Architectural Work (future)\n\n- Remove `CompatRouter` and switch `RoutesWrapper.tsx` to a native v6 router\n- Migrate `LocationService` away from `history` v4\n- Convert `GrafanaRouteComponentProps`-based pages to use hooks directly\n\n---\n\nThe Tier 1 files are the ideal \"small-scale test\" -- each is a single-line import change, they're in different feature areas (core, provisioning, dashboard-scene), and they validate that the compat layer works identically for `useLocation` regardless of import source. If those go smoothly, Tier 2 test utilities are the natural follow-up.",
