  "model": "gpt-5.3-codex",
  "text": "Here’s a concise summary of the official Cursor Cloud Agent docs:\n\n- **What Cloud Agents are:** Remote agents that run in isolated cloud VMs (not your laptop), using the same core agent behavior as local agents.\n- **Why use them:** You can run multiple agents in parallel, keep work running when your machine is offline, and have agents build/test/run the app in their own environment.\n- **Where you can trigger them:** Cursor Desktop/Web (`cursor.com/agents`), GitHub/GitLab comments (`@cursor`), Slack, Linear, and the API.\n- **How they work with code:** They clone your repo, work on a separate branch, and push changes back for handoff/PR flow; you need repo read/write access.\n- **Model + pricing behavior:** Cloud Agents always run in **Max Mode** and are billed at API pricing. On-demand usage must be enabled.\n- **Setup model:** Environment runs on Ubuntu and is configured via either:\n  - Agent-guided onboarding (`cursor.com/onboard`, recommended), or\n  - Dockerfile + `.cursor/environment.json` (advanced).\n- **Environment lifecycle:** Cursor applies environment config by priority (team → personal → repo), runs an idempotent update/install command, and caches checkpoints for faster future startup.\n- **Capabilities:** Desktop/browser computer-use, generated artifacts (screenshots/videos/log refs), CI auto-fix for agent-created PRs (GitHub Actions), and MCP integration for normal Cloud Agent usage.\n- **Important MCP nuance:** Docs say Cloud Agents support MCP servers, but the **Cloud Agents API page** explicitly says MCP is **not yet supported via the API**.\n- **Secrets/security basics:** Secrets are managed in dashboard settings, encrypted at rest, can be redacted, and are recommended over embedding secrets in files/snapshots.\n\nIf you want, I can also give you a **“getting started in 10 minutes” checklist** tailored to your Grafana repo (including a sample `.cursor/environment.json` and update/start commands).",
