{
  "conversation_id": "df1d9d94-af20-41ce-abad-cd80d6f8d8b1",
  "generation_id": "2b3b254a-b18d-4e69-852b-f7bf18052013",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "## Grafana React Router Architecture\n\n### Overview\n\nGrafana uses **React Router v6** (with a v5 compatibility layer via `react-router-dom-v5-compat`) and a centralized **route registry** pattern. Routes are defined as flat `RouteDescriptor[]` arrays, lazily loaded via `SafeDynamicImport`, and wrapped in auth/role guards before rendering.\n\n### Key Layers\n\n1. **Entry point** (`public/app/app.ts`) — bootstraps the app and renders `AppWrapper` into the DOM.\n\n2. **`AppWrapper`** (`public/app/AppWrapper.tsx`) — calls `getAppRoutes()` and maps each `RouteDescriptor` to a React Router `<Route>`, wrapping each in `<GrafanaRouteWrapper>`.\n\n3. **`RouterWrapper`** (`public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx`) — provides `<Router>` using `locationService.getHistory()`, plus `<CompatRouter>` for v5 compat and `<LocationServiceProvider>` for context.\n\n4. **`getAppRoutes()`** (`public/app/routes/routes.tsx`) — the central route registry. Combines:\n   - **Plugin routes** (first, so plugins can override core routes)\n   - **Core routes** (dashboards, explore, admin, login, etc.)\n   - **Feature routes** from modules like alerting, connections, profile, provisioning\n   - **`extraRoutes`** (enterprise extensions)\n   - A catch-all `/*` for 404\n\n5. **`GrafanaRouteWrapper`** (`public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx`) — handles auth checks (`allowAnonymous`, role-based redirects) then delegates to `GrafanaRoute`.\n\n6. **`GrafanaRoute`** — sets up keybindings, updates body classes, renders the route component inside `<Suspense>` + `<ErrorBoundary>`.\n\n7. **`locationService`** (`packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx`) — a singleton wrapping `history` from the `history` library. Provides `push`, `replace`, `partial`, and an observable for location changes. Link clicks are intercepted at the document level (`interceptLinkClicks.ts`) to route through `locationService` instead of full page reloads.\n\n8. **`NavModel` / `navIndex`** — server-provided `navTree` (sidebar items, breadcrumbs) is built into a Redux `navIndex`. Components use `useNavModel(id)` to resolve page navigation context, breadcrumbs, and tabs.\n\n### Mermaid Diagram\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"app.ts — GrafanaApp.init()\"] --> B[\"AppWrapper\"]\n    B --> C[\"RouterWrapper<br/>(Router + CompatRouter + LocationServiceProvider)\"]\n    C --> D[\"AppChrome<br/>(sidebar, top nav, breadcrumbs)\"]\n    D --> E[\"&lt;Routes&gt;\"]\n\n    E --> F[\"getAppRoutes()\"]\n    F --> F1[\"Plugin Routes<br/>(getAppPluginRoutes)\"]\n    F --> F2[\"Core Routes<br/>(dashboards, explore, admin…)\"]\n    F --> F3[\"Feature Routes<br/>(alerting, connections, profile…)\"]\n    F --> F4[\"extraRoutes<br/>(enterprise extensions)\"]\n    F --> F5[\"Catch-all 404\"]\n\n    E --> G[\"&lt;Route&gt; per RouteDescriptor\"]\n    G --> H[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/>(auth + role checks)\"]\n    H --> I[\"GrafanaRoute<br/>(keybindings, body class, cleanup)\"]\n    I --> J[\"Suspense + ErrorBoundary\"]\n    J --> K[\"route.component<br/>(lazy-loaded via SafeDynamicImport)\"]\n\n    L[\"locationService<br/>(HistoryWrapper)\"] -.->|\"provides history\"| C\n    M[\"interceptLinkClicks\"] -.->|\"push(href)\"| L\n    N[\"navIndex<br/>(Redux, from server navTree)\"] -.->|\"useNavModel()\"| D\n\n    style A fill:#2a4,color:#fff\n    style F fill:#36a,color:#fff\n    style L fill:#a63,color:#fff\n    style N fill:#a63,color:#fff\n```\n\n### How It Fits Together\n\n| Concept | Key File |\n|---|---|\n| Router setup | `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` |\n| Route registry | `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` |\n| Route type | `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` |\n| Auth/role guard | `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` |\n| Lazy loading | `public/app/core/components/DynamicImports/SafeDynamicImport.tsx` |\n| Navigation service | `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` |\n| Link interception | `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` |\n| Nav model (sidebar/breadcrumbs) | `public/app/core/reducers/navModel.ts` |\n\n### Route Registration Pattern\n\nEach feature module exports a `get*Routes()` function returning `RouteDescriptor[]`. Components are wrapped in `SafeDynamicImport` (which is just `React.lazy`) for code splitting:\n\n```typescript\nexport function getProfileRoutes(): RouteDescriptor[] {\n  return [\n    {\n      path: '/profile',\n      component: SafeDynamicImport(\n        () => import(/* webpackChunkName: \"UserProfileEditPage\" */ './UserProfileEditPage')\n      ),\n    },\n  ];\n}\n```\n\nThese are then spread into the flat array returned by `getAppRoutes()`. Some features (like Connections and Alerting) use a single catch-all route (`/connections/*`) and handle sub-routing internally with their own nested `<Routes>`.",
