  "text": "Skill created at `~/.cursor/skills/mermaid-diagrams/SKILL.md`. Here's what it captures:\n\n**Core idea:** Diagrams should clarify, not impress. Ruthless simplification over comprehensive coverage.\n\n**Key rules distilled from the earlier diagram:**\n- Max 12-15 nodes — if you need more, split or collapse\n- Dotted lines (`-.->`) for secondary relationships (like `locationService` and `navIndex` were in the earlier diagram)\n- Color only to distinguish categories (entry point vs. external system), not to decorate\n- `<br/>` inside node labels for brief role descriptions instead of spawning extra nodes\n- One idea per diagram — don't mix concerns\n\n**Includes guidance on:** choosing diagram types, architecture overviews, decision flows, sequence diagrams, and a clear anti-patterns table.\n\nIt weighs in at ~100 lines — well under the 500-line target — so it won't bloat context when triggered.",
