{
  "conversation_id": "faa30379-f739-4352-b571-4082b39d445d",
  "generation_id": "27761f8c-4457-4e85-aca6-e2f20ea71d52",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the Grafana frontend testing infrastructure.\n\n---\n\n## Grafana Frontend Test Frameworks Overview\n\nGrafana uses a **multi-layered testing strategy** spanning unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, accessibility checks, Storybook visual tests, and performance benchmarks.\n\n### Architecture Diagram\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Grafana Frontend Testing Stack\"\n        direction TB\n\n        A[\"Test Runner Layer\"] --> B[\"Unit & Integration<br/><b>Jest 29.7</b> + ts-jest\"]\n        A --> C[\"E2E (Primary)<br/><b>Playwright 1.56</b>\"]\n        A --> D[\"E2E (Legacy)<br/><b>Cypress 14.3</b>\"]\n        A --> E[\"Storybook Tests<br/><b>@storybook/test-runner</b>\"]\n        A --> F[\"Accessibility<br/><b>pa11y-ci</b>\"]\n\n        B --> G[\"@testing-library/react 16.3<br/>@testing-library/user-event 14.6<br/>@testing-library/jest-dom 6.6\"]\n        B --> H[\"Mock Service Worker (MSW) 2.10<br/>API Mocking\"]\n        B --> I[\"Custom Utilities<br/>customRender, reduxTester,<br/>reducerTester, thunkTester\"]\n\n        C --> J[\"@grafana/plugin-e2e<br/>Plugin testing helpers\"]\n        C --> K[\"@grafana/e2e-selectors<br/>Shared selectors\"]\n\n        D --> K\n        D --> L[\"Benchmark Plugin<br/>CDP + tracelib\"]\n\n        E --> M[\"Playwright Storybook Config<br/>Visual verification\"]\n    end\n\n    style A fill:#4a90d9,color:#fff\n    style B fill:#c44569,color:#fff\n    style C fill:#3dc1d3,color:#fff\n    style D fill:#e77f67,color:#fff\n    style E fill:#786fa6,color:#fff\n    style F fill:#f8a5c2,color:#333\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. Unit & Integration Tests (Jest)\n\n**Jest 29.7** is the primary test runner for all unit and integration tests. Tests live **co-located with source files** using the `*.test.ts(x)` naming convention.\n\n**Key configuration** (`jest.config.js`):\n- Environment: `jsdom` (browser-like)\n- Timezone forced to `Pacific/Easter` to catch timezone bugs\n- Test timeout: 30 seconds\n- Roots: `public/app`, `public/test`, `packages`, `scripts/tests`\n- `jest-fail-on-console` enabled in CI to catch noisy logs\n\n**Core Libraries:**\n\n| Library | Version | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| `@testing-library/react` | 16.3.0 | Component rendering & queries |\n| `@testing-library/user-event` | 14.6.1 | Realistic user interaction simulation |\n| `@testing-library/jest-dom` | 6.6.4 | Custom DOM matchers (`toBeInTheDocument`, etc.) |\n| `ts-jest` | 29.4.0 | TypeScript transpilation |\n| `MSW` | 2.10.4 | HTTP request interception & mocking |\n| `jest-fail-on-console` | - | Fails tests on unexpected console output |\n| `fishery` / `chance` | - | Test data factories |\n\n**Custom test utilities** in `public/test/`:\n\n- **`customRender`** — wraps components in Redux Provider, GrafanaContext, Router, LocationServiceProvider, and ModalsContextProvider, mirroring the real app hierarchy\n- **`testWithFeatureToggles`** — enables/disables feature flags per test\n- **`testWithLicenseFeatures`** — mocks license features per test\n- **`reduxTester`** / **`reducerTester`** / **`thunkTester`** — utilities for testing Redux logic\n- **`@grafana/test-utils`** — shared package with MSW handlers, RxJS matchers (`toEmitValues`, `toEmitValuesWith`), and fixtures\n\n**Decoupled plugin testing:** 12+ datasource plugins (Elasticsearch, Loki, Tempo, etc.) have their own `jest.config.js` and are excluded from the root Jest run — they are tested independently via Nx:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Jest Test Execution\"\n        ROOT[\"Root jest.config.js\"] -->|excludes| PLUGINS[\"Decoupled Plugin Configs\"]\n        ROOT -->|runs| APP[\"public/app/**/*.test.ts(x)\"]\n        ROOT -->|runs| PKG[\"packages/**/*.test.ts(x)\"]\n        ROOT -->|runs| SCRIPTS[\"scripts/tests/**\"]\n\n        PLUGINS -->|independent| LOKI[\"loki/jest.config.js\"]\n        PLUGINS -->|independent| TEMPO[\"tempo/jest.config.js\"]\n        PLUGINS -->|independent| ES[\"elasticsearch/jest.config.js\"]\n        PLUGINS -->|independent| PROM[\"grafana-prometheus/jest.config.js\"]\n        PLUGINS -->|independent| MORE[\"... 8 more plugins\"]\n    end\n\n    NX[\"nx run-many\"] -->|orchestrates| PLUGINS\n    NX -->|\"plugin:test:ci\"| PLUGINS\n\n    style ROOT fill:#c44569,color:#fff\n    style NX fill:#4a90d9,color:#fff\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. End-to-End Tests (Playwright — Primary)\n\n**Playwright 1.56** is the primary E2E framework with a project-based architecture that handles authentication, role-based testing, and suite isolation.\n\n**Key configuration** (`playwright.config.ts`):\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:3001`\n- Fully parallel execution (single worker in CI)\n- Retries: 2 in CI, 0 locally\n- Traces retained on failure, screenshots on failure only\n\n**Project structure:**\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Playwright Project Dependencies\"\n        AUTH[\"authenticate<br/>(admin login)\"] --> ADMIN[\"admin suite\"]\n        AUTH --> DASH[\"dashboards suite\"]\n        AUTH --> PANELS[\"panels suite\"]\n        AUTH --> SMOKE[\"smoke tests\"]\n        AUTH --> ALERT[\"alerting suite\"]\n        AUTH --> VARIOUS[\"various suite\"]\n        AUTH --> PERF[\"performance tests\"]\n\n        VIEWER_AUTH[\"createUserAndAuthenticate<br/>(viewer login)\"] --> VIEWER[\"viewer suite\"]\n\n        CLOUD[\"cloud-plugins suite\"]\n        STORYBOOK[\"storybook verification\"]\n        PLUGIN[\"plugin-e2e suite\"]\n    end\n\n    style AUTH fill:#3dc1d3,color:#fff\n    style VIEWER_AUTH fill:#3dc1d3,color:#fff\n```\n\n**Test directory layout:**\n\n```\ne2e-playwright/\n├── smoke-tests-suite/          # Critical path tests\n├── dashboards-suite/           # Dashboard CRUD, navigation\n├── panels-suite/               # Panel rendering, editing\n├── alerting-suite/             # Alerting rules and notifications\n├── various-suite/              # Miscellaneous + perf tests\n├── dashboard-cujs/             # Critical user journeys\n├── dashboard-new-layouts/      # New layout system tests\n├── storybook/                  # Storybook visual verification\n├── plugin-e2e/                 # Plugin-specific E2E\n├── test-plugins/               # Test plugin scenarios\n└── unauthenticated/            # Unauthenticated flows\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. End-to-End Tests (Cypress — Legacy)\n\n**Cypress 14.3** remains for legacy E2E tests and benchmarking. It is gradually being replaced by Playwright.\n\n```\ne2e/\n├── old-arch/                   # Old dashboard architecture tests\n├── dashboards-search-suite/    # Dashboard search tests\n├── benchmarks/                 # Live dashboard perf benchmarks\n├── cypress/\n│   ├── support/e2e.js\n│   ├── plugins/\n│   │   ├── benchmark/          # CDP-based performance profiling\n│   │   ├── readProvisions/\n│   │   └── typescriptPreprocessor/\n│   └── fixtures/\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Storybook Testing\n\nTests Storybook stories via two mechanisms:\n\n1. **`@storybook/test-runner`** — runs Storybook interaction tests (`yarn test:storybook`)\n2. **Playwright Storybook config** (`playwright.storybook.config.ts`) — loads stories in a real browser and verifies rendering (`yarn e2e:playwright:storybook`)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Accessibility Testing\n\n**pa11y-ci** runs automated accessibility audits against running Grafana pages, configured in `e2e/pa11yci.conf.js`. Run via `yarn test:accessibility-report`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Performance / Benchmarking\n\n- **Cypress benchmark plugin** — uses Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) via `tracelib` to collect performance traces from live dashboards\n- **Playwright perf tests** — tagged `@performance` in `various-suite/perf-test.spec.ts` for payload-size checks\n- Script: `yarn e2e:benchmark:live`\n\n---\n\n### Test Execution Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    subgraph \"CI Pipeline\"\n        direction TB\n        PR[\"Pull Request\"] --> LINT[\"Lint & Type Check\"]\n        LINT --> UNIT[\"Unit Tests<br/><code>test:ci</code><br/>Jest --shard\"]\n        LINT --> PKGT[\"Package Tests<br/><code>packages:test:ci</code><br/>nx run-many\"]\n        LINT --> PLUGT[\"Plugin Tests<br/><code>plugin:test:ci</code><br/>nx run-many\"]\n        UNIT --> E2E_PW[\"E2E Tests<br/><code>e2e:playwright</code><br/>Playwright\"]\n        UNIT --> E2E_CY[\"Legacy E2E<br/><code>e2e</code><br/>Cypress\"]\n        UNIT --> STORY[\"Storybook Tests<br/><code>test:storybook</code>\"]\n        E2E_PW --> A11Y[\"Accessibility<br/><code>test:accessibility-report</code>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Local Development\"\n        DEV[\"Developer\"] --> WATCH[\"<code>yarn test</code><br/>Jest --watch\"]\n        DEV --> SINGLE[\"<code>yarn test MyComponent</code><br/>Single file\"]\n        DEV --> LOCAL_E2E[\"<code>yarn e2e:playwright</code><br/>Local E2E\"]\n    end\n\n    style PR fill:#4a90d9,color:#fff\n    style UNIT fill:#c44569,color:#fff\n    style E2E_PW fill:#3dc1d3,color:#fff\n    style E2E_CY fill:#e77f67,color:#fff\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key Scripts Summary\n\n| Script | Tool | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|\n| `yarn test` | Jest | Watch mode for local dev |\n| `yarn test:ci` | Jest | CI with sharding and reporters |\n| `yarn test:coverage` | Jest | Coverage report |\n| `yarn test:coverage:by-codeowner` | Jest | Coverage grouped by CODEOWNERS |\n| `yarn packages:test:ci` | Nx + Jest | Tests for `packages/` |\n| `yarn plugin:test:ci` | Nx + Jest | Tests for decoupled plugins |\n| `yarn e2e:playwright` | Playwright | Primary E2E suite |\n| `yarn e2e:acceptance` | Playwright | Acceptance-tagged tests |\n| `yarn e2e` | Cypress | Legacy E2E suite |\n| `yarn e2e:benchmark:live` | Cypress | Performance benchmarks |\n| `yarn test:storybook` | Storybook test-runner | Storybook interaction tests |\n| `yarn e2e:playwright:storybook` | Playwright | Storybook visual tests |\n| `yarn test:accessibility-report` | pa11y-ci | Accessibility audits |\n\n---\n\n### Testing Patterns & Conventions\n\n- **Co-location:** Unit tests sit next to source files (`MyComponent.test.tsx` beside `MyComponent.tsx`)\n- **Custom render:** Always use `render` from `test/test-utils` (not directly from `@testing-library/react`) to get full provider wrapping\n- **Feature toggle testing:** Use `testWithFeatureToggles()` to test behavior under different feature flags\n- **E2E selectors:** Shared via `@grafana/e2e-selectors` between Playwright and Cypress suites\n- **API mocking:** MSW handlers in `@grafana/test-utils` for consistent API stubs\n- **Console discipline:** `jest-fail-on-console` enforces clean console output in CI\n- **Codeowner coverage:** `jest.config.codeowner.js` enables per-team coverage tracking via `CODEOWNER_NAME`",
  "hook_event_name": "afterAgentResponse",
