  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-max-thinking-fast",
  "text": "Here's a breakdown of the `dashboard-scene` folder. It's the **Grafana Scenes-based dashboard implementation** -- the modern replacement for the older Angular-based dashboard system. It contains ~554 files across 18 top-level directories and is the single largest feature folder in the frontend. Here's how to think about it:\n\n---\n\n## What it is\n\nThis folder implements the entire dashboard experience using [Grafana Scenes](https://github.com/grafana/scenes), a reactive framework where UI is modeled as a tree of `SceneObject` instances with state, behaviors, and renderers. Every part of a dashboard -- panels, variables, time ranges, layouts, annotations -- is a scene object.\n\n---\n\n## Directory map (by responsibility)\n\n### Core runtime (`scene/` -- 166 files, the heart of it)\n\n| Subdirectory | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `scene/DashboardScene.tsx` | **The root scene object.** Start here to understand dashboard state |\n| `scene/DashboardSceneRenderer.tsx` | Top-level React renderer |\n| `scene/DashboardSceneUrlSync.ts` | URL <-> scene state synchronization |\n| `scene/DashboardControls.tsx` | Time picker, refresh, variable controls bar |\n| `scene/NavToolbarActions.tsx` | Toolbar buttons (save, share, settings, etc.) |\n| `scene/layout-default/` | Classic grid layout (`DefaultGridLayoutManager`, `DashboardGridItem`) |\n| `scene/layout-rows/` | Row-based layout manager |\n| `scene/layout-tabs/` | Tab-based layout manager |\n| `scene/layout-auto-grid/` | Auto-sizing grid layout |\n| `scene/layouts-shared/` | Shared layout utilities, registry, copy/paste |\n| `scene/types/` | TypeScript interfaces for layouts, items, drop targets, edit elements |\n| `scene/new-toolbar/` | Next-gen toolbar actions and buttons |\n| `scene/panel-timerange/` | Panel-level time range overrides |\n| `scene/panel-actions/` | Panel header action buttons (group-by, etc.) |\n\n### Serialization (`serialization/` -- 37 files)\n\nConverts between the **scene object tree** and the **dashboard JSON save model**. Two directions:\n\n- `transformSaveModelToScene.ts` -- JSON -> Scene (loading)\n- `transformSceneToSaveModel.ts` -- Scene -> JSON (saving)\n- `layoutSerializers/` -- Per-layout-type serializers (tabs, rows, auto-grid)\n- `DashboardSceneSerializer.ts` -- Orchestrates the whole process\n- `testfiles/` -- Sample dashboard JSON fixtures\n\n### Settings (`settings/` -- 110 files)\n\nDashboard settings pages (the gear icon):\n\n- `variables/` -- Variable editor UI (query, custom, datasource, ad-hoc filters, etc.)\n- `annotations/` -- Annotation settings\n- `links/` -- Dashboard link management\n- `version-history/` -- Version history and diffing (`HistorySrv`, `DiffGroup`, etc.)\n- `GeneralSettingsEditView.tsx` -- Title, description, tags, etc.\n- `JsonModelEditView.tsx` -- Raw JSON editor\n- `VersionsEditView.tsx` -- Version history view\n\n### Panel editing (`panel-edit/` -- 43 files)\n\nEverything for the panel edit drawer/page:\n\n- `PanelEditorRenderer.tsx` -- Main panel edit UI\n- `PanelDataPane/` -- Data tab (queries, transforms, alerts)\n- `PanelEditNext/` -- Next-gen query editor UI\n- `PanelVizTypePicker.tsx` -- Visualization type selector\n\n### Saving (`saving/` -- 16 files)\n\nDashboard persistence:\n\n- `SaveDashboardForm.tsx` / `SaveDashboardAsForm.tsx` -- Save dialogs\n- `DashboardSceneChangeTracker.ts` -- Dirty state / unsaved changes detection\n- `getDashboardChanges.ts` -- Diff calculation for save confirmation\n- `DashboardPrompt.tsx` -- \"Unsaved changes\" prompt\n\n### Sharing (`sharing/` -- 54 files)\n\nAll share/export functionality:\n\n- `ShareDrawer/` -- Main share drawer\n- `ShareButton/share-externally/` -- Public dashboard sharing\n- `ShareButton/share-internally/` -- Internal link sharing\n- `ShareButton/share-snapshot/` -- Snapshot sharing\n- `ExportButton/` -- Export as JSON, code, image\n- `public-dashboards/` -- Public dashboard hooks\n\n### Edit pane (`edit-pane/` -- 21 files)\n\nThe side panel shown when editing dashboards:\n\n- `DashboardEditPaneRenderer.tsx` -- Main edit pane\n- `DashboardOutline.tsx` -- Tree outline of dashboard structure\n- `VizPanelEditableElement.tsx` -- Panel selection/editing in the outline\n- `ElementEditPane.tsx` -- Generic element property editor\n\n### Other directories\n\n| Directory | Files | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pages/` | 8 | Route entry points (`DashboardScenePage.tsx` is the main page component) |\n| `utils/` | 31 | Shared helpers: URL builders, tracking, dashboard graph traversal, cloning |\n| `inspect/` | 15 | Panel inspect drawer (data, stats, query, JSON tabs, support snapshots) |\n| `conditional-rendering/` | 16 | Conditional visibility for panels (show/hide based on variable values, data) |\n| `variables/` | 4 | Low-level variable utilities |\n| `addToDashboard/` | 6 | \"Add to dashboard\" from Explore |\n| `v2schema/` | 9 | Dashboard schema v2 tooling (editor, validation, import) |\n| `behaviors/` | 1 | Attached behaviors (analytics tracking) |\n| `embedding/` | 3 | Embedded dashboard support |\n| `solo/` | 4 | Solo panel rendering (e.g., embedded in iframe) |\n| `components/` | 1 | Shared UI components |\n\n---\n\n## How to navigate effectively\n\n1. **Start at `DashboardScene.tsx`** -- it defines `DashboardSceneState` and is the root of the entire object tree. Understanding this file's state interface tells you what a dashboard \"is.\"\n\n2. **Follow the data flow:**\n   - **Loading:** `pages/DashboardScenePage.tsx` -> `serialization/transformSaveModelToScene.ts` -> `DashboardScene`\n   - **Saving:** `DashboardScene` -> `serialization/transformSceneToSaveModel.ts` -> API\n   - **URL sync:** `DashboardSceneUrlSync.ts`\n\n3. **For layout work**, pick the right `layout-*` subfolder. They all implement the `DashboardLayoutManager` interface defined in `scene/types/DashboardLayoutManager.ts`.\n\n4. **For settings/config pages**, look in `settings/` -- each settings page is a class implementing `DashboardEditView` (see the factory in `settings/utils.ts`).\n\n5. **For panel editing**, start at `panel-edit/PanelEditorRenderer.tsx` and work inward.\n\n6. **Use the `types/` folder** in `scene/types/` as an index -- it defines the key interfaces (`DashboardLayoutManager`, `DashboardLayoutItem`, `EditableDashboardElement`, etc.) that the rest of the code implements.",
