  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Yes, I found it. Here's a summary of the Notion page:\n\n---\n\n**[PRD: Copy dashboard link with expiring share tokens](https://www.notion.so/31f9a121891b81648abccba381b34564)**\n\n**Goal:** Give users a simple way to copy a dashboard link that can expire automatically, making sharing feel safer and more intentional.\n\n**Problem:** Sharing a dashboard link today feels too open-ended for temporary access. Users may want to share for a short period without leaving a reusable link active indefinitely.\n\n**Proposed feature:** Add a \"Copy dashboard link\" flow in the dashboard toolbar with expiry options. The basic experience:\n\n1. User clicks **Copy dashboard link** from the toolbar\n2. A simple modal appears with expiry options\n3. User selects an option and copies the generated link\n4. Anyone with the link can use it until it expires\n5. After expiry, the link no longer works\n\n**Suggested expiry options:** 1 hour, 24 hours, 7 days, Never expires\n\n**Scope:**\n- Add a lightweight share modal in the dashboard toolbar\n- Support expiring share links backed by share tokens\n- Reuse existing short link behavior where possible\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Which expiry options should be shown by default?\n- Should never-expiring links be allowed for all users?\n- What should people see when they open an expired link?\n\n---\n\nWould you like to work on implementing this feature?",
