  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "The feature described in the PRD is **not implemented yet**. Here's the breakdown:\n\n### What exists today\n\n| Mechanism | Live dashboard? | Expiry? | Match? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Share internally (copy link)** | Yes | No expiry | Partial |\n| **Public dashboard** (`accessToken`) | Yes | No expiry field in the model | Partial |\n| **Snapshot sharing** | No (frozen copy) | Yes (1h / 1d / 1w / never) | Wrong semantics |\n| **Short URLs** | Redirect only | Stale cleanup, not user-facing | No |\n\n### What's missing\n\nThe PRD asks for a **live dashboard link** (not a frozen snapshot) that **expires after a chosen duration** (1h, 24h, 7 days, never). Nothing in the codebase combines both properties:\n\n- **Public dashboard tokens** are the closest mechanism but have **no expiration fields** in the model (`pkg/services/publicdashboards/models/models.go`).\n- **Snapshots** have expiry but are frozen data, not live dashboards.\n- There's **no feature flag** registered for this feature yet.\n\n### Reusable infrastructure\n\nThere's a lot to build on though:\n\n- The **Share button/menu** in the dashboard scene toolbar (`public/app/features/dashboard-scene/sharing/ShareButton/`)\n- The **public dashboards** backend and token generation (`pkg/services/publicdashboards/`)\n- The **short URL** service (`pkg/services/shorturls/`)\n- The **snapshot expiry pattern** as a reference for the TTL model\n\nIn short: the building blocks are there, but the specific \"copy dashboard link with expiring share token\" feature from the PRD needs to be built. Would you like to start planning the implementation?",
