  "model": "default",
  "text": "Yes, I found the PRD in your Notion workspace.\n\n**PRD: Copy dashboard link with expiring share tokens**\n\n**Goal:** Give users a simple way to copy a dashboard link that can expire automatically, making sharing feel safer and more intentional.\n\n**Problem:** Today, sharing a dashboard link can feel too open-ended for temporary access. Users may want to share a dashboard for a short period without leaving a reusable link active indefinitely.\n\n**Proposed Feature:** Add a **Copy dashboard link** flow in the dashboard toolbar. When a user opens it, they can choose an expiry option and copy a share link that stops working after that time.\n\n**Basic Experience:**\n- User clicks **Copy dashboard link** from the dashboard toolbar\n- A simple modal appears with expiry options\n- User selects an option and copies the generated link\n- Anyone with the link can use it until it expires\n- After expiry, the link no longer works\n\n**Suggested Expiry Options:**\n- 1 hour\n- 24 hours\n- 7 days\n- Never expires\n\n**Scope:**\n- Add a lightweight share modal in the dashboard toolbar\n- Support expiring share links backed by share tokens\n- Reuse the existing short link behavior where possible\n\n**Success Criteria:**\n- Users can create a dashboard share link in a few clicks\n- Users clearly understand when the link will expire\n- Expired links stop working as expected\n\n**Open Questions:**\n- Which expiry options should be shown by default?\n- Should never-expiring links be allowed for all users?\n- What should people see when they open an expired link?\n\nThe full PRD is available at: https://www.notion.so/31f9a121891b81648abccba381b34564\n\nWould you like me to help implement this feature?",
