[2026-03-24 15:46:25] afterAgentResponse
{
  "conversation_id": "3ec7b38c-2e1d-498a-aef5-757b6363713d",
  "generation_id": "77600a91-0788-4c57-997f-799664d7f1bc",
  "model": "composer-2-fast",
  "text": "\n## What `dashboard-scene` is\n\n`public/app/features/dashboard-scene/` is the **frontend implementation of Grafana dashboards built on `@grafana/scenes`**. The main object is **`DashboardScene`** — a `SceneObject` that holds dashboard state (title, layout, variables, time range, edit mode, overlays, etc.) and wires it to URL sync, serialization, and the React tree.\n\nIt sits alongside the older dashboard stack (`DashboardModel`, classic containers under `features/dashboard/`). Routing and loading for the “scene” path go through **`DashboardScenePage`** and **`DashboardScenePageStateManager`**, which load JSON from the API and run **`transformSaveModelToScene`** (and related transforms) to build a `DashboardScene` instance.\n\n```99:152:public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/DashboardScene.tsx\nexport interface DashboardSceneState extends SceneObjectState {\n  /** The title */\n  title: string;\n  /** The description */\n  description?: string;\n  /** Tags */\n  tags?: string[];\n  /** Links */\n  links: DashboardLink[];\n  /** Is editable */\n  editable?: boolean;\n  /** Allows disabling grid lazy loading */\n  preload?: boolean;\n  /** A uid when saved */\n  uid?: string;\n  /** @experimental */\n  scopeMeta?: ScopeMeta;\n  /** @deprecated */\n  id?: number | null;\n  /** Layout of panels */\n  body: DashboardLayoutManager;\n  /** NavToolbar actions */\n  actions?: SceneObject[];\n  /** Fixed row at the top of the canvas with for example variables and time range controls */\n  controls?: DashboardControls;\n  /** True when editing */\n  isEditing?: boolean;\n  /** True when user made a change */\n  isDirty?: boolean;\n  /** meta flags */\n  meta: Omit<DashboardMeta, 'isNew'>;\n  /** Version of the dashboard */\n  version?: number;\n  /** Panel to inspect */\n  inspectPanelKey?: string;\n  /** Panel key to view in fullscreen */\n  viewPanel?: string;\n  /** Edit view */\n  editview?: DashboardEditView;\n  /** Edit panel */\n  editPanel?: PanelEditor;\n  /** Scene object that handles the current drawer or modal */\n  overlay?: SceneObject;\n  /** Share view */\n  shareView?: string;\n  /** Renders panels in grid and filtered */\n  panelSearch?: string;\n  /** How many panels to show per row for search results */\n  panelsPerRow?: number;\n  /** options pane */\n  editPane: DashboardEditPane;\n  /** Manages dragging/dropping of layout items */\n;\n}\n```\n\n(The interface continues in the file; it’s the mental model for “what a dashboard is” in this feature.)\n\n---\n\n## How to navigate the architecture effectively\n\nUse a **top-down path** first, then branch by concern:\n\n| Layer | Folder | Role |\n|--------|--------|------|\n| **Route & lifecycle** | `pages/` | `DashboardScenePage`, `DashboardScenePageStateManager` — load dashboard, cache scene, connect to routes |\n| **Root scene & chrome** | `scene/` | `DashboardScene`, `DashboardSceneRenderer`, URL sync, toolbar (`new-toolbar/`), controls, drilldowns |\n| **Layouts** | `scene/layout-default/`, `layout-rows/`, `layout-tabs/`, `layout-auto-grid/`, `layouts-shared/` | How panels are arranged; each layout has managers/renderers |\n| **Persistence** | `serialization/` | `transformSaveModelToScene` / `transformSceneToSaveModel`, layout serializers, v1 vs v2 dashboard schema |\n| **Dashboard settings UI** | `settings/` | Settings “edit views” (variables, annotations, links, versions, permissions, …) |\n| **Canvas editing** | `edit-pane/` | Selection, edit pane, drag/drop orchestration with the scene |\n| **Panel editor** | `panel-edit/` | Full panel edit experience (options, queries, transforms) |\n| **Share / export** | `sharing/` | Share drawer, public dashboards, snapshots, export |\n| **Save / dirty state** | `saving/` | Change tracking, prompts, save flows |\n| **Cross-cutting** | `utils/`, `variables/`, `conditional-rendering/`, `v2schema/` | URLs, session, variables glue, conditional rules, schema helpers |\n\n**Practical navigation tips:**\n\n1. **Start at `pages/DashboardScenePage.tsx` + `DashboardScenePageStateManager.ts`** — see how a loaded DTO becomes a scene and when state is cleared.\n2. **Open `scene/DashboardScene.tsx` and `scene/DashboardSceneRenderer.tsx`** — see how state maps to the page shell (toolbar, body, overlays, edit/settings).\n3. **For “how does JSON become UI?”** — follow `serialization/transformSaveModelToScene.ts` (and v2 variants under the same tree).\n4. **For “where is feature X?”** — search under `settings/` (dashboard-level), `panel-edit/` (panel-level), or `sharing/` / `saving/` for export/save.\n5. **For layout behavior** — pick the layout folder that matches the product concept (default grid vs rows vs tabs vs auto-grid) and read the `*LayoutManager*` files.\n\n**Mental model:** `DashboardScene` is the **single source of runtime truth**; `serialization/` is the **bridge to the saved JSON model**; `pages/` is **boot/teardown**; everything else is **vertical slices** (settings, panel edit, share, etc.) hung off that tree.\n\nIf you tell me what you’re trying to change (e.g. toolbar, a settings tab, or save format), I can point to the narrowest files to open next.",
