[2026-03-24 15:47:16] afterAgentResponse
{
  "conversation_id": "3ec7b38c-2e1d-498a-aef5-757b6363713d",
  "generation_id": "24942ecc-5987-49cb-98f6-bc28f7f98dc1",
  "model": "composer-2-fast",
  "text": "\nHere’s a practical breakdown of what “adding a new property” means in `dashboard-scene`, which files usually touch, and a sensible order. The exact list depends on **whether the value is stored in JSON**, **v1 vs v2**, and **whether anything outside the scene still reads `DashboardModel`-style APIs**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Decide what the property is\n\n- **Persisted in dashboard JSON (normal case)**  \n  You need a **round trip**: load JSON → `DashboardScene` state → save JSON again. That always goes through the serialization layer, and often through `@grafana/schema` / `DashboardModel` depending on field.\n\n- **UI-only / runtime-only**  \n  You might only extend `DashboardSceneState`, plus any UI that sets it. You can skip save-model transforms **unless** you also want it in exports or “get dashboard JSON”.\n\n- **In the URL**  \n  You’d also touch **`scene/DashboardSceneUrlSync.ts`** (and any tests).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Files in `dashboard-scene` that are usually required\n\n### Core model (always for a real dashboard-level field)\n\n| Step | File | Why |\n|------|------|-----|\n| State | `scene/DashboardScene.tsx` | Add the field on `DashboardSceneState` (and defaults in the constructor if needed). |\n| Dirty / “what counts as a saved change” | Same file: `PERSISTED_PROPS` | If edits to this field should mark the dashboard dirty and participate in change tracking, **add the key here**. `DashboardSceneChangeTracker` imports this list. |\n\n```95:95:public/app/features/dashboard-scene/scene/DashboardScene.tsx\nexport const PERSISTED_PROPS = ['title', 'description', 'tags', 'editable', 'graphTooltip', 'links', 'meta', 'preload'];\n```\n\n### v1 save model (classic `Dashboard` JSON)\n\n| Step | File | Why |\n|------|------|-----|\n| Load | `serialization/transformSaveModelToScene.ts` | In `createDashboardSceneFromDashboardModel`, pass the value into `new DashboardScene({ ... })` from `oldModel` / `dto` (same pattern as `title`, `preload`, `scopeMeta`, etc.). |\n| Save | `serialization/transformSceneToSaveModel.ts` | In `transformSceneToSaveModel`, add it to the `dashboard` object built from `state` (see e.g. `scopeMeta` with `@ts-expect-error` if not in schema). |\n\n### v2 / Kubernetes dashboard spec (if you support v2)\n\n| Step | File | Why |\n|------|------|-----|\n| Load | `serialization/transformSaveModelSchemaV2ToScene.ts` | Map from `dashboard` (`DashboardV2Spec`) into `new DashboardScene({ ... })`. |\n| Save | `serialization/transformSceneToSaveModelSchemaV2.ts` | Map `scene.state` into the v2 spec object. |\n\n### Compatibility with legacy “current dashboard” API\n\n| Step | File | Why |\n|------|------|-----|\n| Optional | `utils/DashboardModelCompatibilityWrapper.ts` | Add a getter (or method) if code still expects `getDashboardSrv().getCurrent()`-style access to the new field (pattern: `graphTooltip`, `tags`, …). |\n\n### Tests (should be updated for persisted fields)\n\n- `serialization/transformSaveModelToScene.test.ts`\n- `serialization/transformSceneToSaveModel.test.ts`\n- `serialization/transformSaveModelSchemaV2ToScene` / `transformSceneToSaveModelSchemaV2` tests if v2 is involved\n- `serialization/DashboardSceneSerializer.test.ts` if serializer behavior changes\n- `saving/DashboardSceneChangeTracker.test.ts` if dirty behavior matters\n\n---\n\n## 3. Often **outside** this folder (still “required” for a real persisted field)\n\nThese are not under `dashboard-scene/`, but they matter if the property is part of the official model:\n\n- **`@grafana/schema`** (`Dashboard`, and/or v2 `Spec`) — so TypeScript and validators match stored JSON.\n- **`app/features/dashboard/state/DashboardModel`** — v1 load path often goes through `DashboardModel`; unknown fields sometimes need explicit handling or migration.\n- **Backend** — if the API persists only known fields, the server may need to accept/store the new key.\n\nExperimental fields sometimes stay out of the schema temporarily using **`@ts-expect-error`** on the assembled object (see `scopeMeta` in `transformSceneToSaveModel.ts`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Suggested order of work\n\n1. **Define persistence & schema** — v1 only, v2, or experimental; whether backend/schema must change.  \n2. **`DashboardScene.tsx`** — `DashboardSceneState` + constructor defaults; **`PERSISTED_PROPS`** if it should affect unsaved changes.  \n3. **Deserialize** — `transformSaveModelToScene.ts` (`createDashboardSceneFromDashboardModel`); **then** `transformSaveModelSchemaV2ToScene.ts` if v2 is in scope.  \n4. **Serialize** — `transformSceneToSaveModel.ts`; **then** `transformSceneToSaveModelSchemaV2.ts` if v2.  \n5. **`DashboardModelCompatibilityWrapper`** — only if legacy callers need the property.  \n6. **`DashboardSceneUrlSync`** — only if the property syncs with the URL.  \n7. **UI** — settings, toolbar, or scene code that calls `scene.setState({ ... })`.  \n8. **Tests** — round-trip and change-tracking tests for the paths you touched.\n\n---\n\n## 5. What you do *not* always touch\n\n- **`serialization/DashboardSceneSerializer.ts`** — only if you change serializer contracts, tracking, or change-diff behavior beyond normal getSaveModel output.\n- **`saving/getDashboardChanges.ts`** — change diffs are usually driven by comparing serialized models; if the new field is in the serialized output, it often “just works,” but worth verifying if you have special save options (time/variables/refresh).\n\n---\n\n**Short answer:** the minimal **in-folder** set for a **persisted** dashboard property is: **`scene/DashboardScene.tsx`** (state + `PERSISTED_PROPS`), **`serialization/transformSaveModelToScene.ts`**, **`serialization/transformSceneToSaveModel.ts`**, plus **v2 transform files** if v2 applies, **tests**, and optionally **`DashboardModelCompatibilityWrapper.ts`** and **`DashboardSceneUrlSync.ts`**. Anything that must appear in stored JSON or API responses usually also needs **schema / `DashboardModel` / backend** updates outside this folder.",
