  "text": "\nHere’s what was added.\n\n## Created: `.cursor/skills/dashboard-scene-new-property/SKILL.md`\n\n**Skill name:** `dashboard-scene-new-property`  \n\n**Description:** Tuned for discovery (third person, WHAT + WHEN): adding or changing dashboard-level properties under `public/app/features/dashboard-scene/`, including state, v1/v2 serialization, dirty tracking, and tests.\n\n**Contents:**\n- **Classification** — persisted vs runtime-only vs URL-synced\n- **Ordered steps** (1–10) — schema/API → `DashboardScene` + `PERSISTED_PROPS` → v1 load/save → v2 load/save → compatibility wrapper → URL sync → UI → tests → verification\n- **Copy-paste checklist** — paths under `dashboard-scene/`\n- **Outside the feature** — `grafana-schema`, `DashboardModel`, backend\n- **Short notes** — serializer, `getDashboardChanges`, link to `grafana-build-patterns.mdc`\n\nIt’s **~99 lines** (well under the 500-line guideline). Stored as a **project skill** under `.cursor/skills/` so it travels with the repo.\n\nTo use it in Cursor: reference it in chat (“use the dashboard-scene property skill”) or rely on the description so the agent picks it up when you work on `dashboard-scene` or new `DashboardSceneState` fields.\n\nIf you want a **`reference.md`** with concrete code pointers (e.g. `scopeMeta` / `@ts-expect-error` examples), say so and we can add it.",
