[2026-03-24 15:55:36] afterAgentResponse
{
  "conversation_id": "83be47de-32de-477f-adcc-65ba6b5e3b75",
  "generation_id": "ba8ef420-cef8-41c7-b97f-237f8b939d08",
  "model": "composer-2-fast",
  "text": "\nHere is a merged picture from two parallel codebase explorations: **backend notification routing** and **how the notification-policies UI is built**.\n\n---\n\n## Notification routing (unified alerting)\n\n**Where it lives:** Unified alerting is under `pkg/services/ngalert` (not legacy `pkg/alerting`). Actual route matching after alerts are ingested is implemented in **`github.com/grafana/alerting/notify`** (Grafana’s Alertmanager stack); this repo owns **config merge**, **autogenerated routes**, and **which Alertmanager instance** receives `PutAlerts`.\n\n**Which Alertmanager gets alerts**\n\n- **`AlertsRouter`** (`pkg/services/ngalert/sender/router.go`) decides per org whether firing alerts go to the **internal** Grafana Alertmanager, **external** Alertmanager URL(s), or **both**, using org admin **`SendAlertsTo`** (`models.AlertmanagersChoice`). Remote-primary / HA modes can change whether routing is local or delegated to a remote tenant.\n\n```28:44:pkg/services/ngalert/sender/router.go\n// AlertsRouter handles alerts generated during alert rule evaluation.\n// Based on rule's orgID and the configuration for that organization,\n// it determines whether an alert needs to be sent to an external Alertmanager and\\or internal notifier.Alertmanager\n//\n// After creating a AlertsRouter, you must call Run to keep the AlertsRouter's\n// state synchronized with the alerting configuration.\ntype AlertsRouter struct {\n\tlogger           log.Logger\n\tclock            clock.Clock\n\tadminConfigStore store.AdminConfigurationStore\n\n\t// externalAlertmanagers help us send alerts to external Alertmanagers.\n\tadminConfigMtx               sync.RWMutex\n\tsendAlertsTo                 map[int64]models.AlertmanagersChoice\n\texternalAlertmanagers        map[int64]*ExternalAlertmanager\n\texternalAlertmanagersCfgHash map[int64]string\n\n\tmultiOrgNotifier *notifier.MultiOrgAlertmanager\n```\n\n**From evaluation to a receiver**\n\n1. **Scheduler** evaluates rules and updates state; **`StateToPostableAlert`** (`state/compat.go`) builds `PostableAlert`s.\n2. **Per-rule “simplified” routing:** If the rule has **`NotificationSettings`**, labels like `__grafana_autogenerated__`, `__grafana_receiver__`, and optionally a **settings hash** are added (`models/notifications.go`, `state/state.go`) so the internal tree can match without manual policy for every rule.\n3. **`AlertsRouter.Send`** forwards batches to internal **`MultiOrgAlertmanager.PutAlerts`** and optionally to externals.\n4. Internal AM **`applyConfig`** merges stored config with **`AddAutogenConfig`** (`notifier/autogen_alertmanager.go`): an **autogenerated subtree** is prepended under the root so simplified-routing alerts match **Continue: false** and do not fall through to user routes.\n5. Remaining alerts follow the **user notification policy tree** (same semantics as upstream Alertmanager). **Contact points** are receivers; **mute/active time intervals** and silences apply in the shared pipeline.\n\n**Config / policy APIs**\n\n- **`NotificationPolicyService`** (`provisioning/notification_policies.go`) for get/update/reset of the **user route tree**.\n- **`PostableUserConfig`**, **`Route`**, **`GetMergedAlertmanagerConfig`** (`api/tooling/definitions/alertmanager.go`).\n\n**Flags that touch routing/delivery** (non-exhaustive): `alertingDisableSendAlertsExternal`, `alertingUseNewSimplifiedRoutingHashAlgorithm` (hash for autogen child routes), remote-primary/secondary flags, `alertingMultiplePolicies` (see `featuremgmt/registry.go`).\n\n---\n\n## Alerting UI: notification policies\n\n**Entry**\n\n- Route: **`/alerting/routes`** → lazy‑loaded **`NotificationPoliciesPage`**.\n\n```43:56:public/app/features/alerting/routes.tsx\n      path: '/alerting/routes',\n      pageNav: {\n        id: 'am-routes',\n        text: 'Notification policies',\n        subTitle: 'Configure how alerts are routed to contact points',\n      },\n      component: () =>\n        import(\n          /* webpackChunkName: \"NotificationPoliciesPage\" */ 'app/features/alerting/unified/NotificationPoliciesPage'\n        ),\n```\n\n**Components**\n\n- **`NotificationPoliciesPage.tsx`** — tabs (policies vs time intervals).\n- **`NotificationPoliciesList.tsx`** — loads tree + contact points + alert groups, filtering, modals.\n- **`Policy.tsx`** — **one route node**: matchers row, **`MetadataRow`** (contact point, group/mute/active timings, repeat/grouping), recursive **`Policy`** for `routes`.\n- **`Matchers.tsx`**, **`Modals.tsx`**, **`EditNotificationPolicyForm.tsx`** / **`EditDefaultPolicyForm.tsx`**.\n\n**Data**\n\n- **`useNotificationPolicyRoute.ts`**:  \n  - **K8s API:** `routingtrees` when `shouldUseK8sApi(alertmanager)`.  \n  - **Classic:** `useGetAlertmanagerConfigurationQuery` → `alertmanager_config.route` as a one-element array.\n- Routes are normalized to **`RouteWithID`** via **`addUniqueIdentifierToRoute`** (`unified/utils/amroutes`), using types from `public/app/plugins/datasource/alertmanager/types`.\n- **`routesReducer`** + **`useProduceNewAlertmanagerConfiguration`** apply edits to the full AM config; K8s path uses replace mutation + **`routeToK8sSubRoute`** mapping.\n\n**Rendering**\n\n- Recursive **Policy** tree (not a graph library): expand/collapse, pagination for large sibling lists, **`findRoutesMatchingFilters`** + **`computeInheritedTree`** for filter-aware display.\n\n---\n\n## How the two sides connect\n\n- The **UI** edits the **same route tree and receiver names** that are persisted into Alertmanager config (or K8s routing tree CRs), which the internal AM loads after merge.\n- **Autogenerated routes** for simplified per-rule contact points are **built in the backend** (`autogen_alertmanager.go`); the UI may show indicators like **`AutogeneratedRootIndicator`** for those nodes, but the **label injection** that drives matching is **evaluation-time**, not drawn from the UI alone.\n\n**Tests to read next:** `NotificationPoliciesPage.test.tsx`, `useNotificationPolicyRoute.test.tsx`, `Policy.test.tsx`, `notificationPolicyRoutes.test.ts` under `public/app/features/alerting/unified/`.",
