  "text": "\nHere’s what was added.\n\n## Subagent: `coverage-scout`\n\n**File:** `.cursor/agents/coverage-scout.md` (project scope, safe to commit for your team)\n\n**Intent:** Fast, **preliminary** pass that pairs production code with tests using **rg/glob/heuristics**—not full coverage metrics. Emphasizes a **fixed summary format** so you can hand off to a deeper review or another agent.\n\n**Frontmatter:**\n- **`name`:** `coverage-scout`\n- **`description`:** When to delegate (quick gap scan, before refactors/features/risk reviews, speed-first)\n\n**Behavior (in the body):**\n- Workflow: anchor scope → inventory non-test sources → pair `foo.go`/`foo_test.go`, `Component`/`Component.test` → flag systemic gaps → **required** report sections: Scope, Coverage signal, Gaps, Fast follow-ups, Out of scope\n- Explicitly avoids heavy steps unless asked (e.g. full `go test -cover` / Jest coverage)\n\n**How to use:** In Cursor, ask something like: *Use the **coverage-scout** subagent to scan `pkg/services/ngalert/sender` (or the whole repo)*.\n\nIf you want the same agent **globally** (all projects), copy the file to `~/.cursor/agents/coverage-scout.md` and optionally trim Grafana-specific table rows from the prompt.",
