  "model": "composer-2-fast",
  "text": "\nHere’s what was verified in the repo and how the subagent was updated.\n\n### Patterns investigated\n\n| Topic | Finding |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Go unit vs integration** | `make test-go-unit` uses `-short`; `test-go-integration` runs `-run \"^TestIntegration\"`. `scripts/ci/backend-tests/pkgs-with-tests-named.sh` filters packages by test name prefix. |\n| **`pkg/tests/`** | Large, separate tree: `pkg/tests/api/` vs `pkg/tests/apis/` (K8s-style), domain folders like `alerting`, `provisioning`. Not the same packages as `pkg/services/*`. |\n| **`apps/`** | App modules under `apps/<name>/` with their own tests—should be scoped per app. |\n| **Jest** | Root `jest.config.js`: roots `public/app`, `public/test`, `packages`, `scripts/tests`; `testRegex` targets **`.test.ts`/`.test.tsx`**, not `.spec` (`.spec` is used heavily under Playwright). |\n| **Playwright** | `playwright.config.ts` uses **`e2e-playwright/`** as `testDirRoot`; older material under **`e2e/`**. |\n| **Makefile** | Documented `test-go-unit-pretty FILES=...`, `test-go-integration`, `test-js`, `test`. |\n\n### Updates to `.cursor/agents/coverage-scout.md`\n\n1. **`model:` removed** from frontmatter so it matches the standard subagent format (`name` + `description` only).\n\n2. **New section: “Grafana repository map”** — table for `pkg/`, `pkg/registry/apis/`, `pkg/tests/`, `apps/`, `public/app/`, `packages/`, `e2e-playwright/` vs `e2e/`, with a **cross-walk rule**: scanning `pkg/services/...` must also consider **`pkg/tests/...`**.\n\n3. **“Go: three layers”** — package unit tests, `TestIntegration*`, and `pkg/tests` API suites; notes on `*_integration_test.go`, rare `*_private_test.go`, and excluding generated files.\n\n4. **“Frontend: Jest”** — roots, `.test.ts(x)` vs Playwright `.spec.ts`, plugins with their own `jest.config.js`.\n\n5. **“E2E”** — when to mention browser tests vs unit gaps.\n\n6. **“Makefile shortcuts”** — table aligned with this repo’s targets.\n\n7. **Workflow** — pairing steps now reference **`pkg/tests`**, **`TestIntegration`**, **`apps/`**, and the **Scope** section of the report asks which **layers** were checked.\n\nThe subagent is now tuned so a preliminary scan follows Grafana’s real layout instead of a generic monorepo guess.",
