  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the React Router architecture and the v5-to-v6 migration status in Grafana.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nGrafana's routing is a **hybrid v5/v6 system**. The outer shell is React Router v5 (`react-router-dom` 5.3.4), but nearly all internal route definitions and hooks use v6-style APIs provided by the **`react-router-dom-v5-compat`** bridge package (resolves to 6.30.3). A custom **`locationService`** abstraction owns the `history` instance and is shared between React Router and imperative navigation code.\n\n### Key files\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/.../LocationService.tsx` | Singleton `locationService` wrapping a `history` v4/v5 `History` object |\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Outer v5 `<Router>` + `<CompatRouter>` bridge |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Builds v6-style `<Routes>` / `<Route element={...}>` tree |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Per-route guard (auth, roles) + lazy `Suspense` wrapper |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central `RouteDescriptor[]` registry |\n\n### Component Tree (top-down)\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[\"index.ts / app.ts<br/>(bootstrap)\"] --> B[\"AppWrapper<br/>(Redux, Theme, Context)\"]\n    B --> C[\"RouterWrapper<br/>(RoutesWrapper.tsx)\"]\n    C --> D[\"v5 Router<br/>history=locationService.getHistory()\"]\n    D --> E[\"CompatRouter<br/>(react-router-dom-v5-compat)\"]\n    E --> F[\"Routes<br/>(v6-style, from compat)\"]\n    F --> G[\"Route element=GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/>(v6-style, from compat)\"]\n    G --> H[\"GrafanaRoute<br/>(auth guard, Suspense, lazy page)\"]\n\n    style D fill:#f9d4d4,stroke:#c33\n    style E fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n    style F fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#059669\n    style G fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#059669\n```\n\n**Legend:** Red = v5 API, Yellow = compat bridge, Green = v6-style API\n\n---\n\n## The Three Layers of Navigation\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Layer 1: History (v4/v5)\"\n        H[\"history package<br/>createBrowserHistory\"]\n    end\n    subgraph \"Layer 2: locationService\"\n        LS[\"locationService<br/>.push() .partial() .replace()<br/>.getLocation() .getHistory()\"]\n    end\n    subgraph \"Layer 3: React Router\"\n        RR5[\"v5 Router<br/>(outer shell)\"]\n        COMPAT[\"CompatRouter<br/>(bridge)\"]\n        RR6[\"v6-style hooks<br/>useNavigate, useLocation,<br/>useParams, Navigate\"]\n    end\n\n    H --> LS\n    H --> RR5\n    RR5 --> COMPAT\n    COMPAT --> RR6\n    LS -.->|\"shared history<br/>instance\"| RR5\n```\n\nThe `locationService` and the v5 `Router` share the **same** `History` object. This means imperative calls like `locationService.push('/foo')` trigger React Router re-renders, and vice versa.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Status: v5 to v6\n\n### What's done vs. what remains\n\n```mermaid\npie title \"v5 → v6 Migration Progress\"\n    \"v6-style APIs via compat (done)\" : 85\n    \"v5 Router shell (remaining)\" : 10\n    \"locationService consolidation (in-progress)\" : 5\n```\n\n### Detailed migration state\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph done [\"Completed ✓\"]\n        direction TB\n        A1[\"Switch → Routes\"]\n        A2[\"Route render= → Route element=\"]\n        A3[\"withRouter → hooks\"]\n        A4[\"useHistory → useNavigate / locationService\"]\n        A5[\"Link via compat package\"]\n        A6[\"Navigate component for redirects\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph inprog [\"In Progress\"]\n        direction TB\n        B1[\"useLocation (react-router)<br/>→ locationService.getLocation()\"]\n        B2[\"2 files still import<br/>from raw react-router\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph remaining [\"Remaining for Full v6\"]\n        direction TB\n        C1[\"Remove v5 Router + CompatRouter<br/>→ v6 createBrowserRouter / BrowserRouter\"]\n        C2[\"Remove history package dependency<br/>→ v6 native history\"]\n        C3[\"Adopt v6 data APIs<br/>(loaders, actions)\"]\n        C4[\"Decouple locationService<br/>from history v4/v5 API\"]\n    end\n\n    style done fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#059669\n    style inprog fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706\n    style remaining fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626\n```\n\n### By the numbers\n\n| Pattern | Status | Count |\n|---------|--------|-------|\n| Files importing from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` | v6-style | ~145 |\n| `<Routes>` / `<Route element={}>` | v6-style | All routes |\n| `useNavigate` (from compat) | v6-style | 17 production files |\n| `withRouter` | Eliminated | 0 |\n| `<Switch>` | Eliminated | 0 (only in a comment) |\n| `Route render={}` | Eliminated | 0 |\n| Raw `react-router-dom` v5 imports | Remaining | 5 files (Router shell + test utils) |\n| `useLocation` from raw `react-router` | Remaining | 2 files |\n\n### What blocks the final v6 cutover\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[\"locationService<br/>wraps history v4/v5\"] -->|\"blocks\"| B[\"Remove v5 Router\"]\n    B -->|\"blocks\"| C[\"Remove compat layer\"]\n    C -->|\"enables\"| D[\"Pure react-router v6<br/>with createBrowserRouter\"]\n    \n    E[\"Plugin API compatibility<br/>(v5 deprecated in v11)\"] -.->|\"external constraint\"| B\n```\n\nThe core blocker is that **`locationService`** is tightly coupled to the `history` package's v4/v5 `History` interface. The v5 `<Router history={...}>` is the only React Router `Router` that accepts an external `history` object — v6's `BrowserRouter` and `createBrowserRouter` manage history internally. So the migration requires either:\n\n1. Refactoring `locationService` to work with v6's internal navigation APIs, or\n2. Replacing `locationService` usage across the codebase with v6 hooks like `useNavigate`\n\nThe `location-service-migration-status.md` document tracks incremental progress on option 2 — moving call sites from React Router hooks to `locationService` first (for testability), with the longer-term goal of having a single navigation abstraction that can be rewired to v6 internals.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nGrafana is roughly **85% migrated** at the API surface level — all route definitions, components, and most hooks use v6-style patterns via the compat bridge. The remaining work is structural: replacing the v5 `Router` shell, decoupling from the `history` package, and deciding the future of `locationService` relative to React Router v6's built-in navigation primitives.",
