  "text": "\nHere’s what I did:\n\n### Scan\n- Searched for **`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`**, **`eval` / `new Function`**, **`innerHTML`**, **`postMessage`**, **`localStorage`**, and **`target=\"_blank\"`**.\n- Spot-checked important paths: **`renderMarkdown`** (sanitizes by default), **`PanelDescription`** / panel chrome (description goes through **`renderMarkdown`**), and **`KeyValuesTable`** vs **`jsonMarkup`** escaping.\n\n### Report\nA short write-up is in:\n\n**`/Users/markboos/.cursor/worktrees/grafana/wzb/FRONTEND_SECURITY_SCAN.md`**\n\nMain takeaway called out there: **`KeyValuesTable`** builds HTML for `code` / `text` rows by inserting **`row.value` raw**, while the JSON path uses **`jsonMarkup`**’s **`escape()`**—that mismatch is the clearest **XSS-style** risk from this pass. Everything else is mostly **expected dynamic JS** (scripted dashboards, table expression filters) or **defense-in-depth** items (`postMessage('*')`, link `rel`, dependency audits).\n\nI did not run **`npm audit`**; the report recommends doing that in CI or locally for supply-chain coverage.",
