[2026-03-31 13:43:14] afterAgentResponse
{
  "conversation_id": "23194eba-284f-46bf-aeab-7fb9dff92ba8",
  "generation_id": "8af7055c-4a17-4436-ada9-8a214a5ceffd",
  "model": "composer-2-fast",
  "text": "\nHere is a concise architecture overview based on the current dashboard-scene sharing code.\n\n## Architecture overview\n\n**Toolbar → share UI** is split into two paths:\n\n1. **Primary “Share” control** — Opens `CopyDashboardLinkModal` (short link + expiration). Implemented in `ShareButton.tsx` and `ShareDashboardButton.tsx` (new toolbar), both wired to the same modal.\n\n2. **Chevron dropdown (`ShareMenu`)** — Builds a list of actions. Most items call `locationService.partial({ shareView: ... })`, which drives the **Share drawer** (`ShareDrawer`) and picks a tab (`ShareInternally`, `ShareExternally`, etc.) via `shareDashboardType` in `ShareModal/utils.ts`. The menu also supports **`addDashboardShareDrawerItem`** for extensions.\n\nSo “add copy dashboard UID to the share menu” almost certainly means **a new row in `ShareMenu`** (and the same behavior whether the menu comes from `ShareButton` or `ShareDashboardButton`). It does **not** automatically require a new `shareView` or a new `ShareDrawer` tab unless you deliberately design it that way (e.g. a dedicated screen). A minimal design is: menu item → copy `dashboard.state.uid` to the clipboard (with handling when there is no UID yet).\n\n**Data source for UID:** `DashboardScene` state exposes `uid` for saved dashboards (`DashboardScene.tsx`).\n\n**Legacy path:** Non-scene dashboards can still use `ShareModal` from `DashboardPage` when `shareView` is set. Scene dashboards use the drawer + URL param pattern. If you only change `ShareMenu`, you target the **scene toolbar**; parity with the old modal would be a **separate** change if product requires it.\n\n---\n\n### Component / flow (Mermaid)\n\n**Where the share UI lives**\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  subgraph toolbar [Toolbar entry points]\n    SB[ShareButton]\n    SDB[ShareDashboardButton]\n  end\n  subgraph shared [Shared pieces]\n    SM[ShareMenu]\n    CDLM[CopyDashboardLinkModal]\n  end\n  SB --> CDLM\n  SB --> SM\n  SDB --> CDLM\n  SDB --> SM\n```\n\n**What happens when a dropdown item is used**\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  SM[ShareMenu item onClick]\n  LS[locationService.partial shareView]\n  SD[ShareDrawer + getShareView]\n  TAB[Tab components e.g. ShareInternally]\n  SM --> LS --> SD --> TAB\n```\n\n**Contrast: primary “Share” / copy link (not the dropdown list)**\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  BTN[Primary Share click]\n  CDLM[CopyDashboardLinkModal]\n  short[shortLinks / buildShareUrl]\n  BTN --> CDLM --> short\n```\n\n---\n\n### Dependencies worth knowing\n\n| Layer | Role |\n|--------|------|\n| `ShareMenu.tsx` | Builds menu items, `SaveBeforeShareModal` when dirty+editing, `DashboardInteractions.sharingCategoryClicked` |\n| `ShareModal/utils.ts` | `shareDashboardType`, `getTrackingSource` |\n| `ShareDrawer.tsx` | Maps `shareView` → tab components; `addDashboardShareView` for custom drawer tabs |\n| `DashboardScene` | `uid`, dirty/editing state |\n| `packages/grafana-e2e-selectors` | Test IDs under `Dashboard.DashNav.newShareButton.menu` |\n| `public/locales/.../grafana.json` | i18n strings |\n| `DashboardInteractions` | Toolbar + sharing analytics |\n\n---\n\n### Blast radius (typical “copy UID” menu item)\n\n**Tight / expected**\n\n- `ShareMenu.tsx` (+ tests in `ShareMenu.test.tsx`)\n- E2E selectors if you add stable `data-testid`s\n- Locale strings\n- Optional: new `DashboardInteractions` / `sharingCategoryClicked` payload for a new `shareId` (or reuse pattern with a distinct `item` value)\n\n**Usually none**\n\n- Go API, short URL service, dashboard schema — **not** required for clipboard copy of an existing UID\n\n**Edge cases / product decisions**\n\n- **Unsaved / new dashboard** — no `uid`; disable item, tooltip, or prompt to save\n- **Provisioning / file-backed** — confirm UID availability matches expectations\n- **Panel context** — `ShareMenu` receives optional `panel`; “dashboard UID” is still the dashboard’s UID (usually unchanged)\n- **Feature parity** — old `ShareModal` path only if you explicitly add it there too\n\n**Plugins**\n\n- Third parties can inject menu rows via `addDashboardShareDrawerItem`; a core “Copy UID” item lives alongside those and should keep stable ordering/semantics\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThe share **dropdown** is a thin orchestration layer: URL-driven drawer tabs vs **modal** for copy-link. Adding **copy dashboard UID** fits naturally as **another `ShareMenu` action** that reads `DashboardScene.state.uid` and uses the clipboard API, with tests and i18n. Blast radius stays **frontend-local** unless you expand scope to the legacy share modal, new analytics contracts, or a full drawer tab for UID-related UX.",
