  "text": "\nUsing **spec-driven development** to produce a structured specification.\n\n## Delivered\n\nA full technical spec is saved at:\n\n**[`docs/specs/2026-04-02-browse-dashboards-grid-layout-spec.md`](docs/specs/2026-04-02-browse-dashboards-grid-layout-spec.md)**\n\nIt is **committed** on your branch (`docs: add spec for Browse Dashboards Grid layout (SearchLayout.Grid)`).\n\nThere is an older draft in [`docs/specs/2026-04-01-dashboard-card-grid-view-spec.md`](docs/specs/2026-04-01-dashboard-card-grid-view-spec.md). The **2026-04-02** doc supersedes it for implementation because it is aligned with **real** behavior:\n\n- **`hasSearchFilters()`** treats **`List`** as search-driving; **Grid** must **not**, or browse would always show `SearchView`.\n- **`getLocalStorageLayout()`** only knows List vs Folders today — **Grid** needs **`SearchStateManager`** updates or the choice will reset on reload.\n- **`BrowseView`** currently always renders **`DashboardsTree`**; the spec branches on **`SearchLayout.Grid`** and types **`DashboardsTreeItem`** from [`public/app/features/browse-dashboards/types.ts`](public/app/features/browse-dashboards/types.ts).\n- **Search** stays on **`SearchView` + `SearchResultsTable`** in v1 to honor your **small file count**; cards are **browse-only**.\n\n## File count (honest)\n\nThe spec lists **six** touched areas: **two new components** + **types**, **`ActionRow`**, **`BrowseView`**, and **`SearchStateManager`**. Your “five files” target matches the **UI-only** slice if you defer persistence; the doc states that **`SearchStateManager.ts` is required** for correct **Grid** persistence and sort/layout rules.\n\n## Next step (per skill)\n\nAfter you approve the spec, run the **writing-plans** skill to turn it into an implementation plan with ordered tasks. If you want, I can do that in a follow-up message once you’ve confirmed Q2/Q3 in section 10 (last-modified on cards, feature flag).",
