  "model": "composer-2-fast",
  "text": "\nHere’s a concise map of what backs the Bookmarks page and how “lightweight” categorization might land.\n\n## Primary UI surface (start here)\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage.tsx` | **Only feature file** for `/bookmarks`: empty state, CSS grid, maps URLs → `NavLandingPageCard`. |\n\n| `public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.tsx` | Card for each bookmark; optional `category` prop maps to **preset** visual styles (`primary`, `secondary`, `success`, `warning`, `error`) — not free-form labels. |\n\n| `public/app/core/components/Page/Page.tsx` | Shell (`Page`, `Page.Contents`) used by Bookmarks. |\n\n## Routing & nav entry\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Registers `/bookmarks` and lazy-loads `BookmarksPage`. |\n| `pkg/services/navtree/navtreeimpl/navtree.go` | Server-side nav item for Bookmarks (URL, icon, empty message id). |\n| `public/app/core/utils/navBarItem-translations.ts` | Strings for `bookmarks` / `bookmarks-empty` nav labels. |\n\n## Data: what you’re categorizing today\n\nBookmarks are **URLs in user preferences**, not a separate entity:\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/hooks.ts` | `usePinnedItems()` → `preferences.data?.navbar?.bookmarkUrls \\|\\| []`. |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenu.tsx` | Patches preferences when pinning (`bookmarkUrls: newItems`). |\n| `public/app/core/reducers/navBarTree.ts` | `setBookmark` keeps the nav tree’s bookmarks section in sync. |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.ts` | `findByUrl`, bookmark-section helpers (used by `BookmarksPage` via import from `MegaMenu/utils`). |\n| `pkg/services/preference/model.go` | Backend: `BookmarkUrls []string`. |\n| `public/app/core/components/SharedPreferences/SharedPreferences.tsx` | Default `navbar.bookmarkUrls: []`. |\n\n## Mega menu (pin/unpin, not the full-page grid)\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenuItemText.tsx` | Bookmark icon on nav rows (hidden on `/bookmarks`). |\n\n## Strings & tests\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/locales/en-US/grafana.json` | `bookmarks-page.*` and related nav strings. |\n| `e2e-playwright/various-suite/bookmarks.spec.ts` | E2E for bookmarks. |\n| `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.test.ts` | Unit tests for mega menu bookmark helpers. |\n\n---\n\n## Scope for “lightweight categorization UI”\n\n- **Lightweight (mostly frontend, no new persistence):**  \n  - Group or label in **`BookmarksPage.tsx`** using data you already have after `findByUrl(navTree, url)` (e.g. parent section, `item.section`, or URL heuristics).  \n  - Optional: pass `category` into **`NavLandingPageCard`** only if you’re fine with the **fixed** palette styles above; for arbitrary category names you’d extend the card or add a small badge row in the page.\n\n- **Heavier (user-defined categories saved per bookmark):**  \n  - Today’s model is **`bookmarkUrls: string[]`** only. Anything like “folder per bookmark” needs **preference schema + API + patch paths** (Go `preference` model, preferences app/OpenAPI, `SharedPreferences`, `MegaMenu` patch shape, possibly K8s preferences). That’s a larger change than tweaking **`BookmarksPage.tsx`**.\n\nSo for investigation, **`BookmarksPage.tsx`**, **`NavLandingPageCard.tsx`**, and **`MegaMenu/hooks.ts` + `utils.ts`** are the right first reads; **`MegaMenu.tsx`** and **`navBarTree.ts`** matter if categorization must stay in sync with pinning or preferences.",
