  "text": "Here's what I added to the BookmarksPage:\n\n### Category assignment\n\n`getBookmarkCategory()` automatically classifies each bookmark into one of three categories based on its nav item `id` and `url`:\n\n- **Operations** — alerting, explore, drilldown, connections, datasources, monitoring, infrastructure, OnCall, etc.\n- **Admin** — administration (`cfg/*`), users, teams, service accounts, API keys, orgs, plugins, SSO, storage, etc.\n- **Content** — dashboards, playlists, library panels, home, starred, reports, and anything else as the default fallback\n\n### Filter controls\n\nA `FilterInput` (text search across bookmark name and subtitle) and a `RadioButtonGroup` with **All / Operations / Admin / Content** options, laid out horizontally using `Stack` — matching the pattern used in the plugins Browse page and ServiceAccountsListPage.\n\n### Grouped display\n\nBookmarks that pass the search+category filter are grouped into collapsible `CollapsableSection` sections (one per non-empty category), each showing its count in the label (e.g. \"Operations (3)\"). Each section contains the existing card grid layout. When no results match, a \"not found\" `EmptyState` is shown.\n\nAll strings go through `t()` for i18n, and no new dependencies were introduced — only existing `@grafana/ui` components (`FilterInput`, `RadioButtonGroup`, `CollapsableSection`, `Stack`, `EmptyState`).",
