{
  "conversation_id": "2fe823fd-227b-4f7e-b16b-45725841ae51",
  "generation_id": "ba678fa1-bc12-47c8-881d-89754bbed43b",
  "model": "composer-2-fast",
  "text": "\nHere’s a concise overview tied to **this repo**, plus diagrams and concrete “next file” ideas.\n\n## Overview: React Router v5 → v6 in Grafana\n\n**1. Dependencies**  \nThe app still declares **`react-router` and `react-router-dom` at 5.3.4** (see root `package.json`). There is **no** full cutover to the standalone v6 packages for core yet.\n\n**2. Compatibility layer (main v5→v6 bridge)**  \nGrafana uses **`react-router-dom-v5-compat`**, which lets you use **v6-style APIs** (`Routes`, `Route` with `element`, `Navigate`, `useNavigate`, `useParams`, `useLocation` from the compat package) while the root is still a **v5-style `Router` with a custom `history`** from `locationService`:\n\n```26:30:public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx\nexport function RouterWrapper(props: RouterWrapperProps) {\n  return (\n    <Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>\n      <LocationServiceProvider service={locationService}>\n        <CompatRouter>\n```\n\nSo the migration is **incremental**: v6 *patterns* and *hooks* via compat, not a single “flip” to `react-router@6` only.\n\n**3. App shell**  \n`AppWrapper` already renders routes with **`<Routes>` / `<Route element={...}>`** from **`react-router-dom-v5-compat`** (v6-style route config on top of the compat stack):\n\n```80:92:public/app/AppWrapper.tsx\n  renderRoute = (route: RouteDescriptor) => {\n    return (\n      <Route\n        caseSensitive={route.sensitive === undefined ? false : route.sensitive}\n        path={route.path}\n        key={route.path}\n        element={<GrafanaRouteWrapper route={route} />}\n      />\n    );\n  };\n\n  renderRoutes() {\n    return <Routes>{getAppRoutes().map((r) => this.renderRoute(r))}</Routes>;\n  }\n```\n\n**4. Plugins**  \n`sharedDependencies` exposes **`react-router-dom`** (v5) and maps **`react-router` → `react-router-dom-v5-compat`** so plugins don’t end up with two incompatible router cores (see comment in `public/app/features/plugins/loader/sharedDependencies.ts`).\n\n**5. Parallel track: `locationService`**  \nThis is **Grafana-specific**, documented in `public/app/core/navigation/location-service-migration-status.md`: move **reads** from `useLocation()` to **`locationService.getLocation()`** and **navigation** to **`locationService.push` / `partial`** where appropriate, so components depend less on router context. That pairs with the compat migration but is not the same as “bump `package.json` to RR6 only.”\n\n**Legacy v5 hooks**  \n`useHistory` / `withRouter` are largely gone; a quick scan shows **`useHistory` only in a few places** (e.g. plugins admin / connections), so the old v5 hook surface is small.\n\n---\n\n## Lightweight Mermaid diagrams\n\n**1) Current routing stack (how pieces sit together)**\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  subgraph deps[\"npm\"]\n    RR5[\"react-router-dom v5\"]\n    Compat[\"react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n  end\n  subgraph tree[\"React tree\"]\n    R[\"Router + history from locationService\"]\n    CR[\"CompatRouter\"]\n    LS[\"LocationServiceProvider\"]\n    RT[\"Routes / Route element=...\"]\n  end\n  RR5 --> R\n  Compat --> CR\n  Compat --> RT\n  R --> CR --> LS --> RT\n```\n\n**2) “Migration status” (two tracks)**\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph A[\"React Router upgrade path\"]\n    A1[\"v5 Router + history\"] --> A2[\"CompatRouter + v6-style Routes/hooks\"]\n    A3[\"Future: data router / drop compat\"] -.-> A2\n  end\n  subgraph B[\"Grafana locationService\"]\n    B1[\"useLocation in components\"] --> B2[\"locationService.getLocation / push / partial\"]\n  end\n  A2 --- B1\n```\n\nInterpretation: **horizontal** progress is “compat + v6 APIs”; **vertical** progress (in many files) is “use `locationService` instead of reading the router directly,” as in the migration doc.\n\n**3) Rough file-level picture (illustrative, not exact counts)**\n\n```mermaid\npie title Public TS/TSX: typical split\n  \"Imports from react-router-dom-v5-compat\" : 70\n  \"Still on raw react-router-dom v5 imports only\" : 5\n  \"Other / tests\" : 25\n```\n\nThe “v5-only” slice is small (e.g. `Router` in `RoutesWrapper`, test helpers). Most feature code already goes through **compat**.\n\n---\n\n## Short list of **good next migration targets** (locationService / fewer `useLocation` calls)\n\nThese are **still using `useLocation()`** (from compat) in places that match the patterns in `location-service-migration-status.md`—good candidates to migrate **next** in small PRs:\n\n| File | Why it’s a reasonable next step |\n|------|----------------------------------|\n| `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/TopBar/SignInLink.tsx` | Small component; only needs current location for `getUrlForPartial` — maps cleanly to `locationService.getLocation()`. |\n| `public/app/core/hooks/useQueryParams.ts` | Central hook; migrating improves many call sites indirectly (may need care for re-renders vs subscriptions). |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/hooks.ts` (`useUrlParams`) | Same idea: shared hook; pairs with `locationService.partial` already. |\n| `public/app/plugins/panel/alertlist/unified-alerting/UngroupedView.tsx` | Isolated panel scope; lower blast radius than a whole feature folder. |\n| `public/app/features/trails/RedirectToDrilldownApp.tsx` | Redirect logic is a natural fit for `locationService` + tests without full router. |\n| `public/app/features/alerting/unified/components/AlertingPageWrapper.tsx` | Wrapper components are high leverage if you want consistency across alerting pages. |\n\n**Honorable mention (harder):** files under `features/dashboard*` / `dashboard-scene` that use `useLocation` (e.g. `DashboardSceneRenderer`, `DashNav`, `PublicDashboardPage`) — valuable but touch critical paths; better after a couple of smaller wins.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** Grafana is **not** on “pure” React Router 6 packages for core; it uses **v5 + compat** with **`Routes`/`Route`/`useNavigate`-style APIs**, plus an ongoing **`locationService`** migration documented in-repo. Next steps are usually **(a)** more `locationService` migrations in **small, shared, or leaf** files, and **(b)** eventually a **larger** project to replace `Router`+`history` with a v6 data router and remove compat—when the team is ready for that coordinated change.\n\nIf you want this tracked in-repo, the living list of completed `locationService` migrations is in `public/app/core/navigation/location-service-migration-status.md`; you can extend it as you finish each file.",
