  "model": "claude-opus-4-6",
  "text": "Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n### What was added\n\n**`BookmarksPage.tsx`** - The bookmarks page now auto-categorizes pinned items into color-coded groups based on where they live in the Grafana nav tree:\n\n| Category | Color | Matches |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Dashboards** | Blue (primary) | Items under `dashboards/browse`, `starred`, or URLs like `/d/`, `/dashboards` |\n| **Alerting** | Red (error) | Items under `alerting`, `alerts-and-incidents` |\n| **Explore** | Green (success) | Items under `explore`, `drilldown` |\n| **Administration** | Orange (warning) | Items under `cfg`, `cfg/general`, `cfg/access`, `cfg/plugins` |\n| **Other** | Purple (secondary) | Everything else (apps, plugins, connections, etc.) |\n\n### How categorization works\n\n1. **`findTopLevelSection()`** walks the nav tree to find which top-level section contains the bookmarked URL\n2. **`categorizeItem()`** maps that section ID to a category key, with URL-based fallbacks for items not found in the tree\n3. Only categories that have at least one bookmark are shown\n\n### UI features\n\n- **Filter chips** at the top let users filter by category - clicking a chip toggles it, showing only that category's bookmarks\n- **Search bar** filters bookmarks by name or description in real-time\n- **Color-coded section headers** with `Badge` components separate each group visually\n- **Color-coded cards** use the existing `NavLandingPageCard` `category` prop to tint card borders and backgrounds\n- **\"No results\" empty state** appears when search/filter yields nothing\n- All category counts are displayed in both the filter chips and section headers",
