  "model": "composer-2",
  "text": "\nHere’s a **speakable prompt flow**—short lines you can say almost verbatim. Adjust names/paths only if you need to.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Local (explore → narrow → do)\n\n**Open the area**\n\n- “Walk me through where dashboard scene state gets turned into something we save—start from the main entry and point me at the files I should care about.”\n\n**Pick a slice**\n\n- “Pick one small thing that could drift between the scene and the saved JSON—like a field we persist but don’t really test—and show me where it’s read and written.”\n\n**Lock intent**\n\n- “Let’s add a unit test that would catch if that field stopped round-tripping. Name the test so a future reader knows what invariant it’s protecting.”\n\n**Execute**\n\n- “Implement the smallest change that makes that test pass—or if behavior is already right, lock it in with the test only.”\n\n**Sanity**\n\n- “What’s the one command I should run here to verify this didn’t break anything obvious?”\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — Handoff to cloud (same story, bigger)\n\n**Frame the ask**\n\n- “Based on what we just did locally, write a short plan for a larger pass: same idea—serialization round-trip and coverage—but across the dashboard scene save/load path, not just this one field.”\n\n**Scope the output**\n\n- “I want concrete deliverables: a gap list, suggested tests or files to touch, and a sensible order of work. Don’t hand-wave—tie each item to a path or function if you can.”\n\n**Optional stretch (only if you want it)**\n\n- “If there’s time in that plan, include a quick note on experimental or ts-expect-error spots and whether they need tests too.”\n\n**How you’ll present it live**\n\n- You don’t need to “run” cloud on stage—say something like: *“I sent that plan to a cloud run earlier; here’s what came back,”* then show the PR, doc, or checklist.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — Automation (related, separate beat)\n\n**Intent**\n\n- “I want a separate automation—not another chat—that nudges people when they change serialization code without touching tests.”\n\n**Trigger**\n\n- “When a pull request touches the dashboard scene serialization folder, what’s a simple rule we could enforce with a webhook—like comment on the PR if there’s no test file change?”\n\n**MCP / tools**\n\n- “Assume we have GitHub and whatever else we need via MCP—sketch the minimal steps: see the PR, check paths, decide, post one short comment.”\n\n**Optional schedule**\n\n- “Separately, what would a weekly job do that’s similar but repo-wide—like a small health report instead of per-PR?”\n\n---\n\n## One-line transitions (if you want glue)\n\n- Local → cloud: *“Same problem, bigger surface—that’s what I’d put in a cloud run.”*  \n- Cloud → automation: *“The manual part was the learning; the automation is so the team doesn’t have to remember every time.”*\n\nThat’s enough to carry the demo conversationally without a full script.",
