  "text": "\nHere’s a **clean restart**: plain English first, then **simple lines you can say out loud**.\n\n---\n\n## What the demo is (in normal words)\n\n**Part 1 — On your machine**  \nYou and the assistant look at how Grafana **saves a dashboard**, find **one place** where something could break quietly, and **add a test** (or a tiny fix + test) so it’s protected.\n\n**Part 2 — In the cloud (already done before the talk)**  \nYou give the assistant a **bigger version of the same job**: “check more files, list what’s missing, suggest more tests.” You show the **finished result** (doc, PR, checklist)—you’re not waiting for it live.\n\n**Part 3 — Automation (different piece)**  \nSomething **automatic** runs when a PR changes certain files—e.g. **post a reminder** if someone changed “save” code but didn’t change any tests. That’s **webhook + tools**, not a chat.\n\n---\n\n## Part 1 — Local (say these kinds of things)\n\n1. “Where in this repo does the dashboard **get saved** to JSON or to the API? Show me the main files.”\n\n2. “Pick **one** thing that could break when you **save, reload, and open again**—something small.”\n\n3. “Show me **where** that thing is set when we save and **where** it’s read when we load.”\n\n4. “Let’s add a **test** that proves save and load still match for that thing.”\n\n5. “Make the **smallest change** so the test passes.”\n\n6. “What **one command** should I run to check tests here?”\n\n---\n\n## Part 2 — Cloud handoff (say these before you show the pre-made result)\n\n1. “Turn what we did into a **short plan** for a **bigger pass**: same idea, but **more files**, **more tests**, **what’s still missing**.”\n\n2. “Write it like a **to-do list** a teammate could follow, with **file names** where you can.”\n\n*(Live:)* “I ran that in the **cloud** earlier—here’s what it produced,” then show PR / doc / list.\n\n---\n\n## Part 3 — Automation (say these for the separate demo)\n\n1. “I want a **small automation**: when someone opens a PR that touches **dashboard save/load code**, **check** if they also changed any **tests**.”\n\n2. “If they didn’t, **post a short comment** on the PR: ‘You changed save/load—add or update a test.’”\n\n3. “Keep it **simple**—no auto-fix, just a **reminder**.”\n\n*(Optional:)* “For a **weekly** job, what’s one **simple report** we could generate instead—like ‘these folders changed a lot, these have no tests’?”\n\n---\n\n## One sentence that ties the room together\n\n- “**Local** we fixed one hole; **cloud** we mapped the rest; **automation** so nobody forgets the next time.”\n\nIf any line still feels stiff, shorten it further to how *you* actually talk—for example swap “save/load code” for “the code that writes the dashboard file.”",
