  "model": "composer-2",
  "text": "\nHere’s a concrete example in the dashboard feature:\n\n## `TemplateDashboardModal` — fetch fails → nothing in the UI\n\n`public/app/features/dashboard/dashgrid/DashboardLibrary/TemplateDashboardModal.tsx` loads Grafana Net templates with **`showErrorAlert: false`**, and on failure it only logs and returns an empty list:\n\n```73:92:public/app/features/dashboard/dashgrid/DashboardLibrary/TemplateDashboardModal.tsx\n  const { value: dashboards = [], loading } = useAsync(async () => {\n    if (!isOpen) {\n      return [];\n    }\n\n    try {\n      const response = await getBackendSrv().get<GnetDashboardsResponse>(\n        `/api/gnet/dashboards?orgSlug=raintank&categorySlug=templates&includeScreenshots=true`,\n        undefined,\n        undefined,\n        {\n          showErrorAlert: false,\n        }\n      );\n\n      return response.items;\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error('Error loading template dashboards ', error);\n      return [];\n    }\n  }, [isOpen]);\n```\n\nIf the request fails, `dashboards` is `[]` and `loading` becomes false. The component then bails out here:\n\n```107:109:public/app/features/dashboard/dashgrid/DashboardLibrary/TemplateDashboardModal.tsx\n  if (!testDataSource || (dashboards.length === 0 && !loading)) {\n    return null;\n  }\n```\n\nSo the user gets **no modal, no toast, no inline error**—only a console message. That’s weak feedback compared to something like `CommunityDashboardSection`, which shows an `Alert` and a **Retry** button on failure.\n\n---\n\n## Same pattern: `SuggestedDashboards`\n\n`SuggestedDashboards.tsx` catches errors with `console.error`, returns `{ dashboards: [], hasMoreDashboards: false }`, then returns `null` when there are no dashboards, so a **failed load looks the same as “no suggestions”** (lines 138–141 and 271–274 in that file).\n\n---\n\n## Optional: `ShareSnapshot` — some paths never surface errors\n\nIn `ShareSnapshot.tsx`, `getSnaphotShareOptions()` is `async` and called from `componentDidMount` with **no `try/catch` or `.catch`**, and `deleteSnapshot` calls `getBackendSrv().get(deleteUrl)` with **no error handling**—failures there won’t show a dedicated message in that modal unless something higher up handles them.\n\nIf you want one clear answer for “a React component in the dashboard feature”: **`TemplateDashboardModal`** is the strongest match (suppressed alerts + empty state + `return null`).",
