  "model": "gpt-5.3-codex",
  "text": "A good example is `public/app/features/dashboard/components/DashboardSettings/VersionsSettings.tsx`.\n\n- It makes API-backed calls via `historySrv.getHistoryList(...)` and `historySrv.getDashboardVersion(...)`.\n- On failure, it does not show a useful user-facing error:\n  - `getVersions()` only does `console.log(err)` in `.catch(...)`.\n  - `getDiff()` has no `try/catch` at all, so failures don’t produce a clear UI message.\n\n```62:80:public/app/features/dashboard/components/DashboardSettings/VersionsSettings.tsx\ngetVersions = (append = false) => {\n  this.setState({ isAppending: append });\n  const requestOptions = this.continueToken\n    ? { limit: this.limit, start: this.start, continueToken: this.continueToken }\n    : { limit: this.limit, start: this.start };\n\n  historySrv\n    .getHistoryList(this.props.dashboard.uid, requestOptions)\n    .then((res) => {\n      this.setState({\n        isLoading: false,\n        versions: [...(this.state.versions ?? []), ...this.decorateVersions(res.versions)],\n      });\n      this.start += this.limit;\n      this.continueToken = res.continueToken ?? '';\n    })\n    .catch((err) => console.log(err))\n    .finally(() => this.setState({ isAppending: false }));\n};\n```\n\nAnd the API call is real HTTP through `getBackendSrv()`:\n\n```22:29:public/app/features/dashboard-scene/settings/version-history/HistorySrv.ts\nexport class HistorySrv {\n  getHistoryList(dashboardUID: string, options: HistoryListOpts) {\n    if (typeof dashboardUID !== 'string') {\n      return Promise.resolve([]);\n    }\n\n    return getBackendSrv().get(`api/dashboards/uid/${dashboardUID}/versions`, options);\n  }\n```\n\nIf you want, I can also point out 1-2 other dashboard components with similar weak error handling.",
